<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study the problem of sampling from a target probability density <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\propto\exp(-V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\propto\exp(-V)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="S1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies, for <math id="S1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha\leqslant\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha\leqslant\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha I\preceq\nabla^{2}V(x)\preceq\beta I\,,\qquad x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,,\qquad\kappa\coloneqq\frac{\beta}{\alpha}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha I\preceq\nabla^{2}V(x)\preceq\beta I\,,\qquad x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,,\qquad\kappa\coloneqq\frac{\beta}{\alpha}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We design a new sampler that combines Gaussian smoothing of the density with a high-order
discretization of Hamiltonian dynamics via Picard iteration and Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. This combination gives a stable unadjusted Hamiltonian step even
though the original potential is assumed to have only two derivatives.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our first result is a low-accuracy sampler with Wasserstein guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.1</span></span><span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee)<span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), let <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose that we are given a point
<math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the smoothed Picard HMC algorithm
(<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Algorithm 3.2 (Smoothed Picard HMC with a terminal FORS step). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) returns a sample from a probability law <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}\,W_{2}(\widehat{\pi},\pi)\leqslant\varepsilon\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}\,W_{2}(\widehat{\pi},\pi)\leqslant\varepsilon\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected number of gradient and proximal queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\Bigl(\Bigl\{\kappa^{2}+\frac{\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}}{\varepsilon^{1/3}}\Bigr\}\log^{4}\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\Bigl(\Bigl\{\kappa^{2}+\frac{\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}}{\varepsilon^{1/3}}\Bigr\}\log^{4}\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We find the dimension dependence in this result to be quite surprising.
Prior to this work, under (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), the best dimension dependence was <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This was achieved with the randomized midpoint discretization of the
underdamped Langevin, with rate
<math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(\kappa d^{1/3}/\varepsilon^{2/3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(\kappa d^{1/3}/\varepsilon^{2/3})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>, and also the shifted ODE method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>.
With the development of the shifted composition framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> and accelerated entropic hypocoercivity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, the rate was improved to <math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{5/6}d^{1/3}/\varepsilon^{2/3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{5/6}d^{1/3}/\varepsilon^{2/3})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math>. The closely related Poisson
midpoint discretization of underdamped Langevin achieved an incomparable rate of roughly <math id="S1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/3}/\varepsilon^{1/3}+\kappa^{11/8}d^{3/8}/\varepsilon^{1/4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/3}/\varepsilon^{1/3}+\kappa^{11/8}d^{3/8}/\varepsilon^{1/4})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>. More recently, exact simulation of the underdamped Langevin
diffusion via FORS achieved
<math id="S1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{2/3}d^{1/3}\operatorname{polylog}(1/\varepsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>polylog</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{2/3}d^{1/3}\operatorname{polylog}(1/\varepsilon))</annotation></semantics></math> complexity
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.
In contrast, <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> achieves dimension dependence <math id="S1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1/6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1/6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In a companion work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, we introduce a new sampler, called the proximal bouncy particle sampler or <em id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">proximal BPS</em>, with <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{1/2}d^{1/4}\operatorname{polylog}(1/\varepsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>polylog</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{1/2}d^{1/4}\operatorname{polylog}(1/\varepsilon))</annotation></semantics></math> complexity from a warm start. One key application of smoothed Picard HMC is to provide an implementable warm start for that sampler.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Toward this end, we develop a novel algorithmic framework which we call the recursive warm start generator. It is designed as a wrapper around smoothed samplers—that is, samplers which target the Gaussian smoothed distribution <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math>—and it upgrades transport metric guarantees into stronger divergence guarantees. Namely, with negligible overhead, it upgrades <math id="S1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds into <math id="S1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math> bounds; <math id="S1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds into mixed TV and Rényi bounds; and <math id="S1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\psi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\psi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds into genuine Rényi bounds. We apply this to smoothed Picard HMC by extending the arguments for <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> to produce stronger <math id="S1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees, leading to the following warm start result.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.2</span></span><span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Warm start)<span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) and that we are given <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying
<math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every
<math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, the algorithm of
<a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> returns a sample from a law
<math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> with the following guarantee.
There exists a law <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}_{\delta},\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{2}(\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant 1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}_{\delta},\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{2}(\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant 1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, the expected number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\Bigl(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\log^{9}\frac{e\kappa d}{\delta}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\Bigl(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\log^{9}\frac{e\kappa d}{\delta}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 7.1 (Picard HMC warm starts). ‣ 7.1 Picard HMC warm starts ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>, we prove a stronger statement that relaxes the assumption of strong log-concavity to a log-Sobolev inequality, and provides a KL divergence guarantee.
Note that the recursive warm start generator also removes the <math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> term from the complexity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, by using this warm start result to initialize proximal BPS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, we obtain a new high-accuracy sampler which enjoys the following guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.3</span></span><span id="S1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Warm start + proximal BPS)<span id="S1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) and suppose that we are given a point <math id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every
<math id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1/4</annotation></semantics></math>, the warm start
algorithm followed by the proximal BPS algorithm returns a sample from a law
<math id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi},\pi)\leqslant\varepsilon\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi},\pi)\leqslant\varepsilon\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected number of gradient evaluations is</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\Bigl(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\log^{9}\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}+\kappa^{1/2}d^{1/4}\log^{11/4}\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\Bigl(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\log^{9}\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}+\kappa^{1/2}d^{1/4}\log^{11/4}\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Prior to this work, the best high-accuracy sampler was exact diffusion simulation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, which achieved a complexity of <math id="S1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{2/3}d^{1/3}\operatorname{polylog}(1/\varepsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>polylog</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{2/3}d^{1/3}\operatorname{polylog}(1/\varepsilon))</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, our new high-accuracy sampler has state-of-the-art dependence on the dimension, but not on the condition number.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 1.4</span></span><span id="S1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Further consequences)<span id="S1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proximal sampler reduction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> converts general
log-smooth sampling problems into well-conditioned log-concave subproblems.
By invoking this framework, we could also state corollaries in other settings, such as when <math id="S1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is only assumed to satisfy a Poincaré inequality.
Since this reduction is standard, we omit these extensions for brevity.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We give an overview of the main new ideas—both algorithmic and analytic—introduced in this work in the technical overview (<a href="#S3" title="3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Related work.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work advances the study of the complexity of log-concave sampling; an
introduction to the subject and an overview of existing approaches can be
found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our use of Gaussian smoothing is reminiscent of score-based diffusion
models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>, <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> and stochastic localization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>,
which also rely on score functions for Gaussian convolutions of a target distribution.
Here, we do not learn score
functions from data: we use queries to the unsmoothed score to construct
nearly unbiased estimators of the smoothed score, and control their bias
and fluctuations in the sampling analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Hamiltonian Monte Carlo was introduced as hybrid Monte Carlo in lattice
field theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> for its development in statistics.
Early analyses quantified its favorable dimension dependence through
asymptotic scaling results for product targets <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.
Subsequent works established non-asymptotic convergence guarantees for
ideal HMC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>.
More recent work has focused on accelerated convergence of randomized
HMC and related piecewise deterministic processes, including convergence
in relative entropy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A substantial literature studies numerical discretization, both for
unadjusted HMC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite>
and for Metropolized HMC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite>.
Representative results achieve <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1/4}</annotation></semantics></math> dimension dependence under
quantitative third derivative bounds, such as structured or
Frobenius-Lipschitz Hessian assumptions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite>.
Higher-order integrators and polynomial collocation yield still better
dimension dependence under stronger smoothness and structural
assumptions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>.
Our departure is to improve the dimension dependence <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">without</em> imposing
higher-order smoothness on the original potential: Gaussian smoothing
provides the regularity needed for accurate integration, while we control
the error from estimating the smoothed score using queries to the
unsmoothed score.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The recursive warm start framework builds heavily on the proximal
sampler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.
The main analytic mechanism for warm start generation is regularization
along the heat flow, leading to reverse transport inequalities. Such inequalities are
dual formulations of dimension-free Harnack inequalities, originating in
Wang’s work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>, <a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>; see also
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> for the transport formulation.
Related regularization arguments have been used to generate algorithmic
warm starts with underdamped Langevin <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and HMC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite>,
and to establish KL divergence guarantees via the shifted composition
framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>.
Coupling-based regularization has also yielded total variation
bounds <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> and divergence guarantees for unadjusted
HMC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. These works analyze regularization for particular
sampling dynamics. Our framework instead applies heat flow regularization
to the output of any smoothed sampler, yielding a general route to KL, mixed TV and Rényi, or genuine
Rényi warm starts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">AI usage.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main ideas underlying the algorithm and its analysis emerged through extensive interactions with GPT-5.6 Sol. The initial goal was to improve the dimensional dependence beyond <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1/3}</annotation></semantics></math>. In response, GPT proposed considering the smoothed potential <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\eta}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)}V(\cdot+\sqrt{\eta}\,G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\eta}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)}V(\cdot+\sqrt{\eta}\,G)</annotation></semantics></math>, which led to a sampler with dimensional dependence <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1/4}</annotation></semantics></math>. We subsequently suggested the more natural smoothing adopted in this paper and, through further refinements of the analysis and extensive interactions between the authors and GPT, obtained the improved dimensional dependence and the algorithms presented here. The authors independently checked the arguments, prepared the manuscript, and take full responsibility for its contents.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Except in the generic warm start result <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>
and its consequence <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 7.1 (Picard HMC warm starts). ‣ 7.1 Picard HMC warm starts ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>, throughout the remainder of the paper
<math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) holds pointwise.
For most of the paper, we normalize <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>; this can be achieved by rescaling.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity of exposition, we initially allow ourselves access to proximal queries to <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, in addition to queries to <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math>.
For step size <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, one proximal query returns</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)\coloneqq\operatorname*{argmin}_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}{\Bigl\{V(x)+\frac{\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">argmin</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)\coloneqq\operatorname*{argmin}_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}{\Bigl\{V(x)+\frac{\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we only ever need to call the proximal oracle for a <math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth potential with step size at most <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/(2\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/(2\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this regime, the computation of <math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{prox}_{aV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{prox}_{aV}</annotation></semantics></math> is a well-conditioned optimization problem and can be easily implemented via standard routines.
In <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, we remove the use of proximal queries altogether.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The sampling analogue of the proximal operator is the restricted Gaussian oracle (RGO), which is the distribution</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{a,y}(\mathrm{d}x)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(x)-\frac{\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}x\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{a,y}(\mathrm{d}x)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(x)-\frac{\lVert x-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}x\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, we show how to approximately implement it in <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(1+{(a^{2}d)}^{1/3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(1+{(a^{2}d)}^{1/3})</annotation></semantics></math> queries, based on the exact diffusion sampler of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that an admissible reference point is supplied:</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This reference point could be obtained via an optimization routine.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The total variation distance is
<math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)\coloneqq\sup_{A}|P(A)-Q(A)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P,Q)\coloneqq\sup_{A}|P(A)-Q(A)|</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also use</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(P\mathbin{\|}Q)\coloneqq\int\log\bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}P\,,\qquad W_{2}^{2}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{(X,Y)}\mathbb{E}\lVert X-Y\rVert^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>dP</mi><mi>dQ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>dP</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P\mathbin{\|}Q)\coloneqq\int\log\bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}P\,,\qquad W_{2}^{2}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{(X,Y)}\mathbb{E}\lVert X-Y\rVert^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">with the usual value <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for KL without absolute continuity; the
infimum in the definition of <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is over all couplings of <math id="S2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, define Rényi divergence by</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}(P\mathbin{\|}Q)\coloneqq\frac{1}{q-1}\log\int\bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}\bigr)^{q}\,\mathrm{d}Q\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}(P\mathbin{\|}Q)\coloneqq\frac{1}{q-1}\log\int\bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}\bigr)^{q}\,\mathrm{d}Q\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">with value <math id="S2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\not\ll Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≪̸</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\not\ll Q</annotation></semantics></math>; this is the standard convention
of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For matrices and tensors, <math id="S2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the operator and Hilbert–Schmidt (or Frobenius) norms,
respectively. For an <math id="S2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-tensor <math id="S2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, this means</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert A\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}=\sum_{j_{1},\ldots,j_{r}\in[d]}\bigl|A[e_{j_{1}},\ldots,e_{j_{r}}]\bigr|^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>A</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert A\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}=\sum_{j_{1},\ldots,j_{r}\in[d]}\bigl|A[e_{j_{1}},\ldots,e_{j_{r}}]\bigr|^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(e_{j})_{j\in[d]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(e_{j})_{j\in[d]}</annotation></semantics></math> is any orthonormal basis of <math id="S2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The notation <math id="S2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(B)</annotation></semantics></math> means <math id="S2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> times a fixed universal power of a
logarithm of the dimension, condition number, inverse accuracy, and any
explicit confidence parameter. Throughout, <math id="S2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C,c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C,c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> denote universal
constants that may change from line to line.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Technical overview</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall our convention that <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>The smoothing trick</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a smoothing variance
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)\,,\qquad\Pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)\,,\qquad\Pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">key algorithmic idea</span> of this paper is to pick a smoothing parameter
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and to sample from the smoothed distribution <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>
instead of the original target <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(Y)\approx\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(Y)\approx\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can recover a sample from <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> via
the RGO: for <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim R_{\eta,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim R_{\eta,Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(X)\approx\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(X)\approx\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The smoothed
potential <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined by
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-V_{\eta}}\coloneqq e^{-V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-V_{\eta}}\coloneqq e^{-V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math>, is given by</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\nabla V(X)\bigm|X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G=y\bigr]\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\nabla V(X)\bigm|X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G=y\bigr]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.
The smoothed potential admits quantitative higher-order derivative bounds, allowing us to apply higher-order integrators.
The catch is that (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 3.1 ‣ 3.1 The smoothing trick ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) is given as a conditional expectation, and is therefore not explicitly computable.
Write <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}\coloneqq\nabla V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}\coloneqq\nabla V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we replace evaluations of <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq\nabla V\bigl(\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)+\sqrt{\eta}\,G\bigr)\,,\qquad G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq\nabla V\bigl(\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)+\sqrt{\eta}\,G\bigr)\,,\qquad G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The intuition is that
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\int\nabla V\,\mathrm{d}R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\int\nabla V\,\mathrm{d}R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)+\sqrt{\eta}\,G)\approx R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)+\sqrt{\eta}\,G)\approx R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)</annotation></semantics></math> is almost an unbiased estimator of
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V_{\eta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V_{\eta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>The higher-order integrator and the <math id="S3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Picard iteration.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The numerical scheme we consider below is a discretization of an unadjusted generalized Hamiltonian sampler
with partial Ornstein–Uhlenbeck (OU) momentum refreshment, following the terminology
of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>.
Between momentum refreshments, we follow the Hamiltonian dynamics</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{X}_{t}=P_{t}\,,\qquad\dot{P}_{t}=-\nabla V_{\eta}(X_{t})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{X}_{t}=P_{t}\,,\qquad\dot{P}_{t}=-\nabla V_{\eta}(X_{t})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The dynamics can be written in integral form as</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}=X_{0}+tP_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,g_{\eta}(X_{s})\,\mathrm{d}s\,,\qquad P_{t}=P_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}g_{\eta}(X_{s})\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}=X_{0}+tP_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,g_{\eta}(X_{s})\,\mathrm{d}s\,,\qquad P_{t}=P_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}g_{\eta}(X_{s})\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since the integral cannot generally be computed explicitly, we simulate it with Picard iteration. Let <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{(X_{t}^{[0]},P_{t}^{[0]})}_{t\geqslant 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{(X_{t}^{[0]},P_{t}^{[0]})}_{t\geqslant 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a computable initial guess for the trajectory.
The ideal Picard iteration maps this to an updated trajectory <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{(X_{t}^{[1]},P_{t}^{[1]})}_{t\geqslant 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{(X_{t}^{[1]},P_{t}^{[1]})}_{t\geqslant 0}</annotation></semantics></math> by applying (<a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3.3 ‣ Picard iteration. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) but with the non-linear term <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated at the preceding trajectory.
That is,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t}^{[1]}\coloneqq X_{0}+tP_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,g_{\eta}(X_{s}^{[0]})\,\mathrm{d}s\,,\qquad P_{t}^{[1]}\coloneqq P_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}g_{\eta}(X_{s}^{[0]})\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t}^{[1]}\coloneqq X_{0}+tP_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,g_{\eta}(X_{s}^{[0]})\,\mathrm{d}s\,,\qquad P_{t}^{[1]}\coloneqq P_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}g_{\eta}(X_{s}^{[0]})\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">A particularly simple choice for the initial trajectory is
<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}^{[0]}\coloneqq X_{0}+tP_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}^{[0]}\coloneqq X_{0}+tP_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This describes one Picard iteration, and in principle one can iterate further.
For the main results of this paper, it suffices to iterate up to depth <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Higher depth iteration is treated in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The ideal Picard iteration requires exact integration, which is not directly implementable.
To develop an algorithm, we apply numerical integration, or quadrature.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix an integer <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>. The Chebyshev–Lobatto nodes on the interval <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,h]</annotation></semantics></math> are defined to be</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{j}\coloneqq\frac{h}{2}\,\bigl\{1-\cos\bigl({\textstyle\frac{j-1}{J-1}}\,\uppi\bigr)\bigr\}\,,\qquad j=1,\ldots,J\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">π</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}\coloneqq\frac{h}{2}\,\bigl\{1-\cos\bigl({\textstyle\frac{j-1}{J-1}}\,\uppi\bigr)\bigr\}\,,\qquad j=1,\ldots,J\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Associated with the nodes are certain interpolating polynomials <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\dotsc,J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\dotsc,J</annotation></semantics></math>,
characterized by
<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell_{j}(t_{i})=\mathbf{1}_{\{i=j\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}(t_{i})=\mathbf{1}_{\{i=j\}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for every vector-valued function
<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> defined at the nodes, let</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}f)(t)\coloneqq\sum_{j=1}^{J}f(t_{j})\,\ell_{j}(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}f)(t)\coloneqq\sum_{j=1}^{J}f(t_{j})\,\ell_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">be its Lagrange interpolant; this is an approximation to <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)</annotation></semantics></math> itself.
Background material on Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature is collected in <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain a numerical scheme, we replace <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 3.4 ‣ Picard iteration. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>) with its interpolant.
This produces the iterations</p>
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t}^{[1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t}^{[1]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{0}+tP_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\bigl(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[0]}]\bigr)(s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{0}+tP_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\bigl(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[0]}]\bigr)(s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{t}^{[1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{t}^{[1]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[0]}](s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[0]}](s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t}^{[2]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t}^{[2]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{0}+tP_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\bigl(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[1]}]\bigr)(s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{0}+tP_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\bigl(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[1]}]\bigr)(s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{t}^{[2]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{t}^{[2]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[1]}](s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{0}-\int_{0}^{t}\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[1]}](s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Note that we only ever need to evaluate these paths at the nodes <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can write the iterations in terms of the precomputed quantities</p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\int_{0}^{h}\ell_{j}(t)\,\mathrm{d}t\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\int_{0}^{h}\ell_{j}(t)\,\mathrm{d}t\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\int_{0}^{t_{i}}(t_{i}-t)\,\ell_{j}(t)\,\mathrm{d}t\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\int_{0}^{t_{i}}(t_{i}-t)\,\ell_{j}(t)\,\mathrm{d}t\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1\leqslant i,j\leqslant J\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1\leqslant i,j\leqslant J\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Finally, we replace <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> by the stochastic-gradient approximation
<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 3.2 ‣ 3.1 The smoothing trick ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>). Thus, throughout
this subsection, the algorithm has exact access to <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We replace these proximal queries by gradient queries in
<a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This leads to the following algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_algorithm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothed Picard HMC)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initialize
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\rm init}\coloneqq x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\rm init}\coloneqq x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\rm init}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\rm init}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Given
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{\rm init},P_{\rm init})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{\rm init},P_{\rm init})</annotation></semantics></math>, one
phase draws independent standard Gaussians
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1},(G_{j}^{[0]},G_{j}^{[1]})_{j=1}^{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1},(G_{j}^{[0]},G_{j}^{[1]})_{j=1}^{J}</annotation></semantics></math>, and performs the following steps.</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Partially refresh the momentum and create the starting trajectory.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="S3.I1.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{0}\coloneqq e^{-h/2}\,P_{\rm init}+\sqrt{1-e^{-h}}\,\zeta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}\coloneqq e^{-h/2}\,P_{\rm init}+\sqrt{1-e^{-h}}\,\zeta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I1.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+t_{j}P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+t_{j}P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Perform the first Picard update:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+t_{i}P_{0}-\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{i,j}\,\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]};G_{j}^{[0]})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+t_{i}P_{0}-\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{i,j}\,\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]};G_{j}^{[0]})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Perform the second Picard update:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{h}^{[2]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{h}^{[2]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+hP_{0}-\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{J,j}\,\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\,,\qquad P_{h}^{[2]}\coloneqq P_{0}-\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{j}\,\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+hP_{0}-\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{J,j}\,\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\,,\qquad P_{h}^{[2]}\coloneqq P_{0}-\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{j}\,\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Partially refresh the momentum and initialize the next phase.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="S3.I1.i4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\rm init}\coloneqq X_{h}^{[2]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\rm init}\coloneqq X_{h}^{[2]}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I1.i4.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{\rm init}\coloneqq e^{-h/2}\,P_{h}^{[2]}+\sqrt{1-e^{-h}}\,\zeta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\rm init}\coloneqq e^{-h/2}\,P_{h}^{[2]}+\sqrt{1-e^{-h}}\,\zeta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">After the prescribed number of phases, return <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\coloneqq X_{\rm init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\coloneqq X_{\rm init}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, recall from <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 The smoothing trick ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> that once we have an approximate sample from the smoothed distribution <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can recover an approximate sample from <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> by sampling from the RGO.
We implement this last step via FORS, leading to the full algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_algorithm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothed Picard HMC with a terminal FORS step)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the final position <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Algorithm 3.1 (Smoothed Picard HMC). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, independently run the terminal
FORS routine of <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> with target <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta,Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Return
its output <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\rm out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\rm out}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The exact guarantee is <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, and it is proven in <a href="#S4" title="4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
We next describe some of the ideas of the analysis at a high level in order to explain the source of the <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1/6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1/6}</annotation></semantics></math> scaling.
For the sake of exposition, we ignore the dependence on <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The analysis is based on the local error framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>, which produces multi-step <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds via computations of “local” or one-step errors.
The key is to decompose the one-step error into “deterministic” and “stochastic” components.
Over the course of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\asymp h^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\asymp h^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, the former is expected to accrue with a prefactor <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the latter only accrues with a prefactor <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> due to cancellations.
In our analysis, the “deterministic” component consists of two terms: the <em id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">bias</em> of our stochastic gradient estimator, since <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(\cdot;G)\neq g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(\cdot;G)\neq g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the <em id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">discretization error</em> of the Picard integrator.
The “stochastic” component consists of the fluctuations, or <em id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">variance</em>, produced by the stochastic gradient estimator.
We handle these terms individually.</p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discretization error.</span>
Here, the error further consists of two parts: the quadrature error, and the error of the Picard iteration itself.
They are controlled in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem15" title="Proposition 4.15 (Discretization error bound). ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.15</span></a>.</p>
<ul id="S3.I2.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Quadrature error.</em> It is classical that the error of approximating an integral via numerical quadrature depends strongly on the smoothness of the integrand.
In our setting, this amounts to the smoothness of <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By studying Gaussian cumulants, we present a refined estimate showing that the size of <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math> is of order at most <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>).
From this bound, we are able to show that the quadrature error is bounded by a term involving <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h/\sqrt{\eta})^{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h/\sqrt{\eta})^{J}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of Chebyshev–Lobatto nodes.
By taking polylogarithmic <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, this error is made negligible, provided <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&lt;\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&lt;\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This shows that the natural scale is to take <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\asymp\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≍</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\asymp\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we henceforth impose this choice in order to facilitate the interpretation of the subsequent bounds.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Picard error.</em>
The error of Picard iteration decreases exponentially with the depth.
We show that already for the depth-<math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> scheme, this error is of order <math id="S3.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}\,h^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}\,h^{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is negligible compared to the other error terms.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bias.</span> Deterministically, we have <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathbb{E}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(\cdot;G)-g_{\eta}\rVert\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathbb{E}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(\cdot;G)-g_{\eta}\rVert\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>).
Propagating this through the dynamics, it is straightforward to show that the bias error is of order <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}\,(h\eta^{3/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3})\asymp\sqrt{d}\,h^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≍</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}\,(h\eta^{3/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3})\asymp\sqrt{d}\,h^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 4.9 (Bias bound). ‣ 4.4.1 Bias bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variance.</span> As shown in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>, sharp analyses of stochastic gradient samplers should leverage the fact that <em id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">centered</em> perturbations of a standard Gaussian are closer in <math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to the Gaussian than a naïve coupling argument would predict; in fact, in this case, the <math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance scales with the square of the size of the perturbation.
We refer to this type of result as a second-order <math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> estimate.
We extend the convolution bound of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite> to a more general setting in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>, based on a novel heat flow interpolation argument.
We use this to prove a bound on the variance error term of order <math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}\,(\eta h^{3/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3})\lesssim\sqrt{d}\,h^{7/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}\,(\eta h^{3/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3})\lesssim\sqrt{d}\,h^{7/2}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem13" title="Proposition 4.13 (Variance bound). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.13</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">After accumulating these errors through the local error framework, we find that the multi-step error is of order <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}\,h^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}\,h^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, leading to the scaling <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h\asymp d^{-1/6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≍</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\asymp d^{-1/6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, since smoothed Picard HMC step targets the smoothed distribution <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need a terminal step in which we sample from the RGO <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As shown in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, when implemented with the exact diffusion sampler of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, the cost of this step is <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(1+(\eta^{2}d)^{1/3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(1+(\eta^{2}d)^{1/3})</annotation></semantics></math>.
At our scale <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta\asymp d^{-1/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≍</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\asymp d^{-1/3}</annotation></semantics></math>, this terminal step only costs <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(d^{1/9})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(d^{1/9})</annotation></semantics></math> queries, so it is not dominant.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Higher moment control</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our warm start construction, we need a stronger <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, for smoothed Picard HMC.
We establish the following result.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thminformalthmx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_informalthm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thminformalthmx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Informal theorem</span></span><span id="Thminformalthmx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(see <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (𝑊_𝑞 guarantee). ‣ 5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> for precise statement)<span id="Thminformalthmx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thminformalthmx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math> and we are given a reference point
<math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and fixed <math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, gradient-only smoothed
Picard HMC can choose a smoothing variance <math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and return a law
<math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}(\widehat{\pi}_{\eta},\pi_{\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}(\widehat{\pi}_{\eta},\pi_{\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, using</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\Bigl(\Bigl\{\kappa^{2}+\frac{\kappa^{4/3}\,(d+q)^{1/6}}{\varepsilon^{1/3}}\Bigr\}\,\Bigl\{q+\log\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\Bigr\}^{6}\Bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\Bigl(\Bigl\{\kappa^{2}+\frac{\kappa^{4/3}\,(d+q)^{1/6}}{\varepsilon^{1/3}}\Bigr\}\,\Bigl\{q+\log\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\Bigr\}^{6}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">gradient queries in expectation, with an implicit constant depending only on
<math id="Thminformalthmx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This is taken up in <a href="#S5" title="5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and follows the same outline as the analysis in <a href="#S4" title="4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, except that we need several <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> extensions of the ingredients from <a href="#S4" title="4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> which can be somewhat subtle.
Note that this theorem only guarantees closeness to the smoothed distribution <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, but this is all that is required for our warm start generator described in <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We highlight in particular that <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3 (Local error framework in 𝑊_𝑞). ‣ 5.2 𝑊_𝑞 local error analysis ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> establishes an <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> extension of the classical local error framework, which could be useful for future works.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Note that when we upgrade the <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee in <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> to a <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee, we pay a price which is polynomial in <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.
However, for our warm start application, we only need to take <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> to be logarithmic in the problem parameters, so this turns out to be harmless.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Recursive warm start generation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we develop a powerful recursive framework for warm start generation.
Here, we suppose we have access to a sampling subroutine which we call a <em id="S3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">smoothed sampler</em>.
Given a strongly convex and smooth potential <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, normalized to satisfy <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as an admissible reference point <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>, the smoothed sampler returns a smoothing level <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leqslant\eta\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leqslant\eta\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math> and a sample which is <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-close in law to <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{V}\propto\exp(-V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{V}\propto\exp(-V)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We remark that if <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq\beta I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq\beta I</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can apply the smoothed sampler to <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V(\cdot/\sqrt{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><msqrt><mi>β</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\cdot/\sqrt{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math>, and then rescale the output by <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
After this rescaling, the reported smoothing level <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the law of the rescaled sample being close to <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\beta^{-1}\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\beta^{-1}\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We consider three types of guarantees for the smoothed sampler: the output law is close to the smoothed distribution in <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, in <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>), or in the sub-Gaussian Orlicz–Wasserstein metric <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\psi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\psi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In these three cases, by taking advantage of regularization along the heat flow, we develop a recursive sampler that upgrades the guarantee to <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL</annotation></semantics></math>, to mixed <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> (as in the guarantee of <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2 (Warm start). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>), and to <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the RGO potential and distribution</p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{A,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{A,u}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq V+\frac{\lVert\cdot-u\rVert^{2}}{2A}\,,\qquad R^{V}_{A,u}\propto\exp(-V_{A,u})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq V+\frac{\lVert\cdot-u\rVert^{2}}{2A}\,,\qquad R^{V}_{A,u}\propto\exp(-V_{A,u})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The following recursive sampler aims to draw an approximate sample from the RGO distribution <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V}_{A,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V}_{A,u}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that when <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, this just corresponds to <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\propto\exp(-V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\propto\exp(-V)</annotation></semantics></math>. The sampling task is easier for smaller <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A,u}</annotation></semantics></math> then has a smaller condition number. The trick of the following algorithm is to recursively reduce the RGO sampling task to one with a smaller <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, until the terminal level is reached.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_algorithm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Recursive RGO sampler)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a terminal level <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{A}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{A}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="S3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\leqslant\underline{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⩽</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\leqslant\underline{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, then simply apply the localized FORS routine in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> directly to <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{A,u}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{A,u}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Otherwise, proceed via the following steps.</p>
<ul id="S3.I3.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Apply the smoothed sampler to <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A,u}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the reported smoothing level, and let <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> be the rescaled output.
Thus, <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(Z)\approx R_{A,u}^{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\beta_{A}^{-1}\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(Z)\approx R_{A,u}^{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,\beta_{A}^{-1}\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is the smoothness of <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A,u}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pick <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, draw an independent
<math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and form</p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\coloneqq Z+\sqrt{\frac{\tau}{\beta_{A}}}\,G\,,\qquad a\coloneqq\frac{\eta+\tau}{\beta_{A}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\coloneqq Z+\sqrt{\frac{\tau}{\beta_{A}}}\,G\,,\qquad a\coloneqq\frac{\eta+\tau}{\beta_{A}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(Y)\approx R^{V}_{A,u}*\mathsf{N}(0,aI)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(Y)\approx R^{V}_{A,u}*\mathsf{N}(0,aI)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We wish to obtain an approximate sample from <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V}_{A,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V}_{A,u}</annotation></semantics></math>. It suffices to sample from <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V_{A,u}}_{a,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V_{A,u}}_{a,Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Indeed, by the definition of the RGO, for any potential <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the identity <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\pi_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\pi_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim\pi_{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,aI)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim\pi_{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,aI)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim R^{V}_{a,Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim R^{V}_{a,Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 6.4 (RGO calculus). ‣ 6.2.2 RGO calculus ‣ 6.2 Technical tools ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>, we justify the following closure property of the RGO: <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{a,Y}^{V_{A,u}}=R^{V}_{A^{+},u^{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{a,Y}^{V_{A,u}}=R^{V}_{A^{+},u^{+}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the updated parameters are</p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{A^{+}}\coloneqq\frac{1}{A}+\frac{1}{a}\,,\qquad u^{+}\coloneqq A^{+}\,\Bigl(\frac{u}{A}+\frac{Y}{a}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>Y</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{A^{+}}\coloneqq\frac{1}{A}+\frac{1}{a}\,,\qquad u^{+}\coloneqq A^{+}\,\Bigl(\frac{u}{A}+\frac{Y}{a}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, we call the recursive RGO sampler on <math id="S3.I3.i2.I1.i3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V}_{A^{+},u^{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V}_{A^{+},u^{+}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
return its output.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">At this point, it may be unclear why we add an additional Gaussian to the output of the smoothed sampler.
In fact, this is the key step which enables the use of regularization along the heat flow—specifically, in the form of reverse transport inequalities—to upgrade the smoothed sampler guarantee from Wasserstein to stronger distances.
The guarantee for <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm 3.3 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> is given in <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 6.5 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We can apply <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm 3.3 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> to sample from <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> by taking <math id="S3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
However, if the iteration complexity of the smoothed sampler has poor dependence on the condition number, then it is better to wrap the entire recursive scheme within the proximal sampler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_algorithm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Proximal sampler wrapper)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given an initial sample <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, an outer variance <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\rm out}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\rm out}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
and a number <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> of outer steps, iterate as follows. At step
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\{0,\ldots,N-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\{0,\ldots,N-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, draw
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{n}=X_{n}+\mathsf{N}(0,a_{\rm out}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{n}=X_{n}+\mathsf{N}(0,a_{\rm out}I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the
output of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm 3.3 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> with target
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V}_{a_{\rm out},Y_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V}_{a_{\rm out},Y_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Return the final iterate <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">This wrapper ensures that we only ever call the smoothed sampler on well-conditioned targets, leading to an overall improved condition number dependence.
This aligns with the original use of the proximal sampler in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>.
The full guarantee for the recursive warm start generator is given in
<a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>.
We emphasize that the guarantee is fully generic and applies to any smoothed sampler implementing our interface.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Instantiating the recursive warm start generator with smoothed Picard HMC as a subroutine then establishes our warm start guarantee in <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2 (Warm start). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Proof of the <math id="S4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, our goal is to prove the <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee (<a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>). However, since we will later need to obtain stronger moment estimates for <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2 (Warm start). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>, we will first develop the part of the analysis that is common to both results.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Setup and smoothing estimates</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a positive-definite matrix <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q,M}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{X\sim P,\,Y\sim Q}\bigl(\mathbb{E}\lVert X-Y\rVert_{M}^{q}\bigr)^{1/q}\,,\qquad\lVert x\rVert_{M}\coloneqq(x^{\mathsf{T}}Mx)^{1/2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q,M}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{X\sim P,\,Y\sim Q}\bigl(\mathbb{E}\lVert X-Y\rVert_{M}^{q}\bigr)^{1/q}\,,\qquad\lVert x\rVert_{M}\coloneqq(x^{\mathsf{T}}Mx)^{1/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Recall that</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)\,,\qquad\Pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}p)\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x)\,\mathsf{N}(0,I)(\mathrm{d}p)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)\,,\qquad\Pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}p)\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x)\,\mathsf{N}(0,I)(\mathrm{d}p)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\mid Y=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\mid Y=y</annotation></semantics></math> be drawn from <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recalling the definition (<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 2.1 ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) of the proximal operator, throughout this section we write</p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{y}^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{y}^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">It is easy to check the identities</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}(y)=\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}\,(y-\mathbb{E}[X\mid Y=y])\,,\qquad\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}I-\eta^{-2}\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}(y)=\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}\,(y-\mathbb{E}[X\mid Y=y])\,,\qquad\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}I-\eta^{-2}\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hessian bounds for the smoothed potential)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\kappa+\eta}\,I\preceq\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}\preceq\frac{1}{1+\eta}\,I\preceq I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\kappa+\eta}\,I\preceq\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}\preceq\frac{1}{1+\eta}\,I\preceq I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The RGO potential has Hessian between
<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})\,I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\eta^{-1})\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta^{-1})\,I</annotation></semantics></math>. The
Brascamp–Lieb covariance inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\preceq(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\preceq(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the reverse bound, the
Cramér–Rao inequality (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Theorem 3.5.8]</cite>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\succeq(1+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\succeq(1+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute both bounds in
(<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following is the key estimate that decomposes the stochastic gradient error into a bias term and a stochastic error term.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stochastic gradient estimates)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Write</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(y)+b_{\eta}(y)+\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\,,\qquad\mathbb{E}\xi_{\eta}(y;G)=0\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(y)+b_{\eta}(y)+\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\,,\qquad\mathbb{E}\xi_{\eta}(y;G)=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for all <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,y,y^{\prime},G,G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,y,y^{\prime},G,G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert b_{\eta}(y)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert b_{\eta}(y)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}e^{\langle u,\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}e^{\langle u,\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant e^{\eta\,\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant e^{\eta\,\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y^{\prime};G)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y^{\prime};G)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G^{\prime})\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G^{\prime})\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G-G^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G-G^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proximal optimality gives
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{y}(u)\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\sqrt{\eta}\,\langle\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{y}(u)\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\sqrt{\eta}\,\langle\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq\nabla^{2}\rho_{y}\preceq\eta I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq\nabla^{2}\rho_{y}\preceq\eta I</annotation></semantics></math>, and under <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X-x_{y}^{+})/\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X-x_{y}^{+})/\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> has density
proportional to <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u\mapsto e^{-\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2-\rho_{y}(u)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto e^{-\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2-\rho_{y}(u)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Call this law <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\mathsf{r}_{y},\mathsf{N}(0,I))\leqslant\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\lVert\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\rVert^{2}]}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\lVert U\rVert^{2}}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\mathsf{r}_{y},\mathsf{N}(0,I))\leqslant\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\lVert\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\rVert^{2}]}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\lVert U\rVert^{2}}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, the first inequality combines Talagrand’s inequality for the standard
Gaussian with the Gaussian log-Sobolev inequality; the second uses that
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\rho_{y}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\rho_{y}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\rho_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\rho_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz; and the last
follows by integration by parts since <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly
log-concave with its mode at <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{\eta}(y)=\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\eta^{-1/2}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\,,\qquad\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)=\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\eta^{-1/2}\,\nabla\rho_{y}(G)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}(y)=\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\eta^{-1/2}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\,,\qquad\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)=\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\eta^{-1/2}\,\nabla\rho_{y}(G)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The gradient of <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, so
(<a href="#S4.E6" title="Equation 4.6 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>) gives (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 4.2 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>). Since <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, the standard Gaussian concentration inequality
gives (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 4.3 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>), and the same observation gives
(<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 4.5 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>). Finally, <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto x_{y}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto x_{y}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-expansive and
<math id="S4.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, proving (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We will also need high-order regularity of the smoothed potential. The key
point is a near-Gaussian cancellation, which is stronger than the generic moment bound for a
strongly log-concave law. The Gaussian cumulant estimates used in the proof
are collected in <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Derivatives of the smoothed potential)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every integer <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\,\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\,\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant(k-1)!\,\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">!</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant(k-1)!\,\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\,\lVert v\rVert=1}\,\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\,\lVert v\rVert=1}\,\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant(k-1)!\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">!</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant(k-1)!\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y)-\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y^{\prime})\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant 2\eta^{-1/2}\,\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y)-\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y^{\prime})\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant 2\eta^{-1/2}\,\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalized RGO from the proof of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. Its potential has Hessian between
<math id="S4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\eta)I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta)I</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimal transport
from the standard Gaussian to <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Caffarelli’s contraction theorem
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, applied in both directions, gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(1+\eta)^{-1/2}I\preceq DT_{y}\preceq I\,,\qquad\lVert DT_{y}-I\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant\eta/2\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="1.889em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta)^{-1/2}I\preceq DT_{y}\preceq I\,,\qquad\lVert DT_{y}-I\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant\eta/2\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">almost everywhere.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#A3.E22" title="Equation C.22 ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.22</span></a>), for <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)=-\eta^{-k}\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X\mid Y=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Cum</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)=-\eta^{-k}\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X\mid Y=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under the RGO,
<math id="S4.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}\,T_{y}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}\,T_{y}(G)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Translation invariance and homogeneity of
cumulants, followed by (<a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 4.10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>) and
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6 (Cumulants of a near-identity Gaussian image). ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a> with <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{T}\leqslant\eta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{T}\leqslant\eta/2</annotation></semantics></math>, prove
(<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 4.7 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>)–(<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>).
The case <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math> is <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Hessian bounds for the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>; integrating the
<math id="S4.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math> estimate (<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>) along a segment gives
(<a href="#S4.E9" title="Equation 4.9 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Local error analysis</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> proof will be based on the local error framework.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local error framework)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,\widehat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,\widehat{P}</annotation></semantics></math> be Markov kernels on <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that, for every
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a coupling
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\delta_{x}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\delta_{x}P</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim\delta_{y}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim\delta_{y}P</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert X-Y\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\rho\,\lVert x-y\rVert\,,\qquad\lVert(X-x)-(Y-y)\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\chi\,\lVert x-y\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert X-Y\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\rho\,\lVert x-y\rVert\,,\qquad\lVert(X-x)-(Y-y)\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\chi\,\lVert x-y\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose also that, writing <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{X}\sim\delta_{x}\widehat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{X}\sim\delta_{x}\widehat{P}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\delta_{x}\widehat{P},\delta_{x}P)\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\,,\qquad\lVert\mathbb{E}\widehat{X}-\mathbb{E}X\rVert\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\delta_{x}\widehat{P},\delta_{x}P)\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\,,\qquad\lVert\mathbb{E}\widehat{X}-\mathbb{E}X\rVert\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\rho&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\rho&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for all probability laws <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu</annotation></semantics></math> on
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}^{2}(\mu\widehat{P},\nu P)\leqslant\rho W_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)+\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}+\frac{(\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}+\chi\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong})^{2}}{\rho\,(1-\rho)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}^{2}(\mu\widehat{P},\nu P)\leqslant\rho W_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)+\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}+\frac{(\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}+\chi\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong})^{2}}{\rho\,(1-\rho)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is the standard local error theorem
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Lemma 5.1.2]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce three kernels and associated mappings.</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the one-phase
kernel defined by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Algorithm 3.1 (Smoothed Picard HMC). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> with
stochastic gradients <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can express the output of the phase as
<math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta,G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta,G)</annotation></semantics></math> for Gaussian variables <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="S4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta,G)\mid\zeta]\,,\qquad\bar{K}(z,\cdot)\coloneqq(\bar{\Phi}_{z})_{\#}\mathsf{N}(0,I_{2d})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta,G)\mid\zeta]\,,\qquad\bar{K}(z,\cdot)\coloneqq(\bar{\Phi}_{z})_{\#}\mathsf{N}(0,I_{2d})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, let <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> be the exact gradient numerical kernel obtained by
replacing every stochastic gradient <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> for the corresponding map, so that</p>
<table id="S4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(z,\cdot)\coloneqq(\Phi_{z})_{\#}\mathsf{N}(0,I_{2d})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(z,\cdot)\coloneqq(\Phi_{z})_{\#}\mathsf{N}(0,I_{2d})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">It is standard that contraction for HMC is only witnessed after a change of coordinates. Set</p>
<table id="S4.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\kappa}\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{2\kappa}+\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}\\[2.84526pt]
\frac{1}{2}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\otimes I_{d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\kappa}\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{2\kappa}+\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}\\[2.84526pt]
\frac{1}{2}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\otimes I_{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, this defines a metric which is uniformly equivalent to the Euclidean norm; such twisted metrics are standard in the analysis of kinetic dynamics; see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>.
We apply the lemma after the linear change of coordinates
<math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\mapsto M_{\kappa}^{1/2}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\mapsto M_{\kappa}^{1/2}z</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\coloneqq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\coloneqq K</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P}\coloneqq\widehat{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P}\coloneqq\widehat{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The structure of the proof is given by the following key theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local error analysis in <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume that <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leqslant c/(\kappa\log J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leqslant c/(\kappa\log J)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for every phase-space law <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant(1-ch/\kappa)\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa}{h}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}^{2})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>disc</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant(1-ch/\kappa)\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa}{h}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}^{2})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z,\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\,\lVert\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert\,,\quad\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}\coloneqq\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}W_{2}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K},\delta_{z}\bar{K})\,,\quad\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}\coloneqq W_{2}(\Pi_{\eta}K,\Pi_{\eta})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z,\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\,\lVert\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert\,,\quad\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}\coloneqq\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}W_{2}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K},\delta_{z}\bar{K})\,,\quad\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}\coloneqq W_{2}(\Pi_{\eta}K,\Pi_{\eta})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K}^{N},\Pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K}^{N},\Pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant e^{-cNh/\kappa}\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+\frac{C\kappa}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa^{2}}{h^{2}}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}^{2})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>disc</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant e^{-cNh/\kappa}\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+\frac{C\kappa}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa^{2}}{h^{2}}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}^{2})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z,z^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z,z^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math> and set
<math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\coloneqq\Phi_{z}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\coloneqq\Phi_{z}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\prime}\coloneqq\Phi_{z^{\prime}}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\prime}\coloneqq\Phi_{z^{\prime}}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{J}\leqslant C\log(J+1)\leqslant C\log J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{J}\leqslant C\log(J+1)\leqslant C\log J</annotation></semantics></math>, the assumption on <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> implies
the hypotheses of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 4.7 (Contraction). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Propositions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 4.8 (Synchronous increment coupling). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a> below.
Those results verify (<a href="#S4.E11" title="Equation 4.11 ‣ Lemma 4.4 (Local error framework). ‣ 4.2 Local error analysis ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>) with
<math id="S4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z,Z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z,Z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> in place of <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>. We can bound</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\,\lVert\mathbb{E}\widehat{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta,G)-\mathbb{E}\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\mathbb{E}\lVert\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\,\lVert\mathbb{E}\widehat{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta,G)-\mathbb{E}\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\mathbb{E}\lVert\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K},\delta_{z}K)\leqslant\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\,\{W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K},\delta_{z}\bar{K})+W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\delta_{z}\bar{K},\delta_{z}K)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K},\delta_{z}K)\leqslant\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\,\{W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K},\delta_{z}\bar{K})+W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\delta_{z}\bar{K},\delta_{z}K)\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">since the <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> norm is equivalent to the standard Euclidean norm.
Thus, the hypotheses of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4.4 (Local error framework). ‣ 4.2 Local error analysis ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> hold with</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\coloneqq 1-\frac{ch}{\kappa}\,,\qquad\chi\coloneqq Ch\,,\qquad\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\leqslant C\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}})\,,\qquad\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\coloneqq 1-\frac{ch}{\kappa}\,,\qquad\chi\coloneqq Ch\,,\qquad\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\leqslant C\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}})\,,\qquad\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">We obtain</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta}K)\leqslant\Bigl(1-\frac{ch}{\kappa}\Bigr)\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta}K)\leqslant\Bigl(1-\frac{ch}{\kappa}\Bigr)\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">By Young’s inequality, for <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant(1+\lambda)\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta}K)+(1+\lambda^{-1})\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\Pi_{\eta}K,\Pi_{\eta})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant(1+\lambda)\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta}K)+(1+\lambda^{-1})\,W_{2,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\Pi_{\eta}K,\Pi_{\eta})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Uniform norm equivalence gives
<math id="S4.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\Pi_{\eta}K,\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\Pi_{\eta}K,\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\asymp h/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≍</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\asymp h/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. After reducing
the universal constant in the contraction factor <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ch/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ch/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, this proves the one-step
bound; summing the recurrence proves the global bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The three errors <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}</annotation></semantics></math> correspond,
respectively, to the bias and centered fluctuation of the stochastic gradient
phase and to the discretization error of the numerical kernel. Thus, the
main task is to bound these errors.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Properties of the exact-gradient kernel</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a\coloneqq e^{-h/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\coloneqq e^{-h/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for a symmetric matrix <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>,
let</p>
<table id="S4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{H}\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;I\\
-H&amp;-I\end{bmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{H}\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;I\\
-H&amp;-I\end{bmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In the lemma below, we make use of the Lebesgue constant <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> for the Chebyshev–Lobatto nodes.
By <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Chebyshev–Lobatto coefficient bounds). ‣ B.1 Nodes, interpolating polynomials, and integrated weights ‣ Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we have <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{J}\lesssim\log J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{J}\lesssim\log J</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First-order difference expansion)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Couple draws <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}\sim\delta_{z}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}\sim\delta_{z}K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}^{\prime}\sim\delta_{z^{\prime}}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}^{\prime}\sim\delta_{z^{\prime}}K</annotation></semantics></math> from
phase-space inputs
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\coloneqq(x_{\rm init},p_{\rm init})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\coloneqq(x_{\rm init},p_{\rm init})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\prime}\coloneqq(x^{\prime}_{\rm init},p^{\prime}_{\rm init})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\prime}\coloneqq(x^{\prime}_{\rm init},p^{\prime}_{\rm init})</annotation></semantics></math> using the same Gaussian variables.
Set</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{0}\coloneqq z-z^{\prime}\,,\qquad\Delta_{1}\coloneqq Z_{1}-Z_{1}^{\prime}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{0}\coloneqq z-z^{\prime}\,,\qquad\Delta_{1}\coloneqq Z_{1}-Z_{1}^{\prime}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}=(I+hA_{H})\Delta_{0}+\mathcal{R}_{h}\Delta_{0}\,,\qquad\lVert\mathcal{R}_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}=(I+hA_{H})\Delta_{0}+\mathcal{R}_{h}\Delta_{0}\,,\qquad\lVert\mathcal{R}_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for a symmetric <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2\kappa}\,I\preceq H\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2\kappa}\,I\preceq H\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To verify this, write
<math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta x\coloneqq x_{\rm init}-x^{\prime}_{\rm init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta x\coloneqq x_{\rm init}-x^{\prime}_{\rm init}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta p\coloneqq p_{\rm init}-p^{\prime}_{\rm init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta p\coloneqq p_{\rm init}-p^{\prime}_{\rm init}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The difference of gradients can be written as</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}(x)-g_{\eta}(x^{\prime})=H(x,x^{\prime})\,(x-x^{\prime})\,,\quad H(x,x^{\prime})\coloneqq\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(x^{\prime}+t\,(x-x^{\prime}))\,\mathrm{d}t\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}(x)-g_{\eta}(x^{\prime})=H(x,x^{\prime})\,(x-x^{\prime})\,,\quad H(x,x^{\prime})\coloneqq\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(x^{\prime}+t\,(x-x^{\prime}))\,\mathrm{d}t\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Hessian bounds for the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>,
<math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2\kappa}\,I\preceq H\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2\kappa}\,I\preceq H\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first OU half-step changes <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta p</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\,\Delta p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\,\Delta p</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}=\Delta x+at_{j}\,\Delta p\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}=\Delta x+at_{j}\,\Delta p\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Writing <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}^{[0]}\coloneqq H(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]},X_{t_{j}}^{\prime[0]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}^{[0]}\coloneqq H(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]},X_{t_{j}}^{\prime[0]})</annotation></semantics></math>,
the first Picard update gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}=\Delta x+at_{i}\,\Delta p\underbrace{-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}H_{j}^{[0]}\,(\Delta x+at_{j}\,\Delta p)}_{\eqqcolon E_{i}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}=\Delta x+at_{i}\,\Delta p\underbrace{-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}H_{j}^{[0]}\,(\Delta x+at_{j}\,\Delta p)}_{\eqqcolon E_{i}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">The bounds <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert H_{j}^{[0]}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert H_{j}^{[0]}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}\leqslant h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}\leqslant h</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}/2</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Chebyshev–Lobatto coefficient bounds). ‣ B.1 Nodes, interpolating polynomials, and integrated weights ‣ Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>) imply</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert E_{i}\rVert\leqslant\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|\,\bigl(\lVert\Delta x\rVert+at_{j}\,\lVert\Delta p\rVert\bigr)\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\,\bigl(\lVert\Delta x\rVert+h\,\lVert\Delta p\rVert\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.111em">⩽</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert E_{i}\rVert\leqslant\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|\,\bigl(\lVert\Delta x\rVert+at_{j}\,\lVert\Delta p\rVert\bigr)\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\,\bigl(\lVert\Delta x\rVert+h\,\lVert\Delta p\rVert\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then, set</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}\coloneqq H\bigl(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]},X_{t_{j}}^{\prime[1]}\bigr)\,,\qquad H\coloneqq h^{-1}\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}H_{j}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}\coloneqq H\bigl(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]},X_{t_{j}}^{\prime[1]}\bigr)\,,\qquad H\coloneqq h^{-1}\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}H_{j}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Positivity and <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}=h</annotation></semantics></math> imply
<math id="S4.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2\kappa}\,I\preceq H\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2\kappa}\,I\preceq H\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>. The exact endpoint differences are</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta X_{\rm init}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta X_{\rm init}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta x+ah\,\Delta p-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{J,j}H_{j}\,\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\,,\qquad\Delta P_{\rm init}^{+}=a^{2}\,\Delta p-a\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}H_{j}\,\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta x+ah\,\Delta p-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{J,j}H_{j}\,\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\,,\qquad\Delta P_{\rm init}^{+}=a^{2}\,\Delta p-a\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}H_{j}\,\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Subtract <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta x+h\,\Delta p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta x+h\,\Delta p</annotation></semantics></math> from the first line and
<math id="S4.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta p-hH\,\Delta x-h\,\Delta p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta p-hH\,\Delta x-h\,\Delta p</annotation></semantics></math> from the second. Use
<math id="S4.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=1-h/2+O(h^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=1-h/2+O(h^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{2}=1-h+O(h^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{2}=1-h+O(h^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A2.E2" title="Equation B.2 ‣ Proposition B.1 (Chebyshev–Lobatto coefficient bounds). ‣ B.1 Nodes, interpolating polynomials, and integrated weights ‣ Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>), and the preceding bound on <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Every remaining
term is bounded by
<math id="S4.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert(\Delta x,\Delta p)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert(\Delta x,\Delta p)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>, which proves the claimed
expansion.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.7</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Contraction)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant c/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant c/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, then, for all <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z,z^{\prime},\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z,z^{\prime},\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\Phi_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z^{\prime}}(\zeta)\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant\Bigl(1-\frac{ch}{\kappa}\Bigr)\,\lVert z-z^{\prime}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\Phi_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z^{\prime}}(\zeta)\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant\Bigl(1-\frac{ch}{\kappa}\Bigr)\,\lVert z-z^{\prime}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> be a unit
eigenvector of <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> with eigenvalue
<math id="S4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[\frac{1}{2\kappa},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[\frac{1}{2\kappa},1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The two-dimensional phase-space subspace <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{(uq,vq):u,v\in\mathbb{R}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(uq,vq):u,v\in\mathbb{R}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
is invariant under <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the coordinates <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math>, the restrictions
of <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> to this subspace are represented by</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{H}(uq,vq)=\bigl(vq,-(\lambda u+v)q\bigr)\,,\qquad A_{\lambda}\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;1\\
-\lambda&amp;-1\end{bmatrix}\,,\qquad M_{\kappa}^{(2)}\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{2\kappa}+\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}\\[2.84526pt]
\frac{1}{2}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{H}(uq,vq)=\bigl(vq,-(\lambda u+v)q\bigr)\,,\qquad A_{\lambda}\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;1\\
-\lambda&amp;-1\end{bmatrix}\,,\qquad M_{\kappa}^{(2)}\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{2\kappa}+\frac{1}{2}&amp;\frac{1}{2}\\[2.84526pt]
\frac{1}{2}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">A direct calculation gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\lambda}^{\mathsf{T}}M_{\kappa}^{(2)}+M_{\kappa}^{(2)}A_{\lambda}=-\begin{bmatrix}\lambda&amp;\lambda-\frac{1}{2\kappa}\\
\lambda-\frac{1}{2\kappa}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\preceq-\frac{1}{8\kappa}\,M_{\kappa}^{(2)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>λ</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>λ</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\lambda}^{\mathsf{T}}M_{\kappa}^{(2)}+M_{\kappa}^{(2)}A_{\lambda}=-\begin{bmatrix}\lambda&amp;\lambda-\frac{1}{2\kappa}\\
\lambda-\frac{1}{2\kappa}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\preceq-\frac{1}{8\kappa}\,M_{\kappa}^{(2)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, the positive matrix after the minus sign has trace at most <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and
determinant</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda-\Bigl(\lambda-\frac{1}{2\kappa}\Bigr)^{2}\geqslant\frac{1}{2\kappa}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda-\Bigl(\lambda-\frac{1}{2\kappa}\Bigr)^{2}\geqslant\frac{1}{2\kappa}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Its smallest eigenvalue is therefore at least <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/(4\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/(4\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S4.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\kappa}^{(2)}\preceq 2I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\kappa}^{(2)}\preceq 2I</annotation></semantics></math>, this proves (<a href="#S4.E14" title="Equation 4.14 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.14</span></a>).
Decomposing along an orthonormal eigenbasis of <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> yields the full
phase-space inequality</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{H}^{\mathsf{T}}M_{\kappa}+M_{\kappa}A_{H}\preceq-\frac{1}{8\kappa}\,M_{\kappa}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{H}^{\mathsf{T}}M_{\kappa}+M_{\kappa}A_{H}\preceq-\frac{1}{8\kappa}\,M_{\kappa}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Apply <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 4.6 (First-order difference expansion). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>. Uniform equivalence of
the Euclidean and <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> norms gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathcal{R}_{h}\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathcal{R}_{h}\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding the square and
applying (<a href="#S4.E15" title="Equation 4.15 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.15</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\Delta_{1}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}^{2}\leqslant\{1-ch/\kappa+C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\}\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\Delta_{1}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}^{2}\leqslant\{1-ch/\kappa+C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\}\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">The step size restriction absorbs the last term. Taking square roots and changing
the universal constant gives (<a href="#S4.E13" title="Equation 4.13 ‣ Proposition 4.7 (Contraction). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.13</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.8</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Synchronous increment coupling)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant c/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant c/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, then, for all <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z,z^{\prime},\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z,z^{\prime},\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\{\Phi_{z}(\zeta)-z\}-\{\Phi_{z^{\prime}}(\zeta)-z^{\prime}\}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant Ch\,\lVert z-z^{\prime}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\{\Phi_{z}(\zeta)-z\}-\{\Phi_{z^{\prime}}(\zeta)-z^{\prime}\}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant Ch\,\lVert z-z^{\prime}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Subtract <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from the expansion in
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 4.6 (First-order difference expansion). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>. Uniform equivalence of the
Euclidean and <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> norms, together with
<math id="S4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert H\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert H\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, gives
<math id="S4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert A_{H}\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert A_{H}\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover,
<math id="S4.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\leqslant h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\leqslant h</annotation></semantics></math> under the step-size assumption. Hence
<math id="S4.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\Delta_{1}-\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant Ch\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\Delta_{1}-\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant Ch\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is
(<a href="#S4.E16" title="Equation 4.16 ‣ Lemma 4.8 (Synchronous increment coupling). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.16</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Local error bounds</h3>

<section id="S4.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.4.1 </span>Bias bound</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first control the displacement between the conditional mean and
exact gradient kernels. Put</p>
<table id="S4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}_{\eta}(y)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)=g_{\eta}(y)+b_{\eta}(y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}_{\eta}(y)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)=g_{\eta}(y)+b_{\eta}(y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.9</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bias bound)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\bigl(h\eta^{3/2}+\Lambda_{J}\eta^{1/2}h^{3}\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\bigl(h\eta^{3/2}+\Lambda_{J}\eta^{1/2}h^{3}\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z,\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z,\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math> and write</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\coloneqq\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\,\lVert b_{\eta}(y)\rVert\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\coloneqq\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\,\lVert b_{\eta}(y)\rVert\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">by (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 4.2 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>). To distinguish the two
first Picard updates, let <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the iterate obtained with
the exact gradient <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}</annotation></semantics></math> denote
the iterate obtained with <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking the expectation over the first
stochastic gradient block,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}-X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}-X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\widehat{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}\mid\zeta]-X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}=-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}b_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\widehat{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}\mid\zeta]-X_{t_{i}}^{[1]}=-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}b_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, (<a href="#A2.E2" title="Equation B.2 ‣ Proposition B.1 (Chebyshev–Lobatto coefficient bounds). ‣ B.1 Nodes, interpolating polynomials, and integrated weights ‣ Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>) gives the
estimate</span></p>
<table id="S4.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert\bar{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]}-X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\rVert\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\,B\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert\bar{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]}-X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\rVert\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\,B\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">We also need to control the fluctuations:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}-\bar{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}=-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}\xi_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]};G_{j}^{[0]})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}-\bar{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}=-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}\xi_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]};G_{j}^{[0]})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">The variables in the sum are independent and centered, and
(<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 4.3 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>) implies
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\lVert\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\rVert^{2}\leqslant\eta d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\lVert\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\rVert^{2}\leqslant\eta d</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\lVert\widehat{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}-\bar{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}\rVert^{2}\mid\zeta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\lVert\widehat{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}-\bar{X}_{t_{i}}^{[1]}\rVert^{2}\mid\zeta]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[\lVert\xi_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]};G_{j}^{[0]})\rVert^{2}\mid\zeta]\leqslant\eta d\,\Bigl(\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|\Bigr)^{2}\leqslant\frac{h^{4}\Lambda_{J}^{2}}{4}\,\eta d\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[\lVert\xi_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]};G_{j}^{[0]})\rVert^{2}\mid\zeta]\leqslant\eta d\,\Bigl(\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|\Bigr)^{2}\leqslant\frac{h^{4}\Lambda_{J}^{2}}{4}\,\eta d\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to propagate these errors through the endpoint update.
The endpoint stochastic gradient block is independent of the first block,
so for each <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{g}_{\eta}(\widehat{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\mid\zeta]=\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{\eta}(\widehat{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]})\mid\zeta]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{g}_{\eta}(\widehat{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\mid\zeta]=\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{\eta}(\widehat{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]})\mid\zeta]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(\,\cdot\,;G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(\,\cdot\,;G)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz for every <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>,
so is <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}_{\eta}=g_{\eta}+b_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}_{\eta}=g_{\eta}+b_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, followed by
(<a href="#S4.E18" title="Equation 4.18 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.4.1 Bias bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.18</span></a>),
(<a href="#S4.E19" title="Equation 4.19 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.4.1 Bias bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.19</span></a>), and Jensen’s inequality,
we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{\eta}(\widehat{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]})\mid\zeta]-g_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]})\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{\eta}(\widehat{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]})\mid\zeta]-g_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]})\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\mathbb{E}[\lVert\widehat{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]}-\bar{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\rVert\mid\zeta]+\lVert\bar{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]}-X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\rVert+\lVert b_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]})\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\mathbb{E}[\lVert\widehat{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]}-\bar{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\rVert\mid\zeta]+\lVert\bar{X}_{t_{j}}^{[1]}-X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\rVert+\lVert b_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]})\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\sqrt{\eta d}+\Bigl(1+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)\,B\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\sqrt{\eta d}+\Bigl(1+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)\,B\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The position and momentum components of
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> are obtained by weighting these
gradient differences by <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{J,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{J,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Since</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{J,j}|\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\,,\qquad a\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}=ah\leqslant h\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{J,j}|\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\,,\qquad a\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}=ah\leqslant h\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We conclude that</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\Bigl(h+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)\,\Bigl\{\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\sqrt{\eta d}+\Bigl(1+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)B\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\Bigl(h+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)\,\Bigl\{\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\sqrt{\eta d}+\Bigl(1+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)B\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant Ch\,\bigl(B+h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\sqrt{\eta d}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant Ch\,\bigl(B+h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\sqrt{\eta d}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\bigl(\eta^{3/2}h+\Lambda_{J}\eta^{1/2}h^{3}\bigr)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\bigl(\eta^{3/2}h+\Lambda_{J}\eta^{1/2}h^{3}\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The bound is uniform in <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>, proving
(<a href="#S4.E17" title="Equation 4.17 ‣ Proposition 4.9 (Bias bound). ‣ 4.4.1 Bias bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.17</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.4.2 </span>Variance bound</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a phase-space input <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\coloneqq(x_{\rm init},p_{\rm init})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\coloneqq(x_{\rm init},p_{\rm init})</annotation></semantics></math>, and put
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\coloneqq(1-e^{-h})^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\coloneqq(1-e^{-h})^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Collect the OU
variables as
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\coloneqq(\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1})\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I_{2d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\coloneqq(\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1})\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I_{2d})</annotation></semantics></math> and all
Gaussian variables used by the stochastic gradients as <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\rm all}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>all</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\rm all}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</p>
<table id="S4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}\coloneqq h^{-1}\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\,,\qquad\mathcal{G}^{\prime}\coloneqq h^{-2}\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{J,j}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}\coloneqq h^{-1}\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\,,\qquad\mathcal{G}^{\prime}\coloneqq h^{-2}\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{J,j}\widehat{g}_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[1]};G_{j}^{[1]})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Direct substitution in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Algorithm 3.1 (Smoothed Picard HMC). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> gives</p>
<table id="S4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}X_{\rm init}^{+}\\[2.5pt]
P_{\rm init}^{+}\end{bmatrix}=u+B_{h}\{\zeta+F(\zeta,G_{\rm all})\}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>all</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}X_{\rm init}^{+}\\[2.5pt]
P_{\rm init}^{+}\end{bmatrix}=u+B_{h}\{\zeta+F(\zeta,G_{\rm all})\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}x_{\rm init}+ah\,p_{\rm init}\\
a^{2}\,p_{\rm init}\end{bmatrix}\,,\qquad B_{h}\coloneqq\sigma\begin{bmatrix}hI&amp;0\\
aI&amp;I\end{bmatrix}\,,\qquad F\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}-h\mathcal{G}^{\prime}/\sigma\\
ah\,(\mathcal{G}^{\prime}-\mathcal{G})/\sigma\end{bmatrix}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}x_{\rm init}+ah\,p_{\rm init}\\
a^{2}\,p_{\rm init}\end{bmatrix}\,,\qquad B_{h}\coloneqq\sigma\begin{bmatrix}hI&amp;0\\
aI&amp;I\end{bmatrix}\,,\qquad F\coloneqq\begin{bmatrix}-h\mathcal{G}^{\prime}/\sigma\\
ah\,(\mathcal{G}^{\prime}-\mathcal{G})/\sigma\end{bmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Moreover, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h/\sigma\asymp\sqrt{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h/\sigma\asymp\sqrt{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert M_{\kappa}^{1/2}B_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C\sqrt{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert M_{\kappa}^{1/2}B_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C\sqrt{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The purpose of this decomposition is to apply the refined second-order <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> estimate in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> below.
First, we record some Lipschitz estimates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.10</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitz bounds)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, then, uniformly in the input,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert F(\zeta,G)-F(\zeta^{\prime},G)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert F(\zeta,G)-F(\zeta^{\prime},G)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert\zeta-\zeta^{\prime}\rVert\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert\zeta-\zeta^{\prime}\rVert\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert F(\zeta,G)-F(\zeta,G^{\prime})\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert F(\zeta,G)-F(\zeta,G^{\prime})\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}\sqrt{\eta h}\,\lVert G-G^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}\sqrt{\eta h}\,\lVert G-G^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider first two OU inputs <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\coloneqq(\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\coloneqq(\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta^{\prime}\coloneqq(\zeta_{0}^{\prime},\zeta_{1}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ζ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta^{\prime}\coloneqq(\zeta_{0}^{\prime},\zeta_{1}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, with the stochastic gradient variables
fixed. The map <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}(\zeta_{0})-X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}(\zeta_{0}^{\prime})\rVert=\sigma t_{j}\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant\sigma h\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}(\zeta_{0})-X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}(\zeta_{0}^{\prime})\rVert=\sigma t_{j}\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant\sigma h\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) and then (<a href="#A2.E2" title="Equation B.2 ‣ Proposition B.1 (Chebyshev–Lobatto coefficient bounds). ‣ B.1 Nodes, interpolating polynomials, and integrated weights ‣ Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}(\zeta_{0},G^{[0]})-X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}(\zeta_{0}^{\prime},G^{[0]})\rVert\leqslant\sigma h\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\,\sigma h\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant 2\sigma h\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}(\zeta_{0},G^{[0]})-X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}(\zeta_{0}^{\prime},G^{[0]})\rVert\leqslant\sigma h\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\,\sigma h\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant 2\sigma h\,\lVert\zeta_{0}-\zeta_{0}^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{j}\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{j}\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}=h</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{J,j}|\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{J,j}|\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}/2</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\Delta\mathcal{G}\rVert\leqslant C\sigma h\,\lVert\Delta\zeta_{0}\rVert\,,\qquad\lVert\Delta\mathcal{G}^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}\sigma h\,\lVert\Delta\zeta_{0}\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\Delta\mathcal{G}\rVert\leqslant C\sigma h\,\lVert\Delta\zeta_{0}\rVert\,,\qquad\lVert\Delta\mathcal{G}^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}\sigma h\,\lVert\Delta\zeta_{0}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Multiplying by the factor <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h/\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h/\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> in the definition of <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> proves
(<a href="#S4.E20" title="Equation 4.20 ‣ Lemma 4.10 (Lipschitz bounds). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.20</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now fix <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> and compare two collections
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\coloneqq(G^{[0]},G^{[1]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\coloneqq(G^{[0]},G^{[1]})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}\coloneqq(G^{\prime[0]},G^{\prime[1]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}\coloneqq(G^{\prime[0]},G^{\prime[1]})</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 4.5 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\rVert\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G^{[0]}-G^{\prime[0]}\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}\rVert\leqslant\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G^{[0]}-G^{\prime[0]}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">At the endpoint gradient evaluations, the first block changes the input
locations through <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[1]}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the second block
changes the Gaussian arguments directly. The Lipschitz estimates in both
arguments therefore yield</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\Delta\mathcal{G}\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\Delta\mathcal{G}\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\bigl\{\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert\Delta G^{[0]}\rVert+\lVert\Delta G^{[1]}\rVert\bigr\}\,,\qquad\lVert\Delta\mathcal{G}^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\bigl\{\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{2}\,\lVert\Delta G^{[0]}\rVert+\Lambda_{J}\,\lVert\Delta G^{[1]}\rVert\bigr\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\bigl\{\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert\Delta G^{[0]}\rVert+\lVert\Delta G^{[1]}\rVert\bigr\}\,,\qquad\lVert\Delta\mathcal{G}^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\bigl\{\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{2}\,\lVert\Delta G^{[0]}\rVert+\Lambda_{J}\,\lVert\Delta G^{[1]}\rVert\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Use <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h/\sigma\leqslant C\sqrt{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h/\sigma\leqslant C\sqrt{h}</annotation></semantics></math> in the definition of <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>,
together with <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, to obtain the second bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The key to our analysis is the following refined bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.11</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Second-order <math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> estimate)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Hilbert space, let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> be independent, and let
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{m}\times\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{m}\times\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert f(z,g)-f(z^{\prime},g)\rVert\leqslant A\,\lVert z-z^{\prime}\rVert\,,\qquad\lVert f(z,g)-f(z,g^{\prime})\rVert\leqslant B\,\lVert g-g^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert f(z,g)-f(z^{\prime},g)\rVert\leqslant A\,\lVert z-z^{\prime}\rVert\,,\qquad\lVert f(z,g)-f(z,g^{\prime})\rVert\leqslant B\,\lVert g-g^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(z,g)-f(z,g^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z,g)-f(z,g^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to a fixed subspace
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the orthogonal projection
onto <math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L:\mathbb{R}^{m}\to\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L:\mathbb{R}^{m}\to\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is linear and
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}(Z)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[f(Z,G)\mid Z]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}(Z)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[f(Z,G)\mid Z]</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\bigl(\law\{L(Z+f(Z,G))\},\law\{L(Z+\bar{f}(Z))\}\bigr)\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+5\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\Bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\bigl(\law\{L(Z+f(Z,G))\},\law\{L(Z+\bar{f}(Z))\}\bigr)\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+5\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">It is instructive to compare this to a more trivial bound.
The obvious coupling, together with the Gaussian Poincaré inequality applied conditionally on <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> and over the subspace <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, yields</p>
<table id="S4.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\lVert L(Z+f(Z,G))-L(Z+\bar{f}(Z))\rVert^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\lVert L(Z+f(Z,G))-L(Z+\bar{f}(Z))\rVert^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\lVert L\Pi_{E}(f(Z,G)-\bar{f}(Z))\rVert^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\lVert L\Pi_{E}(f(Z,G)-\bar{f}(Z))\rVert^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[\lVert f(Z,G)-\bar{f}(Z)\rVert^{2}]\leqslant m\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\,B^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\,\mathbb{E}[\lVert f(Z,G)-\bar{f}(Z)\rVert^{2}]\leqslant m\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\,B^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This yields</p>
<table id="S4.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\bigl(\law\{L(Z+f(Z,G))\},\law\{L(Z+\bar{f}(Z))\}\bigr)\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\bigl(\law\{L(Z+f(Z,G))\},\law\{L(Z+\bar{f}(Z))\}\bigr)\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">This argument does not use any assumption on the distribution of <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>.
In contrast, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> uses the fact that <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is Gaussian, together with the fact that the difference <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Z,G)-\bar{f}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Z,G)-\bar{f}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> is conditionally centered, to obtain a second-order bound which depends quadratically on <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.
The proof, given in
<a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Proofs of the second-order Wasserstein estimates ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, is based on heat flow interpolation and Gaussian integration by parts.
We remark that for the purpose of this paper, we only need the case <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 4.12</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Related second-order estimates are known for centered perturbations
independent of the Gaussian variable being perturbed: see
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>, Lemma 1]</cite> for bounded perturbations on a one-dimensional
subspace, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, Theorems 2.1 and 2.7]</cite> for more general Gaussian
convolution inequalities, and the Ingster–Suslina second moment method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> for divergence bounds.
A complementary heat flow perspective is given by
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, Theorem 2.1]</cite>: the first unmatched moment determines the
asymptotic decay of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> under Gaussian smoothing.
These independent perturbation results do not apply directly when
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Z,G)-\bar{f}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Z,G)-\bar{f}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the Gaussian <math id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> providing the
smoothing; the <math id="S4.Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> term in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>
accounts for this dependence.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">With this in hand, we can now bound the variance term.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.13</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance bound)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <math id="S4.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,\bigl(\eta h^{3/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3}\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,\bigl(\eta h^{3/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3}\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> with</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2d\,,\qquad Z=\zeta\,,\qquad G=G_{\rm all}\,,\qquad f=F\,,\qquad L=B_{h}\,,\qquad E=\mathbb{R}^{2d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>all</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2d\,,\qquad Z=\zeta\,,\qquad G=G_{\rm all}\,,\qquad f=F\,,\qquad L=B_{h}\,,\qquad E=\mathbb{R}^{2d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma 4.10 (Lipschitz bounds). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>, we may take</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\qquad\text{and}\qquad B=C\Lambda_{J}\sqrt{\eta h}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\qquad\text{and}\qquad B=C\Lambda_{J}\sqrt{\eta h}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert B_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C\sqrt{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert B_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C\sqrt{h}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<a href="#S4.E21" title="In Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.21</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\lVert B_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,(B^{2}+AB)\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,(\eta h^{3/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3})\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\lVert B_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,(B^{2}+AB)\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,(\eta h^{3/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3})\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.4.3 </span>Discretization error bound</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the Hamiltonian generator.</p>
<table id="S4.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}\coloneqq\langle p,\nabla_{x}\rangle-\langle g_{\eta}(x),\nabla_{p}\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}\coloneqq\langle p,\nabla_{x}\rangle-\langle g_{\eta}(x),\nabla_{p}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For a position vector field <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=(W_{i})_{i\in[d]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=(W_{i})_{i\in[d]}</annotation></semantics></math>, put
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\coloneqq\langle g_{\eta},W\rangle-\operatorname{div}_{x}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\coloneqq\langle g_{\eta},W\rangle-\operatorname{div}_{x}W</annotation></semantics></math>. Integration by
parts under <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-V_{\eta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-V_{\eta}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the identity</p>
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})}^{2}\leqslant\lVert W\rVert_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}^{2}+\lVert D_{x}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})}^{2}\leqslant\lVert W\rVert_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}^{2}+\lVert D_{x}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Indeed, expanding the square and integrating the two cross terms produces a
contraction of the derivative arrays and the quadratic form generated by
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>; Cauchy–Schwarz and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math> give the displayed bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma relies on Gaussian polynomial bounds collected in
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma C.7 (Gaussian polynomial estimates). ‣ C.4 Gaussian polynomial bounds ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>. In particular, if a
Hilbert-valued momentum polynomial <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(p)</annotation></semantics></math> and a polynomial vector field
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(p)</annotation></semantics></math> have degree at most <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert D_{p}F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\sqrt{r}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\,,\qquad\lVert\delta_{\gamma}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\leqslant\sqrt{r+1}\,\lVert W\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert D_{p}F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\sqrt{r}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\,,\qquad\lVert\delta_{\gamma}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\leqslant\sqrt{r+1}\,\lVert W\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.14</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stationary iterated derivatives in <math id="S4.Thmtheorem14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every integer <math id="S4.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}^{k}g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C^{k+1}(k!)^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-k/2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}^{k}g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C^{k+1}(k!)^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-k/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a tensor-valued function <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, define the weighted Sobolev norm</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\coloneqq\sum_{j=0}^{N}\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\lVert D_{x}^{j}F\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\coloneqq\sum_{j=0}^{N}\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\lVert D_{x}^{j}F\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The weight ratio gives
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert D_{x}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}\leqslant N\eta^{-1/2}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert D_{x}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}\leqslant N\eta^{-1/2}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We next establish the
corresponding bound for <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leqslant j\leqslant N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leqslant j\leqslant N-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the
notation</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{contr}(D_{x}^{\ell}g_{\eta},D_{x}^{j-\ell}W)\coloneqq\operatorname{Sym}\Bigl(\sum_{a\in[d]}D_{x}^{\ell}(g_{\eta})_{a}\otimes D_{x}^{j-\ell}W_{a}\Bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>contr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>Sym</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{contr}(D_{x}^{\ell}g_{\eta},D_{x}^{j-\ell}W)\coloneqq\operatorname{Sym}\Bigl(\sum_{a\in[d]}D_{x}^{\ell}(g_{\eta})_{a}\otimes D_{x}^{j-\ell}W_{a}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">denotes contraction over the position index <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, followed by
normalized symmetrization over the <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> derivative indices. The
higher-order Leibniz rule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, Exercise 1.2.13]</cite> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x}^{j}(\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W)=\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{x}^{j}W)+\sum_{\ell=1}^{j}\binom{j}{\ell}\operatorname{contr}(D_{x}^{\ell}g_{\eta},D_{x}^{j-\ell}W)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>contr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x}^{j}(\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W)=\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{x}^{j}W)+\sum_{\ell=1}^{j}\binom{j}{\ell}\operatorname{contr}(D_{x}^{\ell}g_{\eta},D_{x}^{j-\ell}W)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 4.22 ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.22</span></a>), the weighted sum of the first terms is
bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{x}^{j}W)\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{x}^{j}W)\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\bigl(\lVert D_{x}^{j}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}+\lVert D_{x}^{j+1}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\bigl(\lVert D_{x}^{j}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}+\lVert D_{x}^{j+1}W\rVert_{L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2N}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2N}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">For the remaining terms, (<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>) implies</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert\operatorname{contr}(D_{x}^{\ell}g_{\eta},D_{x}^{j-\ell}W)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\ell!\,\eta^{-(\ell-1)/2}\,\lVert D_{x}^{j-\ell}W\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>contr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em">!</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\operatorname{contr}(D_{x}^{\ell}g_{\eta},D_{x}^{j-\ell}W)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\ell!\,\eta^{-(\ell-1)/2}\,\lVert D_{x}^{j-\ell}W\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Relative to the weight of <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x}^{j-\ell}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x}^{j-\ell}W</annotation></semantics></math>, the coefficient of the term
with <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> derivatives on <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\binom{j}{\ell}\,\ell!\,\eta^{-(\ell-1)/2}\bigg/\frac{\eta^{(j-\ell)/2}}{(j-\ell)!}=\sqrt{\eta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em">!</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\binom{j}{\ell}\,\ell!\,\eta^{-(\ell-1)/2}\bigg/\frac{\eta^{(j-\ell)/2}}{(j-\ell)!}=\sqrt{\eta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">After setting <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=j-\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=j-\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, each fixed position derivative <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x}^{s}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x}^{s}W</annotation></semantics></math>
appears for at most <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1-s\leqslant N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1-s\leqslant N</annotation></semantics></math> choices of <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the
commutator contribution is at most
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining the two contributions, using <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}\leqslant\frac{CN}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}\leqslant\frac{CN}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to control the Hamiltonian generator. One can check that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}F=\delta_{\gamma}(D_{x}F)-\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{p}F)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}F=\delta_{\gamma}(D_{x}F)-\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{p}F)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> has momentum
degree at most <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, the
Gaussian divergence estimate in (<a href="#S4.E23" title="Equation 4.23 ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.23</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\delta_{\gamma}(D_{x}F)\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\delta_{\gamma}(D_{x}F)\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{r+1}\,\lVert D_{x}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}\leqslant\frac{N\sqrt{r+1}}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{r+1}\,\lVert D_{x}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}\leqslant\frac{N\sqrt{r+1}}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text">For the second term, the Sobolev divergence estimate above and the Gaussian
gradient estimate in (<a href="#S4.E23" title="Equation 4.23 ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.23</span></a>) yield</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{p}F)\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{p}F)\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{CN}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert D_{p}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\leqslant\frac{CN\sqrt{r}}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{CN}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert D_{p}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\leqslant\frac{CN\sqrt{r}}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.11.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the last two displays proves</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}\leqslant\frac{CN\sqrt{r+1}}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,2}}\leqslant\frac{CN\sqrt{r+1}}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.12.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, integration by parts gives
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})}^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}\Delta V_{\eta}\leqslant d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})}^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}\Delta V_{\eta}\leqslant d</annotation></semantics></math>, while
(<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 4.7 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\leqslant\sqrt{d}+N\sqrt{\eta d}\leqslant(N+1)\sqrt{d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,2}}\leqslant\sqrt{d}+N\sqrt{\eta d}\leqslant(N+1)\sqrt{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.13.1" class="ltx_text">Since
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}^{j}g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}^{j}g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> has momentum degree at most <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, iterating the
bound (<a href="#S4.E25" title="Equation 4.25 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.25</span></a>) for <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0,\ldots,k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0,\ldots,k-1</annotation></semantics></math> produces
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k!\sqrt{k!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k!\sqrt{k!}</annotation></semantics></math>. The extra factor <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math> from the initialization is
absorbed into <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t},P_{t})_{t\geqslant 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t},P_{t})_{t\geqslant 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the exact Hamiltonian flow and put
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(X_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(X_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> when the initial state has law <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Invariance
and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem14" title="Lemma 4.14 (Stationary iterated derivatives in 𝐿^2). ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.14</span></a> give</p>
<table id="S4.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g^{(k)}(t)\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant C^{k+1}(k!)^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-k/2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g^{(k)}(t)\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant C^{k+1}(k!)^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-k/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.15</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discretization error bound)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\Bigl[B_{J,2}h\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}+\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{5}\Bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\Bigl[B_{J,2}h\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}+\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{5}\Bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem15.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem15.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here, one may take
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{J,2}=C_{0}^{J+1}\sqrt{J!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{J,2}=C_{0}^{J+1}\sqrt{J!}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is universal.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For an <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>-valued curve <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,h]</annotation></semantics></math>, write</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert f\rVert_{\infty,2}\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert f(t)\rVert_{L^{2}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert f\rVert_{\infty,2}\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert f(t)\rVert_{L^{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, we can identify the position coordinates <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{[0]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{[0]}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{[1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{[1]}</annotation></semantics></math> of the Hamiltonian flow and Picard iterations, respectively, as well as <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>-valued curves.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply the Banach-valued interpolation remainder in
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2 (Banach-valued interpolation error bound). ‣ B.2 Interpolation error bound ‣ Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> to the curve
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:[0,h]\to L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:[0,h]\to L^{2}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Together with
(<a href="#S4.E26" title="Equation 4.26 ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.26</span></a>), it gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{J,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{J,2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex79.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g(t)-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}g(t)\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\frac{h^{J}}{J!}\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g^{(J)}(t)\rVert_{L^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>J</mi></msup><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g(t)-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}g(t)\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\frac{h^{J}}{J!}\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g^{(J)}(t)\rVert_{L^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C^{J+1}\sqrt{J!}\,\sqrt{d}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\leqslant B_{J,2}\sqrt{d}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C^{J+1}\sqrt{J!}\,\sqrt{d}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\leqslant B_{J,2}\sqrt{d}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since
the exact flow is stationary under <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, integration by parts gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert g_{\eta}\circ X\rVert_{\infty,2}^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}\Delta V_{\eta}\leqslant d\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert g_{\eta}\circ X\rVert_{\infty,2}^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\eta}}\Delta V_{\eta}\leqslant d\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the integral equation for <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> shows that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert X^{[0]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}\leqslant\sqrt{d}\,\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert X^{[0]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}\leqslant\sqrt{d}\,\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">To control the first Picard iteration, insert the interpolant of the force along
the exact trajectory:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t}^{[1]}-X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t}^{[1]}-X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\bigl\{g_{\eta}(X_{s})-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[0]}](s)\bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\bigl\{g_{\eta}(X_{s})-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X^{[0]}](s)\bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\bigl\{g_{\eta}(X_{s})-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X](s)\bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}s+\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X-g_{\eta}\circ X^{[0]}](s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\bigl\{g_{\eta}(X_{s})-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X](s)\bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}s+\int_{0}^{t}(t-s)\,\mathcal{I}_{J,h}[g_{\eta}\circ X-g_{\eta}\circ X^{[0]}](s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz,
(<a href="#S4.E28" title="Equation 4.28 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.28</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert X^{[1]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert X^{[1]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\bigl\{\mathcal{E}_{J,2}+\Lambda_{J}\,\lVert X^{[0]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}\bigr\}\leqslant\frac{\mathcal{E}_{J,2}}{2}\,h^{2}+\frac{\Lambda_{J}\sqrt{d}}{4}\,h^{4}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\bigl\{\mathcal{E}_{J,2}+\Lambda_{J}\,\lVert X^{[0]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}\bigr\}\leqslant\frac{\mathcal{E}_{J,2}}{2}\,h^{2}+\frac{\Lambda_{J}\sqrt{d}}{4}\,h^{4}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{X}_{h},\widehat{P}_{h})\coloneqq(X_{h}^{[2]},P_{h}^{[2]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{X}_{h},\widehat{P}_{h})\coloneqq(X_{h}^{[2]},P_{h}^{[2]})</annotation></semantics></math>, the
Hamiltonian endpoint produced by the exact gradient numerical scheme. For
the momentum endpoint, insert the interpolant of the force along the exact
trajectory once more to obtain</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{P}_{h}-P_{h}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{J,2}\,h+\Lambda_{J}h\,\lVert X^{[1]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{P}_{h}-P_{h}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{J,2}\,h+\Lambda_{J}h\,\lVert X^{[1]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex85.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\Bigl(1+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)\,h\,\mathcal{E}_{J,2}+\frac{\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}}{4}\,h^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\Bigl(1+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)\,h\,\mathcal{E}_{J,2}+\frac{\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}}{4}\,h^{5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{J,2}\,h+C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,h^{5}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{J,2}\,h+C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,h^{5}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{X}_{h}-X_{h}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\mathcal{E}_{J,2}+\frac{\Lambda_{J}h^{2}}{2}\,\lVert X^{[1]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{X}_{h}-X_{h}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\mathcal{E}_{J,2}+\frac{\Lambda_{J}h^{2}}{2}\,\lVert X^{[1]}-X\rVert_{\infty,2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex87.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\Bigl(1+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)\,\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\mathcal{E}_{J,2}+\frac{\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}}{8}\,h^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\Bigl(1+\frac{h^{2}\Lambda_{J}}{2}\Bigr)\,\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\mathcal{E}_{J,2}+\frac{\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}}{8}\,h^{6}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{J,2}\,h^{2}+C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,h^{6}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{J,2}\,h^{2}+C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,h^{6}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">In the last lines, we used <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, start both the numerical phase and an exact Hamiltonian phase from
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and use the same Gaussian variables in the two OU refreshes.
The first refresh preserves <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the preceding stationary bounds
apply. The exact Hamiltonian flow and the final refresh also preserve
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the final refresh the common Gaussian increment cancels,
while the momentum difference is multiplied by <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-h/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-h/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,
using also <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows from <math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{J}\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{J}\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex89.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert\widehat{X}_{h}-X_{h}\rVert_{L^{2}}+\lVert\widehat{P}_{h}-P_{h}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{J,2}\,h+C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,h^{5}\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\Bigl[B_{J,2}h\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}+\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{5}\Bigr]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert\widehat{X}_{h}-X_{h}\rVert_{L^{2}}+\lVert\widehat{P}_{h}-P_{h}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant C\mathcal{E}_{J,2}\,h+C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,h^{5}\leqslant C\sqrt{d}\,\Bigl[B_{J,2}h\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}+\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{5}\Bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">This proves (<a href="#S4.E27" title="Equation 4.27 ‣ Proposition 4.15 (Discretization error bound). ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.27</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Proof of
<a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref">Theorem <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></span></a></h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We record the following standard initialization lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.16</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Initialization)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{0}\coloneqq\delta_{x_{\rm ref}}\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{0}\coloneqq\delta_{x_{\rm ref}}\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. For every
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q,M_{\kappa}}(\widehat{\mu}_{0},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa\,(d+q)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q,M_{\kappa}}(\widehat{\mu}_{0},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa\,(d+q)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> minimize <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. Strong monotonicity and the assumption
on <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert x_{\rm ref}-x_{\star}\rVert\leqslant\kappa\,\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\kappa d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x_{\rm ref}-x_{\star}\rVert\leqslant\kappa\,\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\kappa d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, concentration from strong log-concavity
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Chapter 5]</cite> and integration by parts give
<math id="S4.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert X-x_{\star}\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa\,(d+q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert X-x_{\star}\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa\,(d+q)}</annotation></semantics></math>. A draw from <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S4.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa\,(d+q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>G</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa\,(d+q)}</annotation></semantics></math> because
<math id="S4.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leqslant 1\leqslant\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leqslant 1\leqslant\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. Coupling the initial and stationary momenta
identically, the claim follows from the triangle inequality and <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\kappa}\preceq CI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\kappa}\preceq CI</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma handles the terminal step.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.17</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Terminal RGO step in <math id="S4.Thmtheorem17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>. For every
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta}(y,\mathrm{d}x)\coloneqq R_{\eta,y}(\mathrm{d}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta}(y,\mathrm{d}x)\coloneqq R_{\eta,y}(\mathrm{d}x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for every
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y,y^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y,y^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(R_{\eta,y},R_{\eta,y^{\prime}})\leqslant\frac{\kappa}{\kappa+\eta}\,\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(R_{\eta,y},R_{\eta,y^{\prime}})\leqslant\frac{\kappa}{\kappa+\eta}\,\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\leqslant\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}R_{\eta}=\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}R_{\eta}=\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, for any center laws
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\mu R_{\eta},\mu^{\prime}R_{\eta})\leqslant W_{2}(\mu,\mu^{\prime})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\mu R_{\eta},\mu^{\prime}R_{\eta})\leqslant W_{2}(\mu,\mu^{\prime})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">These are the standard invariance and contraction properties of the
restricted Gaussian oracle; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> is completed by
plugging the bias, variance, and
discretization error bounds from <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> into
(<a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 4.12 ‣ Theorem 4.5 (Local error analysis in 𝑊_2). ‣ 4.2 Local error analysis ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>) and performing some bookkeeping.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout, we assume access to exact proximal queries; this assumption can be removed via the arguments in in <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>. After the change of variables <math id="S4.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\sqrt{\beta}\,x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>β</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\sqrt{\beta}\,x</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to work
under <math id="S4.SS5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math> and prove <math id="S4.SS5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\leqslant\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\leqslant\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex94.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\log\frac{C\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\,,\qquad J\coloneqq\lceil C\mathfrak{L}^{2}\rceil\,,\qquad h\coloneqq\frac{c}{\mathfrak{L}}\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{\kappa},\frac{\varepsilon^{1/3}}{\kappa^{1/6}d^{1/6}}\Bigr\}\,,\qquad N\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil\frac{C\kappa\mathfrak{L}}{h}\Bigr\rceil\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>𝔏</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\log\frac{C\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\,,\qquad J\coloneqq\lceil C\mathfrak{L}^{2}\rceil\,,\qquad h\coloneqq\frac{c}{\mathfrak{L}}\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{\kappa},\frac{\varepsilon^{1/3}}{\kappa^{1/6}d^{1/6}}\Bigr\}\,,\qquad N\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil\frac{C\kappa\mathfrak{L}}{h}\Bigr\rceil\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are universal constants; the following assertions hold after adjusting these constants appropriately.
Here, <math id="S4.SS5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is introduced to streamline the bookkeeping of logarithmic terms.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
to be chosen below, and choose <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> so that
<math id="S4.SS5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}/\eta=\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}/\eta=\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
The explicit choice of <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{J,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{J,2}</annotation></semantics></math> in
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem15" title="Proposition 4.15 (Discretization error bound). ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.15</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{J,2}\theta^{J/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{J,2}\theta^{J/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{0}^{J+1}\sqrt{J!}\,\theta^{J/2}\leqslant C_{0}^{J+1}(J\theta)^{J/2}\leqslant e^{-c_{1}J}\leqslant h^{4}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{0}^{J+1}\sqrt{J!}\,\theta^{J/2}\leqslant C_{0}^{J+1}(J\theta)^{J/2}\leqslant e^{-c_{1}J}\leqslant h^{4}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">provided that <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leqslant c\mathfrak{L}^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leqslant c\mathfrak{L}^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We henceforth choose <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\coloneqq c/\mathfrak{L}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\coloneqq c/\mathfrak{L}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS5.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leqslant c/(\kappa\log J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leqslant c/(\kappa\log J)</annotation></semantics></math>,
so the restrictions in
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem15" title="Proposition 4.15 (Discretization error bound). ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Propositions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.15</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 4.7 (Contraction). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>
hold, and moreover <math id="S4.SS5.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take square roots in (<a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 4.12 ‣ Theorem 4.5 (Local error analysis in 𝑊_2). ‣ 4.2 Local error analysis ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>) and substitute
the local bounds from
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem13" title="Proposition 4.13 (Variance bound). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Propositions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.13</span></a>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 4.9 (Bias bound). ‣ 4.4.1 Bias bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem15" title="Proposition 4.15 (Discretization error bound). ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.15</span></a>.
Together with <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 4.16 (Initialization). ‣ 4.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.16</span></a>, this gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}^{\rm ph},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi><mi>ph</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}^{\rm ph},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex95.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle C\sqrt{\kappa d}\,e^{-cNh/\kappa}+C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{\kappa d}\,(\eta h+\eta^{1/2}h^{5/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msqrt><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C\sqrt{\kappa d}\,e^{-cNh/\kappa}+C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{\kappa d}\,(\eta h+\eta^{1/2}h^{5/2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad{}+C\kappa\sqrt{d}\,(\eta^{3/2}+\Lambda_{J}\eta^{1/2}h^{2}+\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{4})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad{}+C\kappa\sqrt{d}\,(\eta^{3/2}+\Lambda_{J}\eta^{1/2}h^{2}+\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{4})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{N}^{\rm ph}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi><mi>ph</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{N}^{\rm ph}</annotation></semantics></math> is the final phase-space law. The Picard iteration error
term is included in the last monomial by
(<a href="#S4.E29" title="Equation 4.29 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 4.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.29</span></a>). Since
<math id="S4.SS5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{J}\leqslant C\log\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{J}\leqslant C\log\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, the preceding bounds on
<math id="S4.SS5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h,\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h,\eta</annotation></semantics></math> show that the sum of the last five terms can is at most <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon/4</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> appropriately small.
This bookkeeping is uniform over <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>. The definition of <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> makes the initial
term at most <math id="S4.SS5.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon/4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem17" title="Lemma 4.17 (Terminal RGO step in 𝑊_2). ‣ 4.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.17</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}R_{\eta},\pi)=W_{2}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}R_{\eta},\pi_{\eta}R_{\eta})\leqslant W_{2}(\widehat{\mu}_{N},\pi_{\eta})\leqslant CW_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}^{\rm ph},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant\frac{\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon}{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi><mi>ph</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}R_{\eta},\pi)=W_{2}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}R_{\eta},\pi_{\eta}R_{\eta})\leqslant W_{2}(\widehat{\mu}_{N},\pi_{\eta})\leqslant CW_{2,M_{\kappa}}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}^{\rm ph},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant\frac{\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon}{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">after adjusting universal constants. Let <math id="S4.SS5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the
conditional output law of the terminal FORS routine in
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Algorithm 3.2 (Smoothed Picard HMC with a terminal FORS step). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, and set</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\rm term}\coloneqq\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2},\frac{\kappa\varepsilon^{2}}{8\eta}\Bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>term</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\rm term}\coloneqq\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2},\frac{\kappa\varepsilon^{2}}{8\eta}\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> with <math id="S4.SS5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=2</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS5.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{2}\coloneqq\min\{1/4,\delta_{\rm term}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>term</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{2}\coloneqq\min\{1/4,\delta_{\rm term}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, uniformly in <math id="S4.SS5.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,
we can ensure that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(\widehat{R}_{\eta,y}\mathbin{\|}R_{\eta,y})\leqslant\mathsf{R}_{2}(\widehat{R}_{\eta,y}\mathbin{\|}R_{\eta,y})\leqslant\delta_{\rm term}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>term</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(\widehat{R}_{\eta,y}\mathbin{\|}R_{\eta,y})\leqslant\mathsf{R}_{2}(\widehat{R}_{\eta,y}\mathbin{\|}R_{\eta,y})\leqslant\delta_{\rm term}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">The RGO potential is
<math id="S4.SS5.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly convex.
Talagrand’s inequality therefore gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}^{2}(\widehat{R}_{\eta,y},R_{\eta,y})\leqslant\frac{2\delta_{\rm term}}{\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1}}\leqslant 2\eta\delta_{\rm term}\leqslant\frac{\kappa\varepsilon^{2}}{4}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>term</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>term</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}^{2}(\widehat{R}_{\eta,y},R_{\eta,y})\leqslant\frac{2\delta_{\rm term}}{\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1}}\leqslant 2\eta\delta_{\rm term}\leqslant\frac{\kappa\varepsilon^{2}}{4}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">The triangle inequality then yields
<math id="S4.SS5.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}\widehat{R}_{\eta},\pi)\leqslant\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\widehat{\mu}_{N}\widehat{R}_{\eta},\pi)\leqslant\sqrt{\kappa}\,\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each phase uses <math id="S4.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2J</annotation></semantics></math> gradients and <math id="S4.SS5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2J</annotation></semantics></math> proximal calls. Substitution
of <math id="S4.SS5.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2JN\leqslant C\,\Bigl\{\kappa^{2}+\frac{\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}}{\varepsilon^{1/3}}\Bigr\}\,\mathfrak{L}^{4}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2JN\leqslant C\,\Bigl\{\kappa^{2}+\frac{\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}}{\varepsilon^{1/3}}\Bigr\}\,\mathfrak{L}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">calls of each type. By <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, the terminal routine
has expected cost at most <math id="S4.SS5.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\mathfrak{L}^{5/3}\,(1+\varepsilon^{4/9}d^{1/9}/\kappa^{2/9})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\mathfrak{L}^{5/3}\,(1+\varepsilon^{4/9}d^{1/9}/\kappa^{2/9})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Any fixed power of
<math id="S4.SS5.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is dominated by a positive power of
<math id="S4.SS5.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa d/\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa d/\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence this cost is dominated by the Picard
HMC bound for <math id="S4.SS5.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa,d\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa,d\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS5.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves the theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span><math id="S5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> analysis</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our warm start application, we need to upgrade the <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee to a <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee, for <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
We organize the proof in parallel with <a href="#S4" title="4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, and along the way, we describe the new ingredients needed for this part of the analysis.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span><math id="S5.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee</h3>

<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix any <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. There is a constant <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=C(c_{0})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=C(c_{0})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with the following
property. Suppose
<math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I\,,\qquad\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/\kappa}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I\,,\qquad\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/\kappa}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, put</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}_{q}\coloneqq q+\log\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}_{q}\coloneqq q+\log\frac{e\kappa d}{\varepsilon}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, there is a smoothing variance <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for which a gradient-only
implementation of Picard HMC returns a sample whose output law <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}(\widehat{\pi}_{\eta},\pi_{\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}(\widehat{\pi}_{\eta},\pi_{\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Its expected number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\,\Bigl\{\kappa^{2}+\frac{\kappa^{4/3}\,(d+q)^{1/6}}{\varepsilon^{1/3}}\Bigr\}\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{6}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>6</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\,\Bigl\{\kappa^{2}+\frac{\kappa^{4/3}\,(d+q)^{1/6}}{\varepsilon^{1/3}}\Bigr\}\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{6}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that unlike <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, this guarantee targets the smoothed distribution <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>; that is, we omit the terminal FORS step.
This is because the terminal FORS guarantee does not immediately hold in <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>; moreover, the guarantee for sampling from <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> will be enough for our eventual warm start application.
Indeed, the guarantee is intended to implement the smooth sampler <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a> in <a href="#S6" title="6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span><math id="S5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> local error analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> proof, the local error framework (<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4.4 (Local error framework). ‣ 4.2 Local error analysis ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) separates a weak error from a
strong error by expanding a square. For <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>, we replace
it with the following smoothness inequality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> smoothness)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a centered random vector in a Hilbert space and
<math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic, then</span></p>
<table id="S5.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{E}\lVert a+Z\rVert^{q})^{2/q}\leqslant\lVert a\rVert^{2}+(q-1)\,(\mathbb{E}\lVert Z\rVert^{q})^{2/q}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{E}\lVert a+Z\rVert^{q})^{2/q}\leqslant\lVert a\rVert^{2}+(q-1)\,(\mathbb{E}\lVert Z\rVert^{q})^{2/q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This follows from the smoothness of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>. It also
follows directly by differentiating
<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto(\mathbb{E}\lVert a+tZ\rVert^{q})^{2/q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto(\mathbb{E}\lVert a+tZ\rVert^{q})^{2/q}</annotation></semantics></math>: centeredness gives zero derivative at
the origin and Hölder’s inequality bounds the second derivative by
<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\,(q-1)\,\lVert Z\rVert_{L^{q}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\,(q-1)\,\lVert Z\rVert_{L^{q}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local error framework in <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,\widehat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,\widehat{P}</annotation></semantics></math> be Markov kernels on <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose that, for every <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a coupling
<math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\delta_{x}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\delta_{x}P</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim\delta_{y}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim\delta_{y}P</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathbb{E}(X-Y)\rVert\leqslant\rho\,\lVert x-y\rVert\,,\qquad\lVert(X-Y)-\mathbb{E}(X-Y)\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant\chi_{q}\,\lVert x-y\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathbb{E}(X-Y)\rVert\leqslant\rho\,\lVert x-y\rVert\,,\qquad\lVert(X-Y)-\mathbb{E}(X-Y)\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant\chi_{q}\,\lVert x-y\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose also that, writing <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{X}\sim\delta_{x}\widehat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{X}\sim\delta_{x}\widehat{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\delta_{x}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\delta_{x}P</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}(\delta_{x}\widehat{P},\delta_{x}P)\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\,,\qquad\lVert\mathbb{E}\widehat{X}-\mathbb{E}X\rVert\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}(\delta_{x}\widehat{P},\delta_{x}P)\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\,,\qquad\lVert\mathbb{E}\widehat{X}-\mathbb{E}X\rVert\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\rho&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\rho&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\,(q-1)\,\chi_{q}^{2}\leqslant\rho\,(1-\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>χ</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\,(q-1)\,\chi_{q}^{2}\leqslant\rho\,(1-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for all probability laws <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}^{2}(\mu\widehat{P},\nu P)\leqslant\rho W_{q}^{2}(\mu,\nu)+\frac{16\,(q-1)}{1+\rho}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}+\frac{2}{1-\rho}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}^{2}(\mu\widehat{P},\nu P)\leqslant\rho W_{q}^{2}(\mu,\nu)+\frac{16\,(q-1)}{1+\rho}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}+\frac{2}{1-\rho}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z,Z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z,Z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> coupling of <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. Given
<math id="S5.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z,Z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z,Z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{X}\sim\widehat{P}(Z,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{X}\sim\widehat{P}(Z,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim P(Z,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim P(Z,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> be optimally coupled in <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim P(Z^{\prime},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim P(Z^{\prime},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> be coupled to <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> via the coupling in the theorem statement.
Write <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\coloneqq\widehat{X}-X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\coloneqq\widehat{X}-X</annotation></semantics></math>.
Conditionally on <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z,Z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z,Z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, Jensen’s inequality gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\,,\qquad\lVert\Delta-\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}\leqslant 2\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\,,\qquad\lVert\Delta-\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}\leqslant 2\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Minkowski’s inequality and Young’s inequality, for <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{X}-Y\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{X}-Y\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant(1+\lambda)\,\lVert\Delta-\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]+X-Y\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}+(1+\lambda^{-1})\,\lVert\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant(1+\lambda)\,\lVert\Delta-\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]+X-Y\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}+(1+\lambda^{-1})\,\lVert\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">For the first term, by (<a href="#S5.E1" title="Equation 5.1 ‣ Lemma 5.2 (𝐿^𝑞 smoothness). ‣ 5.2 𝑊_𝑞 local error analysis ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\Delta-\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]+X-Y\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\Delta-\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]+X-Y\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leqslant\lVert\mathbb{E}[X-Y\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert^{2}+(q-1)\,\lVert\Delta-\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]+X-Y-\mathbb{E}[X-Y\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leqslant\lVert\mathbb{E}[X-Y\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert^{2}+(q-1)\,\lVert\Delta-\mathbb{E}[\Delta\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]+X-Y-\mathbb{E}[X-Y\mid Z,Z^{\prime}]\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leqslant\rho^{2}\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert^{2}+(q-1)\,\bigl(2\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}+\chi_{q}\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert\bigr)^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leqslant\rho^{2}\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert^{2}+(q-1)\,\bigl(2\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}+\chi_{q}\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert\bigr)^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u+v)^{2}\leqslant 2u^{2}+2v^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u+v)^{2}\leqslant 2u^{2}+2v^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the assumption on <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, the
right-hand side is at most</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\rho\,(1+\rho)}{2}\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert^{2}+8\,(q-1)\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\rho\,(1+\rho)}{2}\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert^{2}+8\,(q-1)\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Take the <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q/2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm over <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z,Z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z,Z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, choosing <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\frac{1-\rho}{1+\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\frac{1-\rho}{1+\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{X}-Y\rVert_{L^{q}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{X}-Y\rVert_{L^{q}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigl\lVert\lVert\widehat{X}-Y\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}\bigr\rVert_{L^{q/2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigl\lVert\lVert\widehat{X}-Y\rVert_{L^{q}\mid Z,Z^{\prime}}^{2}\bigr\rVert_{L^{q/2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\Bigl\lVert(1+\lambda)\,\Bigl(\frac{\rho\,(1+\rho)}{2}\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert^{2}+8\,(q-1)\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}\Bigr)+(1+\lambda^{-1})\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}^{2}\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q/2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⩽</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\Bigl\lVert(1+\lambda)\,\Bigl(\frac{\rho\,(1+\rho)}{2}\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert^{2}+8\,(q-1)\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}\Bigr)+(1+\lambda^{-1})\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}^{2}\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q/2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\rho\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert_{L^{q}}^{2}+\frac{16\,(q-1)}{1+\rho}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}+\frac{2}{1-\rho}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}^{2}\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\rho\,\lVert Z-Z^{\prime}\rVert_{L^{q}}^{2}+\frac{16\,(q-1)}{1+\rho}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}^{2}+\frac{2}{1-\rho}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}^{2}\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the kernels
<math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. For
<math id="S5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, define the centered variance and bias errors</p>
<table id="S5.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>var</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}W_{q}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K},\delta_{z}\bar{K})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}W_{q}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K},\delta_{z}\bar{K})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z,\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\,\lVert\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{z,\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}}\,\lVert\bar{\Phi}_{z}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z}(\zeta)\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Take <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P}\coloneqq\widehat{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P}\coloneqq\widehat{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\coloneqq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\coloneqq K</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of
<math id="S5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>, the laws <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}\widehat{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}\widehat{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}\bar{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}\bar{K}</annotation></semantics></math> have the same mean. The triangle inequality yields</p>
<table id="S5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\,,\qquad\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>strong</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>var</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>weak</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\rm strong}\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\,,\qquad\mathcal{E}_{\rm weak}\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Also, define</p>
<table id="S5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}\coloneqq W_{q}(\Pi_{\eta}K,\Pi_{\eta})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>disc</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}\coloneqq W_{q}(\Pi_{\eta}K,\Pi_{\eta})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">The analogue of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 4.5 (Local error analysis in 𝑊_2). ‣ 4.2 Local error analysis ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a> is the
following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local error analysis in <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leqslant c/(\kappa\,(q+\log J))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leqslant c/(\kappa\,(q+\log J))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for every phase-space law <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant(1-ch/\kappa)\,W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+Cq\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa}{h}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}^{2})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>var</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>disc</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant(1-ch/\kappa)\,W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+Cq\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa}{h}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}^{2})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K}^{N},\Pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}\widehat{K}^{N},\Pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant e^{-cNh/\kappa}\,W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+\frac{C\kappa q}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa^{2}}{h^{2}}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}^{2})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>var</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>disc</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant e^{-cNh/\kappa}\,W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+\frac{C\kappa q}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa^{2}}{h^{2}}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}^{2})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Repeat the proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 4.5 (Local error analysis in 𝑊_2). ‣ 4.2 Local error analysis ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>, using
<a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3 (Local error framework in 𝑊_𝑞). ‣ 5.2 𝑊_𝑞 local error analysis ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> in place of the <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
local error framework; <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 4.7 (Contraction). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Propositions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 4.8 (Synchronous increment coupling). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>
still apply and give <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1-ch/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1-ch/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{q}\leqslant 2Ch" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{q}\leqslant 2Ch</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span><math id="S5.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> local error bounds</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bias term <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as before, and is controlled by <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 4.9 (Bias bound). ‣ 4.4.1 Bias bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>.
Thus, we focus on controlling the other two terms.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.3.1 </span>Variance bound</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the variance bound, we must extend the second-order <math id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> estimate in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> to <math id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.5</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Second-order <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> estimate)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the setting of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>, for all <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}\bigl(\law\{L(Z+f(Z,G))\}\,,\law\{L(Z+\bar{f}(Z))\}\bigr)\leqslant C\sqrt{m}\,\bigl(\sqrt{q}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+q^{2}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}\bigl(\law\{L(Z+f(Z,G))\}\,,\law\{L(Z+\bar{f}(Z))\}\bigr)\leqslant C\sqrt{m}\,\bigl(\sqrt{q}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+q^{2}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof, which is given in <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Proofs of the second-order Wasserstein estimates ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, relies on the same strategy as <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>, but relies on a more involved Gaussian divergence inequality (<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma C.3 (Gaussian Sobolev inequalities). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>).
Using this, we can control the variance term in <math id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5.6</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance bound in <math id="S5.Thmtheorem6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,\bigl(\eta h^{3/2}q^{1/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3}q^{2}\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>var</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}^{2}\sqrt{d}\,\bigl(\eta h^{3/2}q^{1/2}+\eta^{1/2}h^{3}q^{2}\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5.5 (Second-order 𝑊_𝑞 estimate). ‣ 5.3.1 Variance bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a> with the constants in
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma 4.10 (Lipschitz bounds). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.3.2 </span>Discretization error bound</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we need to replace the <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> bound (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 4.22 ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.22</span></a>) with an <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> version.
The following lemma reduces this to an <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> bound for the Gaussian divergence operator, which in turn is handled in <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma C.3 (Gaussian Sobolev inequalities). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.7</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Divergence bound)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> be independent, and set <math id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\coloneqq X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\coloneqq X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G</annotation></semantics></math>. For a smooth
tensor-valued position vector field <math id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=(W_{i})_{i\in[d]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=(W_{i})_{i\in[d]}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the representation</span></p>
<table id="S5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W(Y,P)=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\eta^{-1/2}\,\delta_{\gamma}\{W(X+\sqrt{\eta}\,\cdot,P)\}(G)\bigm|Y,P\bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W(Y,P)=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\eta^{-1/2}\,\delta_{\gamma}\{W(X+\sqrt{\eta}\,\cdot,P)\}(G)\bigm|Y,P\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, for every <math id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C\sqrt{q/\eta}\,\lVert W\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}+Cq^{2}\,\lVert DW\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C\sqrt{q/\eta}\,\lVert W\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}+Cq^{2}\,\lVert DW\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The constant is independent of all tensor dimensions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The identity in (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) is equivalent to <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{\eta}(Y)=\eta^{-1/2}\,\mathbb{E}[G\mid Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}(Y)=\eta^{-1/2}\,\mathbb{E}[G\mid Y]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Gaussian divergence gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{\gamma}\{W(X+\sqrt{\eta}\,\cdot,P)\}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{\gamma}\{W(X+\sqrt{\eta}\,\cdot,P)\}(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle G,W(Y,P)\rangle-\eta^{1/2}\operatorname{div}_{x}W(Y,P)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle G,W(Y,P)\rangle-\eta^{1/2}\operatorname{div}_{x}W(Y,P)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{div}_{x}W\coloneqq\sum_{i\in[d]}\partial_{x_{i}}W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>div</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{div}_{x}W\coloneqq\sum_{i\in[d]}\partial_{x_{i}}W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the divergence in the position argument; the <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> factor comes from the chain rule.
Conditioning on <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,P)</annotation></semantics></math> proves
(<a href="#S5.E5" title="Equation 5.5 ‣ Lemma 5.7 (Divergence bound). ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>). Conditional expectation is an
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction. Apply Jensen’s inequality and (<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.3 (Gaussian Sobolev inequalities). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>) to obtain (<a href="#S5.E6" title="Equation 5.6 ‣ Lemma 5.7 (Divergence bound). ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.8</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stationary iterated derivatives in <math id="S5.Thmtheorem8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}^{k}g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C^{k+1}q^{2k}\,(k!)^{2}\,\sqrt{d+q}\,\eta^{-k/2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}^{k}g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C^{k+1}q^{2k}\,(k!)^{2}\,\sqrt{d+q}\,\eta^{-k/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a tensor-valued <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, define the weighted Sobolev norm</span></p>
<table id="S5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,q}}\coloneqq\sum_{j=0}^{N}\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\lVert D_{x}^{j}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,q}}\coloneqq\sum_{j=0}^{N}\frac{\eta^{j/2}}{j!}\,\lVert D_{x}^{j}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta};\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Tracing through the proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem14" title="Lemma 4.14 (Stationary iterated derivatives in 𝐿^2). ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.14</span></a>, but using (<a href="#S5.E6" title="Equation 5.6 ‣ Lemma 5.7 (Divergence bound). ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>) in place of (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 4.22 ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.22</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,q}}\leqslant\frac{Cq^{2}N}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,q}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,q}}\leqslant\frac{Cq^{2}N}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert W\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,q}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the factorization <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}F=\delta_{\gamma}(D_{x}F)-\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{p}F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}F=\delta_{\gamma}(D_{x}F)-\delta_{\pi_{\eta}}(D_{p}F)</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S4.E24" title="Equation 4.24 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.24</span></a>). If <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is polynomial of
degree at most <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma C.8 (𝐿^𝑞 Gaussian polynomial estimates). ‣ C.4 Gaussian polynomial bounds ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>, (<a href="#S5.E8" title="Equation 5.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a>), and
(<a href="#S5.E9" title="Equation 5.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a>) yield the
dimension-free bound</span></p>
<table id="S5.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,q}}\leqslant\frac{CN\,(\sqrt{q}+q^{2}r)}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,q}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N-1,q}}\leqslant\frac{CN\,(\sqrt{q}+q^{2}r)}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,q}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to initialize the induction.
From <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Lemma 6.2.7]</cite>, we have <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{q}(\pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C\sqrt{d+q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{q}(\pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C\sqrt{d+q}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the uniform
bound (<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 4.7 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>) and the weights in
(<a href="#S5.E8" title="Equation 5.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,q}}\leqslant C(N+1)\sqrt{d+q}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝖶</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{\mathsf{W}^{N,q}}\leqslant C(N+1)\sqrt{d+q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}^{j}g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{H}}^{j}g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is polynomial of degree at most <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> in
momentum. Apply (<a href="#S5.E10" title="Equation 5.10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.10</span></a>) <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> times, starting at <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=k</annotation></semantics></math> and
using <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=j</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{q}+q^{2}j\leqslant q^{2}\,(j+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{q}+q^{2}j\leqslant q^{2}\,(j+1)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, the product of the
one-step factors is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}[(k-j)\,(\sqrt{q}+q^{2}j)]\leqslant q^{2k}\,(k!)^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}[(k-j)\,(\sqrt{q}+q^{2}j)]\leqslant q^{2k}\,(k!)^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the initialization factor satisfies <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1\leqslant 2^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1\leqslant 2^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and
can therefore be absorbed into <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>; the case <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> follows
directly from the initialization bound. This proves
(<a href="#S5.E7" title="Equation 5.7 ‣ Lemma 5.8 (Stationary iterated derivatives in 𝐿^𝑞). ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5.9</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Discretization error bound)<span id="S5.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, then, for every <math id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}\leqslant C\sqrt{d+q}\,\Bigl[B_{J,q}h\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}+\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{5}\Bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>disc</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}\leqslant C\sqrt{d+q}\,\Bigl[B_{J,q}h\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}+\Lambda_{J}^{2}h^{5}\Bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here, one may take
<math id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{J,q}=C_{0}^{J+1}q^{2J}J!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{J,q}=C_{0}^{J+1}q^{2J}J!</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is universal.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Repeat the proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem15" title="Proposition 4.15 (Discretization error bound). ‣ 4.4.3 Discretization error bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.15</span></a> with
the uniform-in-time <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> norm in place of the uniform-in-time <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
norm. The interpolation estimate is replaced by</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{J,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{J,q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g(t)-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}g(t)\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant\frac{h^{J}}{J!}\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g^{(J)}(t)\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C^{J+1}q^{2J}J!\sqrt{d+q}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>J</mi></msup><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g(t)-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}g(t)\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant\frac{h^{J}}{J!}\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g^{(J)}(t)\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C^{J+1}q^{2J}J!\sqrt{d+q}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Also, stationarity and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Lemma 6.2.7]</cite> give</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g_{\eta}(X_{t})\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}=\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{q}(\pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C\sqrt{d+q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g_{\eta}(X_{t})\rVert_{L^{q}(\Pi_{\eta})}=\lVert g_{\eta}\rVert_{L^{q}(\pi_{\eta})}\leqslant C\sqrt{d+q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">in place of the corresponding <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> bound by <math id="S5.SS3.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Proof of
<a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (𝑊_𝑞 guarantee). ‣ 5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref">Theorem <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></span></a></h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (𝑊_𝑞 guarantee). ‣ 5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first assume exact proximal queries. The modifications needed to remove
proximal access are deferred to <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> be as in
the theorem. Choose</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\coloneqq c\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{-3}\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{\kappa},\Bigl(\frac{\varepsilon}{\kappa\sqrt{d+q}}\Bigr)^{1/3}\Bigr\}\,,\qquad\eta\coloneqq C_{\eta}\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{6}h^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>6</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\coloneqq c\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{-3}\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{\kappa},\Bigl(\frac{\varepsilon}{\kappa\sqrt{d+q}}\Bigr)^{1/3}\Bigr\}\,,\qquad\eta\coloneqq C_{\eta}\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{6}h^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\eta}\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\eta}\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> is universal and <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> will be chosen
sufficiently small. Set</span></p>
<table id="S5.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\coloneqq\lceil C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\rceil\,,\qquad N\coloneqq\lceil C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}/h\rceil\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\coloneqq\lceil C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\rceil\,,\qquad N\coloneqq\lceil C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}/h\rceil\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">With appropriately large <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and small <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, the definitions
give</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-C\mathfrak{L}_{q}}\leqslant h\leqslant\frac{c}{\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{3}}\,,\qquad h\mathfrak{L}_{q}\leqslant\frac{c}{\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}}\leqslant\frac{c}{\kappa}\,,\qquad\eta\leqslant\frac{C_{\eta}c^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\leqslant\min\{c_{0},1/2\}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-C\mathfrak{L}_{q}}\leqslant h\leqslant\frac{c}{\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{3}}\,,\qquad h\mathfrak{L}_{q}\leqslant\frac{c}{\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}}\leqslant\frac{c}{\kappa}\,,\qquad\eta\leqslant\frac{C_{\eta}c^{2}}{\kappa^{2}}\leqslant\min\{c_{0},1/2\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(h^{-1})\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(h^{-1})\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since
<math id="S5.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{J,q}=C_{0}^{J+1}q^{2J}J!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{J,q}=C_{0}^{J+1}q^{2J}J!</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{J,q}C_{\eta}^{-J/2}\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{-3J}\leqslant e^{-cJ}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝔏</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{J,q}C_{\eta}^{-J/2}\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{-3J}\leqslant e^{-cJ}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">A sufficiently large <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> therefore gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{J,q}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\leqslant h^{4}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{J,q}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\leqslant h^{4}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Tedious bookkeeping shows that</span></p>
<table id="S5.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q,M_{\kappa}}(\widehat{\mu}_{N},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{9}\kappa\sqrt{d+q}\,h^{3}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>9</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q,M_{\kappa}}(\widehat{\mu}_{N},\Pi_{\eta})\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{9}\kappa\sqrt{d+q}\,h^{3}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Each phase makes <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2J</annotation></semantics></math> gradient queries and
<math id="S5.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2J</annotation></semantics></math> exact proximal queries. Since
<math id="S5.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leqslant C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}/h+1\leqslant C^{\prime}\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}/h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leqslant C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}/h+1\leqslant C^{\prime}\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}/h</annotation></semantics></math>, the numbers of direct gradient queries
and exact proximal queries are each at most
<math id="S5.SS4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}/h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}/h</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking position marginals in
(<a href="#S5.E13" title="Equation 5.13 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 5.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.13</span></a>) and
the definition of <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}(\widehat{\pi}_{\eta},\pi_{\eta})\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{9}\kappa\sqrt{d+q}\,h^{3}\leqslant\varepsilon\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>9</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}(\widehat{\pi}_{\eta},\pi_{\eta})\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{9}\kappa\sqrt{d+q}\,h^{3}\leqslant\varepsilon\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">The modifications in <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> remove the proximal
queries altogether with expected gradient cost at most
<math id="S5.SS4.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{3}/h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{3}/h</annotation></semantics></math>. Substitution of <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> gives the query
bound in the theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Recursive warm start generator</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we describe the recursive warm start generator and its guarantee.
See <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> for the algorithm and an overview.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Main result</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For probability laws <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the sub-Gaussian
Orlicz–Wasserstein distance</p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\psi_{2}}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{(X,Y)}\inf\Bigl\{\varepsilon&gt;0:\mathbb{E}\exp\Bigl(\frac{\lVert X-Y\rVert^{2}}{\varepsilon^{2}}\Bigr)\leqslant 2\Bigr\}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\psi_{2}}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{(X,Y)}\inf\Bigl\{\varepsilon&gt;0:\mathbb{E}\exp\Bigl(\frac{\lVert X-Y\rVert^{2}}{\varepsilon^{2}}\Bigr)\leqslant 2\Bigr\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the outer infimum ranges over all couplings of <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The recursive warm start generator assumes access to a smoothed sampler as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumptionx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumptionx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption</span></span><span id="Thmassumptionx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothed sampler)<span id="Thmassumptionx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumptionx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a sampler <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math> which, provided any normalized potential <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{U}^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}U\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{U}^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}U\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>,
and an admissible reference point <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla U(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/\kappa_{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla U(x_{\rm ref})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/\kappa_{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>, implements one of the interfaces below. Here,
<math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{U,\eta}\coloneqq\pi_{U}*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{U,\eta}\coloneqq\pi_{U}*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the smoothed distribution.</p>
<ol id="S6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.8em;">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S6.I1.i1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠𝟣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A1}</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the sampler returns
<math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a sample
with law <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\,W_{2}(\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta},\pi_{U,\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\,W_{2}(\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta},\pi_{U,\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">using at most <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{C}_{2}(\kappa_{U},d,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{C}_{2}(\kappa_{U},d,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> expected gradient queries.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S6.I1.i2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠𝟤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A2}</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it returns <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a
sample with law <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\,W_{p}(\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta},\pi_{U,\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\,W_{p}(\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta},\pi_{U,\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">using at most <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{C}_{p}(\kappa_{U},d,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{C}_{p}(\kappa_{U},d,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> expected gradient queries.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S6.I1.i3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠𝟥</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A3}</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it returns <math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a sample with law
<math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\,W_{\psi_{2}}(\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta},\pi_{U,\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\,W_{\psi_{2}}(\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta},\pi_{U,\eta})\leqslant\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">using at most <math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{C}_{\psi_{2}}(\kappa_{U},d,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{C}_{\psi_{2}}(\kappa_{U},d,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> expected gradient
queries.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Assume that each complexity function is non-decreasing in its condition number
argument and non-increasing in its accuracy argument, and that
<math id="Thmassumptionx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\mapsto\mathsf{C}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\mapsto\mathsf{C}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We will apply this interface directly to potentials whose smoothness is not normalized to
<math id="S6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Concretely, if
<math id="S6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{U}I\preceq\nabla^{2}U\preceq\beta_{U}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{U}I\preceq\nabla^{2}U\preceq\beta_{U}I</annotation></semantics></math>, apply <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to
the normalized potential <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U(\cdot/\sqrt{\beta_{U}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(\cdot/\sqrt{\beta_{U}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and then divide
its output by <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\beta_{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\beta_{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalized smoothing level, then the law of the rescaled output
approximates <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{U}*\mathsf{N}(0,\beta_{U}^{-1}\eta I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{U}*\mathsf{N}(0,\beta_{U}^{-1}\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding scale-invariant guarantee is
<math id="S6.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha_{U}}\,W_{\bullet}\leqslant\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha_{U}}\,W_{\bullet}\leqslant\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, and the query cost is unchanged.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S4" title="4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#S5" title="5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we have shown that Picard HMC implements the first two interfaces above.
We have not shown that it implements the third, but we include this case for completeness because, as shown below, <a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a> leads to a genuine Rényi warm start.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now present the main guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Recursive warm start generator)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\propto\exp(-V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\propto\exp(-V)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-log-smooth, in the
sense that <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, and satisfies the
logarithmic Sobolev inequality with constant <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Write <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\coloneqq\beta/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\coloneqq\beta/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and
suppose that we are given a point <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(x_{\rm ref})-\inf V\leqslant d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(x_{\rm ref})-\inf V\leqslant d</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the smoothed sampler <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy one of
<a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>, <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, and
<a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>. Fix <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta,\Delta\leqslant 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta,\Delta\leqslant 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. For
<math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, write</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}_{q}\coloneqq q+\log\frac{d\kappa q}{\Delta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}_{q}\coloneqq q+\log\frac{d\kappa q}{\Delta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the proximal sampler wrapper in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Algorithm 3.4 (Proximal sampler wrapper). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, with
each inner RGO sampled by <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm 3.3 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, has the
following guarantees.</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.4em;">
<li id="S6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under </span><a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the generator returns a
sample with law </span><math id="S6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(\widehat{\pi}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(\widehat{\pi}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected total number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{2}^{2}\,\mathsf{C}_{2}\Bigl(6,d,\frac{c\Delta}{\sqrt{\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{2}}}\Bigr)+C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{2}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{2}^{2}\,\mathsf{C}_{2}\Bigl(6,d,\frac{c\Delta}{\sqrt{\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{2}}}\Bigr)+C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{2}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix </span><math id="S6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leqslant q&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leqslant q&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Under </span><a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the generator
returns a sample with law </span><math id="S6.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for which there exists a law
</span><math id="S6.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi},\widehat{\pi}^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{\pi}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi},\widehat{\pi}^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{\pi}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected total number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}\,\mathsf{C}_{p}\Bigl(6,d,\frac{c\Delta}{\sqrt{q\kappa\log(eq)\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}}}\Bigr)+C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,\Bigl(\mathfrak{L}_{q}+\log\frac{C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}}{\delta}\Bigr)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}\,\mathsf{C}_{p}\Bigl(6,d,\frac{c\Delta}{\sqrt{q\kappa\log(eq)\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}}}\Bigr)+C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,\Bigl(\mathfrak{L}_{q}+\log\frac{C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}}{\delta}\Bigr)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I2.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\coloneqq 2\vee\Bigl\lceil\log\frac{C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}}{\delta}\Bigr\rceil\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\coloneqq 2\vee\Bigl\lceil\log\frac{C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}}{\delta}\Bigr\rceil\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix </span><math id="S6.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leqslant q&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leqslant q&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Under </span><a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a><span id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the generator returns
a sample with law </span><math id="S6.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{\pi}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{\pi}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected total number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}\,\mathsf{C}_{\psi_{2}}\Bigl(6,d,c\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{q},\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{q\kappa\log(eq)\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}}}\Bigr\}\Bigr)+C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}\,\mathsf{C}_{\psi_{2}}\Bigl(6,d,c\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{q},\frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{q\kappa\log(eq)\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}}}\Bigr\}\Bigr)+C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Although the statement of <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> is cumbersome, it is quite powerful: it states that once we have a smoothed sampler with Wasserstein guarantees, we can immediately obtain a stronger guarantee with a negligible overhead.
Indeed, the cost of the warm start generation is essentially the cost of the original smoothed sampler, called with a slightly smaller accuracy <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta/\sqrt{q\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta/\sqrt{q\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> up to logarithmic factors.
Crucially, in case (ii), we only need the smoothed sampler
guarantee in <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> for an order <math id="S6.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> which is logarithmic in
<math id="S6.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Due to the use of the outer proximal sampler wrapper, note that the smoothed sampler is only ever called on distributions with condition number bounded by a universal constant; above we take it to be <math id="S6.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>. This will ultimately improve the condition number dependence of our combined sampler.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Technical tools</h3>

<section id="S6.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.2.1 </span>Regularization and reverse transport inequalities</h4>

<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The key to the recursive warm start is the regularizing property of the heat flow, which enables proving reverse transport inequalities. We collect together the key inequalities here.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with a simple lemma on truncation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.2</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Truncation)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q</annotation></semantics></math> be probability laws satisfying
<math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{p}(P,Q)\leqslant\varepsilon_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{p}(P,Q)\leqslant\varepsilon_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,
there is a probability law <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P,P^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad W_{\infty}(P^{\dagger},Q)\leqslant\varepsilon_{p}\delta^{-1/p}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P,P^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad W_{\infty}(P^{\dagger},Q)\leqslant\varepsilon_{p}\delta^{-1/p}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose an optimal <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> coupling <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,Y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,Y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\dagger}\coloneqq\begin{cases}Y\,,&amp;\lVert Y-Y^{\star}\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{p}\delta^{-1/p}\,,\\
Y^{\star}\,,&amp;\lVert Y-Y^{\star}\rVert&gt;\varepsilon_{p}\delta^{-1/p}\,.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>δ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>δ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\dagger}\coloneqq\begin{cases}Y\,,&amp;\lVert Y-Y^{\star}\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{p}\delta^{-1/p}\,,\\
Y^{\star}\,,&amp;\lVert Y-Y^{\star}\rVert&gt;\varepsilon_{p}\delta^{-1/p}\,.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Markov’s inequality shows that <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\neq Y^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\neq Y^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at most
<math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas
<math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert Y^{\dagger}-Y^{\star}\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{p}\delta^{-1/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert Y^{\dagger}-Y^{\star}\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{p}\delta^{-1/p}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely. Taking
<math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\dagger}\coloneqq\law(Y^{\dagger})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\dagger}\coloneqq\law(Y^{\dagger})</annotation></semantics></math> proves the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\tau}\coloneqq\mathsf{N}(0,\tau I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\tau}\coloneqq\mathsf{N}(0,\tau I)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The following lemma shows that after applying the heat flow, we can bound stronger information-theoretic divergences in terms of transport distances.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.3</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Reverse transport along the heat flow)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q</annotation></semantics></math> be probability laws on <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.4em;">
<li id="S6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S6.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(P*\gamma_{\tau}\mathbin{\|}Q*\gamma_{\tau})\leqslant\frac{W_{2}^{2}(P,Q)}{2\tau}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(P*\gamma_{\tau}\mathbin{\|}Q*\gamma_{\tau})\leqslant\frac{W_{2}^{2}(P,Q)}{2\tau}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S6.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q\in\mathcal{P}_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q\in\mathcal{P}_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then for every
</span><math id="S6.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, there is a probability law </span><math id="S6.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(P,P^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}(P^{\dagger}*\gamma_{\tau}\mathbin{\|}Q*\gamma_{\tau})\leqslant\frac{qW_{p}^{2}(P,Q)}{2\delta^{2/p}\tau}\,,\qquad\text{for all}~q&gt;1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(P,P^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}(P^{\dagger}*\gamma_{\tau}\mathbin{\|}Q*\gamma_{\tau})\leqslant\frac{qW_{p}^{2}(P,Q)}{2\delta^{2/p}\tau}\,,\qquad\text{for all}~q&gt;1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="S6.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and suppose that
</span><math id="S6.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\psi_{2}}(P,Q)\leqslant\varepsilon_{\psi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\psi_{2}}(P,Q)\leqslant\varepsilon_{\psi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{q\,(q-1)\,\varepsilon_{\psi_{2}}^{2}}{2\tau}\leqslant 1\implies\mathsf{R}_{q}(P*\gamma_{\tau}\mathbin{\|}Q*\gamma_{\tau})\leqslant\frac{q\log 2}{2\tau}\,\varepsilon_{\psi_{2}}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{q\,(q-1)\,\varepsilon_{\psi_{2}}^{2}}{2\tau}\leqslant 1\implies\mathsf{R}_{q}(P*\gamma_{\tau}\mathbin{\|}Q*\gamma_{\tau})\leqslant\frac{q\log 2}{2\tau}\,\varepsilon_{\psi_{2}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Statement (i) follows from the joint convexity of the KL divergence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (ii), choose <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> as in <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 6.2 (Truncation). ‣ 6.2.1 Regularization and reverse transport inequalities ‣ 6.2 Technical tools ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a> and use the fact that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}(P^{\dagger}*\gamma_{\tau}\mathbin{\|}Q*\gamma_{\tau})\leqslant\frac{q}{2\tau}\,W_{\infty}^{2}(P^{\dagger},Q)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}(P^{\dagger}*\gamma_{\tau}\mathbin{\|}Q*\gamma_{\tau})\leqslant\frac{q}{2\tau}\,W_{\infty}^{2}(P^{\dagger},Q)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Part (iii) is <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Remark 3.8]</cite>, with the regularization
parameter there specialized to zero, with zero initial shift,
the source displacement parameter equal to <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\psi_{2}}(P,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\psi_{2}}(P,Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=t</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.2.2 </span>RGO calculus</h4>

<div id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in(0,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in(0,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the RGO potential</p>
<table id="S6.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{A,u}\coloneqq U+\frac{\lVert\cdot-u\rVert^{2}}{2A}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{A,u}\coloneqq U+\frac{\lVert\cdot-u\rVert^{2}}{2A}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and let <math id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{U}_{A,u}\propto\exp(-U_{A,u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{U}_{A,u}\propto\exp(-U_{A,u})</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding RGO.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the lemma below, we note that the RGO of an RGO is itself an RGO for the original distribution, and we record how the parameters change. The proof is an elementary calculation and is omitted.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(RGO calculus)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}U\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}U\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{A,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{A,u}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly convex and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, where</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{A}\coloneqq\kappa^{-1}+A^{-1}\,,\qquad\beta_{A}\coloneqq 1+A^{-1}\,,\qquad\kappa_{A}\coloneqq\frac{\beta_{A}}{\alpha_{A}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{A}\coloneqq\kappa^{-1}+A^{-1}\,,\qquad\beta_{A}\coloneqq 1+A^{-1}\,,\qquad\kappa_{A}\coloneqq\frac{\beta_{A}}{\alpha_{A}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{U_{A,u}}_{a,y}=R^{U}_{A^{+},u^{+}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mi>U</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{U_{A,u}}_{a,y}=R^{U}_{A^{+},u^{+}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="S6.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S6.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{A^{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{A^{+}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{1}{A}+\frac{1}{a}\,,\qquad u^{+}\coloneqq A^{+}\,\Bigl(\frac{u}{A}+\frac{y}{a}\Bigr)\,,\qquad\kappa_{A^{+}}=\frac{a\beta_{A}+1}{a\beta_{A}+\kappa_{A}}\,\kappa_{A}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>A</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>u</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>u</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{1}{A}+\frac{1}{a}\,,\qquad u^{+}\coloneqq A^{+}\,\Bigl(\frac{u}{A}+\frac{y}{a}\Bigr)\,,\qquad\kappa_{A^{+}}=\frac{a\beta_{A}+1}{a\beta_{A}+\kappa_{A}}\,\kappa_{A}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>Recursive RGO sampler</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following result gives the formal guarantee for
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm 3.3 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.
This is essentially the same as <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>, but without the outer proximal sampler wrapper.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.5</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Recursive RGO sampler)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), and suppose that the sampler <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{A}</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfies one of
<a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>, <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, or
<a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>. Fix <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\in(0,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\in(0,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and correspondingly a target <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> for which an admissible reference point <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> is
supplied, let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}\coloneqq\kappa_{A_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}\coloneqq\kappa_{A_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and fix
<math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta_{0},\Delta_{0}\leqslant 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta_{0},\Delta_{0}\leqslant 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, write</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}_{q}\coloneqq q+\log\frac{\kappa_{0}dq}{\Delta_{0}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}_{q}\coloneqq q+\log\frac{\kappa_{0}dq}{\Delta_{0}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm 3.3 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> has the following guarantees.</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I4" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.4em;">
<li id="S6.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under </span><a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a><span id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, it returns a sample with law
</span><math id="S6.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}\mathbin{\|}R^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})\leqslant\Delta_{0}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}\mathbin{\|}R^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})\leqslant\Delta_{0}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I4.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected total number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\mathfrak{L}_{2}\,\mathsf{C}_{2}\Bigl(2\kappa_{0},d,\frac{c\Delta_{0}}{\sqrt{\mathfrak{L}_{2}}}\Bigr)+C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\mathfrak{L}_{2}\,\mathsf{C}_{2}\Bigl(2\kappa_{0},d,\frac{c\Delta_{0}}{\sqrt{\mathfrak{L}_{2}}}\Bigr)+C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix </span><math id="S6.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
Under </span><a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, it returns a sample with law
</span><math id="S6.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for which there exists
</span><math id="S6.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{TV}\bigl(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}},(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})^{\dagger}\bigr)\leqslant\delta_{0}\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}\bigl((\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})^{\dagger}\bigm\|R^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}\bigr)\leqslant\Delta_{0}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}\bigl(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}},(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})^{\dagger}\bigr)\leqslant\delta_{0}\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}\bigl((\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})^{\dagger}\bigm\|R^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}\bigr)\leqslant\Delta_{0}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I4.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected total number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,\mathsf{C}_{p}\Bigl(2\kappa_{0},d,\frac{c\Delta_{0}}{\sqrt{q\mathfrak{L}_{q}}}\Bigr)+C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,\mathsf{C}_{p}\Bigl(2\kappa_{0},d,\frac{c\Delta_{0}}{\sqrt{q\mathfrak{L}_{q}}}\Bigr)+C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I4.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="S6.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\coloneqq 2\vee\lceil\log(C\mathfrak{L}_{q}/\delta_{0})\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\coloneqq 2\vee\lceil\log(C\mathfrak{L}_{q}/\delta_{0})\rceil</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix </span><math id="S6.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Under </span><a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a><span id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, it returns a sample
with law </span><math id="S6.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}\mathbin{\|}R^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})\leqslant\Delta_{0}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}}\mathbin{\|}R^{V}_{A_{0},u_{0}})\leqslant\Delta_{0}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I4.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected total number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,\mathsf{C}_{\psi_{2}}\Bigl(2\kappa_{0},d,c\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{q},\frac{\Delta_{0}}{\sqrt{q\mathfrak{L}_{q}}}\Bigr\}\Bigr)+C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,\mathsf{C}_{\psi_{2}}\Bigl(2\kappa_{0},d,c\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{q},\frac{\Delta_{0}}{\sqrt{q\mathfrak{L}_{q}}}\Bigr\}\Bigr)+C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Although <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm 3.3 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> is written recursively, it is convenient to analyze it iteratively.
Thus, we break down the algorithm into stages, so that the target at stage <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{A_{j},u_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{A_{j},u_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the reported smoothing level at stage <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote the rescaled output by
<math id="S6.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>; its law approximates <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V}_{A_{j},u_{j}}*\mathsf{N}(0,\beta_{A_{j}}^{-1}\eta_{j}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V}_{A_{j},u_{j}}*\mathsf{N}(0,\beta_{A_{j}}^{-1}\eta_{j}I)</annotation></semantics></math>
in a Wasserstein metric. Draw an independent
<math id="S6.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> and set</p>
<table id="S6.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{j}\coloneqq X_{j}+\sqrt{\frac{\tau_{j}}{\beta_{A_{j}}}}\,G_{j}\,,\qquad a_{j}\coloneqq\frac{\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}}{\beta_{A_{j}}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{j}\coloneqq X_{j}+\sqrt{\frac{\tau_{j}}{\beta_{A_{j}}}}\,G_{j}\,,\qquad a_{j}\coloneqq\frac{\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}}{\beta_{A_{j}}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(Y_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(Y_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is close to <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{A_{j},u_{j}}^{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,a_{j}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{A_{j},u_{j}}^{V}*\mathsf{N}(0,a_{j}I)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The algorithm then updates <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{j+1},u_{j+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{j+1},u_{j+1})</annotation></semantics></math> by
(<a href="#S6.E1" title="Equation 6.1 ‣ Lemma 6.4 (RGO calculus). ‣ 6.2.2 RGO calculus ‣ 6.2 Technical tools ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>) with RGO variance <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and center <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, as
in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm 3.3 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. At the terminal level <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>,
it samples the remaining target <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V}_{A_{J},u_{J}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V}_{A_{J},u_{J}}</annotation></semantics></math> with the FORS subroutine.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At stage <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{j}\coloneqq\kappa_{A_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{j}\coloneqq\kappa_{A_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> and choose the heat flow
duration</p>
<table id="S6.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{j}\coloneqq\begin{cases}\kappa_{j}\,,&amp;\kappa_{j}\geqslant 2\,,\\
c_{0}\,,&amp;\kappa_{j}&lt;2\,.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{j}\coloneqq\begin{cases}\kappa_{j}\,,&amp;\kappa_{j}\geqslant 2\,,\\
c_{0}\,,&amp;\kappa_{j}&lt;2\,.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.6</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Geometric progress of the recursive stages)<span id="S6.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="S6.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}\in(0,1/4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}\in(0,1/4)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S6.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta_{j}\leqslant c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta_{j}\leqslant c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> at every stage.</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I5" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.4em;">
<li id="S6.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S6.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{j}\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{j}\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="S6.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\,\kappa_{j}\leqslant\kappa_{j+1}\leqslant\frac{4}{5}\,\kappa_{j}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\,\kappa_{j}\leqslant\kappa_{j+1}\leqslant\frac{4}{5}\,\kappa_{j}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S6.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{j}&lt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{j}&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S6.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j+1}\leqslant 2c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j+1}\leqslant 2c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I5.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and all later
well-conditioned stages obey</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j+1}\leqslant\rho_{0}A_{j}\,,\qquad\rho_{0}\coloneqq\frac{2c_{0}}{1+2c_{0}}&lt;1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j+1}\leqslant\rho_{0}A_{j}\,,\qquad\rho_{0}\coloneqq\frac{2c_{0}}{1+2c_{0}}&lt;1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the first case, by
(<a href="#S6.E2" title="Equation 6.2 ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>), <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{j}=\tau_{j}\leqslant\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}\leqslant\kappa_{j}+c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{j}=\tau_{j}\leqslant\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}\leqslant\kappa_{j}+c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substitution in
(<a href="#S6.E1" title="Equation 6.1 ‣ Lemma 6.4 (RGO calculus). ‣ 6.2.2 RGO calculus ‣ 6.2 Technical tools ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>) gives
(<a href="#S6.E3" title="Equation 6.3 ‣ Item (i) ‣ Lemma 6.6 (Geometric progress of the recursive stages). ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>) after decreasing <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> if necessary.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the well-conditioned regime,
<math id="S6.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}\leqslant\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}\leqslant 2c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}\leqslant\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}\leqslant 2c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By (<a href="#S6.E1" title="Equation 6.1 ‣ Lemma 6.4 (RGO calculus). ‣ 6.2.2 RGO calculus ‣ 6.2 Technical tools ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>), the definition of <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S6.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}\beta_{A_{j}}=A_{j}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}\beta_{A_{j}}=A_{j}+1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j+1}=\frac{A_{j}a_{j}}{A_{j}+a_{j}}=\frac{A_{j}\,(\eta_{j}+\tau_{j})}{A_{j}\beta_{A_{j}}+\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}}=\frac{A_{j}\,(\eta_{j}+\tau_{j})}{A_{j}+1+\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j+1}=\frac{A_{j}a_{j}}{A_{j}+a_{j}}=\frac{A_{j}\,(\eta_{j}+\tau_{j})}{A_{j}\beta_{A_{j}}+\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}}=\frac{A_{j}\,(\eta_{j}+\tau_{j})}{A_{j}+1+\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">This yields</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\tau_{j}+\eta_{j}\leqslant 2c_{0}\,,\qquad\frac{A_{j+1}}{A_{j}}=\frac{\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}}{A_{j}+\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}+1}\leqslant\frac{2c_{0}}{1+2c_{0}}\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\tau_{j}+\eta_{j}\leqslant 2c_{0}\,,\qquad\frac{A_{j+1}}{A_{j}}=\frac{\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}}{A_{j}+\eta_{j}+\tau_{j}+1}\leqslant\frac{2c_{0}}{1+2c_{0}}\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 6.5 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recursive error propagation.</span>
Here and below, take <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=2</annotation></semantics></math> under <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>. For sufficiently small and
large universal constants <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, set</p>
<table id="S6.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{A}\coloneqq\frac{c}{\sqrt{d\mathfrak{L}_{q}}+\mathfrak{L}_{q}}\,,\qquad J\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil C\log\frac{e\kappa_{0}}{\underline{A}}\Bigr\rceil\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{A}\coloneqq\frac{c}{\sqrt{d\mathfrak{L}_{q}}+\mathfrak{L}_{q}}\,,\qquad J\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil C\log\frac{e\kappa_{0}}{\underline{A}}\Bigr\rceil\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">At every stage
<math id="S6.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{0,\ldots,J-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{0,\ldots,J-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, call the smoothed sampler with accuracy</p>
<table id="S6.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{2,j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{2,j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{2\tau_{j}\Delta_{0}^{2}}{\kappa_{j}\,(J+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{2\tau_{j}\Delta_{0}^{2}}{\kappa_{j}\,(J+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-w2}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>under </mtext><mtext><a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag"> A1 </span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-w2}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{p,j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{p,j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{2e^{-2}\tau_{j}\Delta_{0}^{2}}{q\kappa_{j}\,(J+1)}\,,\qquad p\coloneqq 2\vee\Bigl\lceil\log\frac{C\mathfrak{L}_{q}}{\delta_{0}}\Bigr\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{2e^{-2}\tau_{j}\Delta_{0}^{2}}{q\kappa_{j}\,(J+1)}\,,\qquad p\coloneqq 2\vee\Bigl\lceil\log\frac{C\mathfrak{L}_{q}}{\delta_{0}}\Bigr\rceil</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-wp}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>under </mtext><mtext><a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag"> A2 </span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-wp}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\psi_{2},j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\psi_{2},j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{c\tau_{j}}{\kappa_{j}}\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{q\,(q-1)},\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{q\,(J+1)}\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{c\tau_{j}}{\kappa_{j}}\min\Bigl\{\frac{1}{q\,(q-1)},\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{q\,(J+1)}\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.E7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-psi2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>under </mtext><mtext><a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag"> A3 </span></a></mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-psi2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Fix a stage <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&lt;J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&lt;J</annotation></semantics></math> and condition on the complete history up to that stage.
Write <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for the conditional law of <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
write <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{j}\coloneqq R^{V}_{A_{j},u_{j}}*\mathsf{N}(0,a_{j}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{j}\coloneqq R^{V}_{A_{j},u_{j}}*\mathsf{N}(0,a_{j}I)</annotation></semantics></math>
for its ideal law.
Also, let <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{j}(y,\cdot)\coloneqq R^{V_{A_{j},u_{j}}}_{a_{j},y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{j}(y,\cdot)\coloneqq R^{V_{A_{j},u_{j}}}_{a_{j},y}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and let <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{j}(y,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{j}(y,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> be the conditional law returned by the
remaining recursive call after the center <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is selected.
Thus, <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{j}\coloneqq R^{V}_{A_{j},u_{j}}=P_{j}K_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{j}\coloneqq R^{V}_{A_{j},u_{j}}=P_{j}K_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the
output law from level <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{j}=\widehat{P}_{j}\widehat{K}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{j}=\widehat{P}_{j}\widehat{K}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We prove by backward induction that, conditional on every history,</p>
<table id="S6.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\KL(\widehat{R}_{j}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\KL(\widehat{R}_{j}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{J-j+1}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{J-j+1}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-w2}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>under </mtext><mtext><a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag"> A1 </span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-w2}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{J-j+1}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}\,,\qquad\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{R}_{j},\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger})\leqslant\frac{J-j}{J}\,\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>J</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{J-j+1}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}\,,\qquad\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{R}_{j},\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger})\leqslant\frac{J-j}{J}\,\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex34.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-wp}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>under </mtext><mtext><a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag"> A2 </span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-wp}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}_{j}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}_{j}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{J-j+1}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{J-j+1}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex35.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-psi2}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>under </mtext><mtext><a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag"> A3 </span></a></mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{under \ref{ass:smoothed-psi2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p">The terminal construction below establishes the base case <math id="S6.SS3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=J</annotation></semantics></math>, with
<math id="S6.SS3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{J}^{\dagger}=\widehat{R}_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>J</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{J}^{\dagger}=\widehat{R}_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> under
<a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that these inequalities are valid at stage <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Under
<a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>, after rescaling the output, the smoothed sampler provides the guarantee <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}^{2}\leqslant\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{2,j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}^{2}\leqslant\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{2,j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
After convolving with
<math id="S6.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{N}(0,\beta_{A_{j}}^{-1}\tau_{j}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{N}(0,\beta_{A_{j}}^{-1}\tau_{j}I)</annotation></semantics></math>, part (i) of
<a href="#S6.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 6.3 (Reverse transport along the heat flow). ‣ 6.2.1 Regularization and reverse transport inequalities ‣ 6.2 Technical tools ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a> and
(<a href="#S6.E5" title="Equation 6.5 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a>) yield</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(\widehat{P}_{j}\mathbin{\|}P_{j})\leqslant\frac{\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{2,j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}}{2\tau_{j}/\beta_{A_{j}}}=\frac{\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{2,j}^{2}}{2\tau_{j}}=\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{J+1}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(\widehat{P}_{j}\mathbin{\|}P_{j})\leqslant\frac{\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{2,j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}}{2\tau_{j}/\beta_{A_{j}}}=\frac{\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{2,j}^{2}}{2\tau_{j}}=\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{J+1}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, the corresponding guarantee is
<math id="S6.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{p}^{2}\leqslant\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{p,j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{p}^{2}\leqslant\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{p,j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Apply
part (ii) of the same lemma with TV budget <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}/J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}/J</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="S6.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geqslant\log(J/\delta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geqslant\log(J/\delta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="S6.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(J/\delta_{0})^{2/p}\leqslant e^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(J/\delta_{0})^{2/p}\leqslant e^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence there exists <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{P}_{j},\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger})\leqslant\frac{\delta_{0}}{J}\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}P_{j})\leqslant\frac{qe^{2}\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{p,j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}}{2\tau_{j}/\beta_{A_{j}}}=\frac{qe^{2}\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{p,j}^{2}}{2\tau_{j}}=\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{J+1}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>J</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{P}_{j},\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger})\leqslant\frac{\delta_{0}}{J}\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}P_{j})\leqslant\frac{qe^{2}\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{p,j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}}{2\tau_{j}/\beta_{A_{j}}}=\frac{qe^{2}\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{p,j}^{2}}{2\tau_{j}}=\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{J+1}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>, the corresponding guarantee is
<math id="S6.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\psi_{2}}^{2}\leqslant\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{\psi_{2},j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\psi_{2}}^{2}\leqslant\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{\psi_{2},j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a sufficiently small universal <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#S6.E7" title="Equation 6.7 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a>) verifies both</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{q(q-1)\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{\psi_{2},j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}}{2\tau_{j}/\beta_{A_{j}}}=\frac{q(q-1)\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{\psi_{2},j}^{2}}{2\tau_{j}}\leqslant 1\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{P}_{j}\mathbin{\|}P_{j})\leqslant\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{J+1}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{q(q-1)\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{\psi_{2},j}^{2}/\beta_{A_{j}}}{2\tau_{j}/\beta_{A_{j}}}=\frac{q(q-1)\kappa_{j}\varepsilon_{\psi_{2},j}^{2}}{2\tau_{j}}\leqslant 1\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{P}_{j}\mathbin{\|}P_{j})\leqslant\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{J+1}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">We now verify the induction step. Under <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>, the KL
chain rule and data processing give</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\KL(\widehat{R}_{j}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\KL(\widehat{R}_{j}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\KL(\widehat{P}_{j}\mathbin{\|}P_{j})+\int\KL\bigl(\widehat{K}_{j}(y,\cdot)\bigm\|K_{j}(y,\cdot)\bigr)\,\widehat{P}_{j}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>dy</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\KL(\widehat{P}_{j}\mathbin{\|}P_{j})+\int\KL\bigl(\widehat{K}_{j}(y,\cdot)\bigm\|K_{j}(y,\cdot)\bigr)\,\widehat{P}_{j}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{J+1}+\frac{J-j}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}=\frac{J-j+1}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{\Delta_{0}^{2}}{J+1}+\frac{J-j}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}=\frac{J-j+1}{J+1}\,\Delta_{0}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>, the same argument applies except that we replace the KL chain rule with the Rényi composition rule.
Finally, under <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, we take <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger}\coloneqq\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger}\widehat{K}_{j}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger}\coloneqq\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger}\widehat{K}_{j}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we obtain the bound on <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}R_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> as before.
Also, we maximally couple <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S6.SS3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, and on the event that their draws agree, we use the inductive
coupling of <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{j}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{j}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{R}_{j},\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{R}_{j},\widehat{R}_{j}^{\dagger})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{P}_{j},\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger})+\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathsf{TV}\bigl(\widehat{K}_{j}(y,\cdot),\widehat{K}_{j}^{\dagger}(y,\cdot)\bigr)\leqslant\frac{\delta_{0}}{J}+\frac{J-j-1}{J}\,\delta_{0}=\frac{J-j}{J}\,\delta_{0}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>J</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>J</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{P}_{j},\widehat{P}_{j}^{\dagger})+\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathsf{TV}\bigl(\widehat{K}_{j}(y,\cdot),\widehat{K}_{j}^{\dagger}(y,\cdot)\bigr)\leqslant\frac{\delta_{0}}{J}+\frac{J-j-1}{J}\,\delta_{0}=\frac{J-j}{J}\,\delta_{0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reference point construction.</span>
We verify that every smoothed sampler call is supplied with an admissible
reference point and account for the work needed to construct these points.
Let <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> be the current normalized potential and <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> the output of the
smoothed sampler, and write <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for the current heat flow duration.
Under <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a> and <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, use <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\leqslant W_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\leqslant W_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under <a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>, Jensen’s inequality in the definition of
<math id="S6.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\psi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\psi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\leqslant\sqrt{\log 2}\,W_{\psi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\leqslant\sqrt{\log 2}\,W_{\psi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, in every
case, we can couple <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> to the ideal
<math id="S6.SS3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\star}=X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\star}=X+\sqrt{\eta}\,G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\pi_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\pi_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This yields, by <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness of <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S6.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla U(Y)\rVert^{2}\leqslant 2\,\bigl(\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla U(Y^{\star})\rVert^{2}+\kappa_{U}\varepsilon_{j}^{2}\bigr)\leqslant C\,(d+\eta d+\kappa_{U}\varepsilon_{j}^{2})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla U(Y)\rVert^{2}\leqslant 2\,\bigl(\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla U(Y^{\star})\rVert^{2}+\kappa_{U}\varepsilon_{j}^{2}\bigr)\leqslant C\,(d+\eta d+\kappa_{U}\varepsilon_{j}^{2})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the accuracy at stage <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">In normalized coordinates, the next RGO potential is</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{+}\coloneqq U+\frac{\lVert\cdot-(Y+\sqrt{\tau}\,G)\rVert^{2}}{2\,(\eta+\tau)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>τ</mi></msqrt><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{+}\coloneqq U+\frac{\lVert\cdot-(Y+\sqrt{\tau}\,G)\rVert^{2}}{2\,(\eta+\tau)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since
<math id="S6.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{U}^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}U\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{U}^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}U\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>, the potential <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S6.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly convex and <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, where</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{+}\coloneqq\kappa_{U}^{-1}+(\eta+\tau)^{-1}\,,\qquad\beta^{+}\coloneqq 1+(\eta+\tau)^{-1}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{+}\coloneqq\kappa_{U}^{-1}+(\eta+\tau)^{-1}\,,\qquad\beta^{+}\coloneqq 1+(\eta+\tau)^{-1}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Its gradient at <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> adds only
<math id="S6.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\sqrt{\tau}\,G/(\eta+\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>τ</mi></msqrt><mi>G</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\sqrt{\tau}\,G/(\eta+\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla U^{+}(Y)\rVert^{2}\leqslant C\,\Bigl(d+\kappa_{U}\varepsilon_{j}^{2}+\frac{\tau d}{(\eta+\tau)^{2}}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla U^{+}(Y)\rVert^{2}\leqslant C\,\Bigl(d+\kappa_{U}\varepsilon_{j}^{2}+\frac{\tau d}{(\eta+\tau)^{2}}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Gradient descent with step size <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\beta^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\beta^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> produces iterates <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{k}\}_{k\geqslant 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{k}\}_{k\geqslant 0}</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla U^{+}(x_{k})\rVert^{2}\leqslant\kappa^{+}\,\Bigl(1-\frac{1}{\kappa^{+}}\Bigr)^{k}\,\lVert\nabla U^{+}(Y)\rVert^{2}\,,\qquad\kappa^{+}\coloneqq\frac{\beta^{+}}{\alpha^{+}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla U^{+}(x_{k})\rVert^{2}\leqslant\kappa^{+}\,\Bigl(1-\frac{1}{\kappa^{+}}\Bigr)^{k}\,\lVert\nabla U^{+}(Y)\rVert^{2}\,,\qquad\kappa^{+}\coloneqq\frac{\beta^{+}}{\alpha^{+}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">Stopping when <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla U^{+}(x_{k})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha^{+}d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla U^{+}(x_{k})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{\alpha^{+}d}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the admissible reference point for the next stage. The requested radii make the
initial squared gradient polynomial in the stage parameters, so Jensen’s
inequality bounds the expected work at this stage by
<math id="S6.SS3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(\kappa^{+})</annotation></semantics></math>. The condition numbers in the
large conditioning regime form a decreasing geometric sequence, and all later
stages have universally bounded condition number. Summing over the stages
in (<a href="#S6.E4" title="Equation 6.4 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>) bounds the expected cost of all inner reference
points by <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Terminal stage.</span>
By <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 6.6 (Geometric progress of the recursive stages). ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>(i), the regime
<math id="S6.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{j}\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{j}\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> lasts for at most <math id="S6.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\log(e\kappa_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\log(e\kappa_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> stages. Thereafter,
part (ii) of the same lemma contracts <math id="S6.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> by the fixed factor
<math id="S6.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus (<a href="#S6.E4" title="Equation 6.4 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>) ensures that
<math id="S6.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{J}\leqslant\underline{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{J}\leqslant\underline{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set
<math id="S6.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{J}\coloneqq\Delta_{0}/\sqrt{J+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{J}\coloneqq\Delta_{0}/\sqrt{J+1}</annotation></semantics></math>; this is the accuracy requested from the
terminal FORS sampler.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Starting from the retained reference point, gradient descent on the terminal
potential produces <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V_{A_{J},u_{J}}(x_{+})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/A_{J}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V_{A_{J},u_{J}}(x_{+})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{d/A_{J}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The same descent estimate used for the inner reference points shows that
this terminal construction costs at most <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa_{0}\mathfrak{L}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>
expected gradient queries. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert u_{J}-A_{J}\nabla V(x_{+})-x_{+}\rVert=A_{J}\,\lVert\nabla V_{A_{J},u_{J}}(x_{+})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{dA_{J}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert u_{J}-A_{J}\nabla V(x_{+})-x_{+}\rVert=A_{J}\,\lVert\nabla V_{A_{J},u_{J}}(x_{+})\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{dA_{J}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly the condition in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> with
target <math id="S6.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{V}_{A_{J},u_{J}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{V}_{A_{J},u_{J}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>, let <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> be the output of FORS at
order <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. Under <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, let
<math id="S6.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> be the output of FORS at order <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and set
<math id="S6.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{J}^{\dagger}=\widehat{R}_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>J</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{J}^{\dagger}=\widehat{R}_{J}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under
<a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>, let <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> be the output of FORS at order
<math id="S6.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. The choice of <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the localized-scale condition in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>. Hence every terminal call
contributes at most <math id="S6.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{0}^{2}/(J+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{0}^{2}/(J+1)</annotation></semantics></math> in the relevant divergence and has
constant expected gradient query cost, establishing the base cases of the
backward induction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.4 </span>Outer proximal sampler</h3>

<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1 (𝑊_2 guarantee). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorems</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (𝑊_𝑞 guarantee). ‣ 5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, the smoothed Picard HMC sampler requires at least <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> queries, and if we use it as our smoothed sampler then this cost is inherited by the recursive RGO sampler.
Instead, the full warm start generator runs an outer proximal chain with step size
<math id="S6.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2\beta)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2\beta)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and applies the recursive RGO sampler only to its uniformly
well-conditioned RGO targets. This is the construction described in
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Algorithm 3.4 (Proximal sampler wrapper). ‣ 3.4 Recursive warm start generation ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Initialize
<math id="S6.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{0}\coloneqq\mathsf{N}(x_{\rm ref},(2\beta)^{-1}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{0}\coloneqq\mathsf{N}(x_{\rm ref},(2\beta)^{-1}I)</annotation></semantics></math>.
An outer step draws
<math id="S6.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{n}=X_{n}+\mathsf{N}(0,(2\beta)^{-1}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{n}=X_{n}+\mathsf{N}(0,(2\beta)^{-1}I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and then applies an approximate RGO
kernel at <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>, choose</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{0}^{2}\coloneqq\frac{c\Delta^{2}}{\kappa}\,,\qquad N\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil C\kappa\log\frac{ed\kappa}{\Delta}\Bigr\rceil\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{0}^{2}\coloneqq\frac{c\Delta^{2}}{\kappa}\,,\qquad N\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil C\kappa\log\frac{ed\kappa}{\Delta}\Bigr\rceil\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a> and <a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>, keep the
prescribed order <math id="S6.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and choose</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{0}^{2}\coloneqq\frac{c\Delta^{2}}{\kappa\log(eq)}\,,\qquad N_{0}\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil C\kappa\log\frac{ed\kappa}{\Delta}\Bigr\rceil\,,\qquad N_{1}\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil\frac{\log(q-1)}{\log(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})}\Bigr\rceil\,,\qquad N\coloneqq N_{0}+N_{1}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{0}^{2}\coloneqq\frac{c\Delta^{2}}{\kappa\log(eq)}\,,\qquad N_{0}\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil C\kappa\log\frac{ed\kappa}{\Delta}\Bigr\rceil\,,\qquad N_{1}\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil\frac{\log(q-1)}{\log(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})}\Bigr\rceil\,,\qquad N\coloneqq N_{0}+N_{1}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialization.</span>
Write <math id="S6.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\star}\coloneqq\inf V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\star}\coloneqq\inf V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})</annotation></semantics></math>. The
logarithmic Sobolev inequality implies the Poincaré inequality, and hence
<math id="S6.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}_{\pi}\preceq\alpha^{-1}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}_{\pi}\preceq\alpha^{-1}I</annotation></semantics></math>. The Gaussian
maximum entropy bound, together with
<math id="S6.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\int\log\pi\,\mathrm{d}\pi\geqslant V_{\star}+\log\int e^{-V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>∫</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\int\log\pi\,\mathrm{d}\pi\geqslant V_{\star}+\log\int e^{-V}</annotation></semantics></math>,
therefore gives</p>
<table id="S6.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}e^{-V}+V_{\star}\leqslant\frac{d}{2}\log\frac{2\uppi e}{\alpha}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}e^{-V}+V_{\star}\leqslant\frac{d}{2}\log\frac{2\uppi e}{\alpha}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, <math id="S6.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness yields</p>
<table id="S6.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(x)\leqslant V(x_{\rm ref})+\langle g,x-x_{\rm ref}\rangle+\frac{\beta}{2}\,\lVert x-x_{\rm ref}\rVert^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(x)\leqslant V(x_{\rm ref})+\langle g,x-x_{\rm ref}\rangle+\frac{\beta}{2}\,\lVert x-x_{\rm ref}\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">and by the descent lemma,</p>
<table id="S6.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lVert g\rVert^{2}}{2\beta}\leqslant V(x_{\rm ref})-V_{\star}\leqslant d\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lVert g\rVert^{2}}{2\beta}\leqslant V(x_{\rm ref})-V_{\star}\leqslant d\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Comparing the density of
<math id="S6.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{0}=\mathsf{N}(x_{\rm ref},(2\beta)^{-1}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{0}=\mathsf{N}(x_{\rm ref},(2\beta)^{-1}I)</annotation></semantics></math> with that of
<math id="S6.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, and maximizing the resulting quadratic upper bound, gives the
pointwise estimate</p>
<table id="S6.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\widehat{\mu}_{0}}{\mathrm{d}\pi}\leqslant\frac{d}{2}\log(2e\kappa)+2d\leqslant Cd\log(e\kappa)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{\mathrm{d}\widehat{\mu}_{0}}{\mathrm{d}\pi}\leqslant\frac{d}{2}\log(2e\kappa)+2d\leqslant Cd\log(e\kappa)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p4.5" class="ltx_p">Consequently,
<math id="S6.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{\mu}_{0}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant Cd\log(e\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{\mu}_{0}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant Cd\log(e\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> for every
<math id="S6.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, with the convention <math id="S6.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{1}=\KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{1}=\KL</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Approximate RGO kernels.</span>
For every outer RGO target, apply
<a href="#S6.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 6.5 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a> with the local accuracy <math id="S6.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
chosen above. Under
<a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, use <math id="S6.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0}=\delta/(2N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0}=\delta/(2N)</annotation></semantics></math>. Every outer RGO
has curvature between <math id="S6.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\beta I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\beta I</annotation></semantics></math>. Apply
<a href="#S6.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 6.5 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a> to sample from the RGO, taking <math id="S6.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, its three explicit bounds
apply with <math id="S6.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}\leqslant 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}\leqslant 3</annotation></semantics></math>, uniformly over the outer center and complete
history.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Outer contraction and error propagation.</span>
Let <math id="S6.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the law of the <math id="S6.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th iterate <math id="S6.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of the proximal sampler,
and, under <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, let <math id="S6.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>
denote the comparison law. Write
<math id="S6.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n}^{\sharp}=\widehat{\mu}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n}^{\sharp}=\widehat{\mu}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> under <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a> and
<a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>, and <math id="S6.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n}^{\sharp}=\mu_{n}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n}^{\sharp}=\mu_{n}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> under
<a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>, the forward half of the proximal sampler
contraction in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, Theorem 3 and Appendix A.4]</cite> and the KL chain rule give</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(\widehat{\mu}_{n+1}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})^{-1}\KL(\widehat{\mu}_{n}\mathbin{\|}\pi)+\Delta_{0}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(\widehat{\mu}_{n+1}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})^{-1}\KL(\widehat{\mu}_{n}\mathbin{\|}\pi)+\Delta_{0}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(\widehat{\mu}_{N}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})^{-N}\,Cd\log(e\kappa)+C\kappa\Delta_{0}^{2}\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cd</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(\widehat{\mu}_{N}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})^{-N}\,Cd\log(e\kappa)+C\kappa\Delta_{0}^{2}\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to treat <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a> and
<a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>. During the first <math id="S6.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> steps, use the
Rényi contraction from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, Theorem 3 and
Appendix A.4]</cite> and Rényi composition. This yields</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{2}(\mu_{N_{0}}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})^{-N_{0}/2}\,Cd\log(e\kappa)+C\kappa\Delta_{0}^{2}\leqslant\frac{\Delta^{2}}{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>κ</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{2}(\mu_{N_{0}}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})^{-N_{0}/2}\,Cd\log(e\kappa)+C\kappa\Delta_{0}^{2}\leqslant\frac{\Delta^{2}}{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the remaining <math id="S6.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> steps, we leverage hypercontractivity to obtain a sharper dependence on <math id="S6.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="S6.SS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{N_{0}}\coloneqq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>≔</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{N_{0}}\coloneqq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{n+1}-1\coloneqq\min\{q-1,(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})\,(q_{n}-1)\}\,,\qquad n=N_{0},\ldots,N-1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≔</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{n+1}-1\coloneqq\min\{q-1,(1+(2\kappa)^{-1})\,(q_{n}-1)\}\,,\qquad n=N_{0},\ldots,N-1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <math id="S6.SS4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{N}=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{N}=q</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S6.SS4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> has log-Sobolev constant at most
<math id="S6.SS4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, hypercontractivity of simultaneous heat flow
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, Theorem 1.2 and Corollary 1.3]</cite> gives</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q_{n+1}}(\mu_{n}^{\sharp}*\gamma_{(2\beta)^{-1}}\mathbin{\|}\pi*\gamma_{(2\beta)^{-1}})\leqslant\mathsf{R}_{q_{n}}(\mu_{n}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q_{n+1}}(\mu_{n}^{\sharp}*\gamma_{(2\beta)^{-1}}\mathbin{\|}\pi*\gamma_{(2\beta)^{-1}})\leqslant\mathsf{R}_{q_{n}}(\mu_{n}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Data processing through the exact backward RGO, followed by
Rényi composition with the approximate RGO kernel, therefore yields</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q_{n+1}}(\mu_{n+1}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\mathsf{R}_{q_{n}}(\mu_{n}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)+\Delta_{0}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q_{n+1}}(\mu_{n+1}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\mathsf{R}_{q_{n}}(\mu_{n}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)+\Delta_{0}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Iterating and using <math id="S6.SS4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}\leqslant C\kappa\log(eq)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}\leqslant C\kappa\log(eq)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{q}(\mu_{N}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\mathsf{R}_{2}(\mu_{N_{0}}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)+N_{1}\Delta_{0}^{2}\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">♯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{q}(\mu_{N}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\mathsf{R}_{2}(\mu_{N_{0}}^{\sharp}\mathbin{\|}\pi)+N_{1}\Delta_{0}^{2}\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, the TV errors also sum to at most <math id="S6.SS4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Outer reference points.</span>
Under <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a> and <a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>, the preceding
bounds on the KL divergence, followed by
Talagrand’s inequality and smoothness, bounds the second moment of
<math id="S6.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V(Y_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V(Y_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. If we run gradient descent starting from <math id="S6.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,
Jensen’s inequality implies that we can find an admissible reference point to apply <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 6.5 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a> using logarithmic expected work per
outer step.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, the implementable chain need not have
controlled moments of all orders, so cap the outer reference gradient descent after</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\rm cap}\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil\log_{2}\frac{C\kappa N}{\delta}\Bigr\rceil" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>cap</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\rm cap}\coloneqq\Bigl\lceil\log_{2}\frac{C\kappa N}{\delta}\Bigr\rceil</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">steps. Markov’s inequality shows that the
sum of the probabilities that we hit <math id="S6.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\rm cap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>cap</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\rm cap}</annotation></semantics></math> iterations is at most <math id="S6.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Together with TV bounds from the preceding argument, this gives
<math id="S6.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\mu}_{N},\mu_{N}^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\mu}_{N},\mu_{N}^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Set
<math id="S6.SS4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}\coloneqq\widehat{\mu}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}\coloneqq\widehat{\mu}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and, under <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, set
<math id="S6.SS4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}^{\dagger}\coloneqq\mu_{N}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}^{\dagger}\coloneqq\mu_{N}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Query cost.</span>
The choice above satisfies <math id="S6.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leqslant C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leqslant C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> under
<a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>, and <math id="S6.SS4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leqslant C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leqslant C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> under
<a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a> and <a href="#S6.I1.i3" title="Item 
                    
                      A3 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A3
                    
                  </span></a>.
Since the capped outer reference construction uses at most</p>
<table id="S6.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,\Bigl(\mathfrak{L}_{q}+\log\frac{C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}}{\delta}\Bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,\Bigl(\mathfrak{L}_{q}+\log\frac{C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}}{\delta}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p11.2" class="ltx_p">queries, and in the other two cases the cost is at most the final displayed term, <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 6.5 (Recursive RGO sampler). ‣ 6.3 Recursive RGO sampler ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a> and careful bookkeeping proves the result.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler</h2>

<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>Picard HMC warm starts</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first state a strengthened form of <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2 (Warm start). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>. In
particular, strong log-concavity is replaced by log-smoothness and a logarithmic
Sobolev inequality, and we also state KL divergence guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 7.1</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Picard HMC warm starts)<span id="S7.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\propto\exp(-V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\propto\exp(-V)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-log-smooth and satisfies
the logarithmic Sobolev inequality with constant <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Write
<math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\coloneqq\beta/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\coloneqq\beta/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose that we are given a point
<math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(x_{\rm ref})-\inf V\leqslant d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(x_{\rm ref})-\inf V\leqslant d</annotation></semantics></math>.
For every <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\Delta,\delta\leqslant 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\Delta,\delta\leqslant 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, Picard HMC within the recursive warm start
generator satisfies the following guarantees.</span></p>
<ol id="S7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2.4em;">
<li id="S7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It returns a sample with law </span><math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\KL(\widehat{\pi}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\KL(\widehat{\pi}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C\,\bigl(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\Delta^{-1/3}+\kappa\bigr)\log^{9}\frac{e\kappa d}{\Delta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\,\bigl(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\Delta^{-1/3}+\kappa\bigr)\log^{9}\frac{e\kappa d}{\Delta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It returns a sample with law </span><math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
for which there exists
</span><math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}_{\delta},\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{2}(\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}_{\delta},\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger})\leqslant\delta\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{2}(\widehat{\pi}_{\delta}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected number of gradient queries is at most</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C\,\bigl(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\Delta^{-1/3}+\kappa\bigr)\log^{9}\frac{e\kappa d}{\Delta\delta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\,\bigl(\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\Delta^{-1/3}+\kappa\bigr)\log^{9}\frac{e\kappa d}{\Delta\delta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We verify that Picard HMC implements <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a> and
<a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a>, and then invoke
<a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>. Fix a normalized potential <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> with
condition number <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and put <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{\varepsilon}\coloneqq\min\{\varepsilon,\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\varepsilon}\coloneqq\min\{\varepsilon,\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Apply <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (𝑊_𝑞 guarantee). ‣ 5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> with accuracy
<math id="S7.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\kappa_{U}}\,\bar{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\kappa_{U}}\,\bar{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. It returns <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a law
<math id="S7.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\,W_{p}(\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta},\pi_{U,\eta})\leqslant\bar{\varepsilon}\leqslant\varepsilon\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{U}^{-1/2}\,W_{p}(\widehat{\pi}_{U,\eta},\pi_{U,\eta})\leqslant\bar{\varepsilon}\leqslant\varepsilon\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus Picard HMC implements <a href="#S6.I1.i2" title="Item 
                    
                      A2 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A2
                    
                  </span></a> with complexity</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{C}_{p}(\kappa_{U},d,\varepsilon)\leqslant C\,\bigl(\kappa_{U}^{2}+\kappa_{U}^{7/6}\,(d+p)^{1/6}\,\bar{\varepsilon}^{-1/3}\bigr)\,\Bigl(p+\log\frac{e\sqrt{\kappa_{U}}\,d}{\bar{\varepsilon}}\Bigr)^{6}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{C}_{p}(\kappa_{U},d,\varepsilon)\leqslant C\,\bigl(\kappa_{U}^{2}+\kappa_{U}^{7/6}\,(d+p)^{1/6}\,\bar{\varepsilon}^{-1/3}\bigr)\,\Bigl(p+\log\frac{e\sqrt{\kappa_{U}}\,d}{\bar{\varepsilon}}\Bigr)^{6}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=2</annotation></semantics></math> also implements <a href="#S6.I1.i1" title="Item 
                    
                      A1 ‣ Assumption (Smoothed sampler). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
                    
                      A1
                    
                  </span></a>.
Careful bookkeeping shows that the costs are as displayed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Under (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), the reference assumption of
<a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2 (Warm start). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> implies</p>
<table id="S7.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(x_{\rm ref})-\inf V\leqslant\frac{\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert^{2}}{2\alpha}\leqslant\frac{d}{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(x_{\rm ref})-\inf V\leqslant\frac{\lVert\nabla V(x_{\rm ref})\rVert^{2}}{2\alpha}\leqslant\frac{d}{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Thus <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2 (Warm start). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> follows from
<a href="#S7.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 7.1 (Picard HMC warm starts). ‣ 7.1 Picard HMC warm starts ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>(ii) by taking <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Part (i)
also gives a genuine KL warm start under the more general assumptions of
<a href="#S7.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 7.1 (Picard HMC warm starts). ‣ 7.1 Picard HMC warm starts ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>From the proxy warm start to high accuracy</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now record the guarantee for proximal BPS.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 7.2</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Proximal BPS)<span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\tau&lt;1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\tau&lt;1/4</annotation></semantics></math>, and set</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}\coloneqq\Delta^{2}+\log\frac{Cd\kappa}{\tau}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>BPS</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}\coloneqq\Delta^{2}+\log\frac{Cd\kappa}{\tau}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the proximal BPS Markov kernel
<math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\tau,\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\tau,\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following guarantee:
for every <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{2}(\lambda_{0}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{2}(\lambda_{0}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\Delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\lambda_{0}K_{\tau,\Delta},\pi)\leqslant\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\lambda_{0}K_{\tau,\Delta},\pi)\leqslant\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, if <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nabla V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nabla V}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of gradient queries made by this
kernel, then</span></p>
<table id="S7.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa}\,\bigl(d\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}+\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}^{2}\bigr)^{1/4}\,\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}^{3/2}\log(\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>BPS</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>BPS</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>BPS</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>BPS</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa}\,\bigl(d\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}+\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}^{2}\bigr)^{1/4}\,\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}^{3/2}\log(\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is Algorithm 4.2, Theorem 4.3, and Corollary 4.4 of
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 1.3 (Warm start + proximal BPS). ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 7.1 (Picard HMC warm starts). ‣ 7.1 Picard HMC warm starts ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>(ii) with
<math id="S7.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=1/2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>. This produces an
implementable law <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}</annotation></semantics></math> and a comparison law
<math id="S7.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2},\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger})\leqslant\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{2}(\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\frac{1}{4}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}(\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2},\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger})\leqslant\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\,,\qquad\mathsf{R}_{2}(\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger}\mathbin{\|}\pi)\leqslant\frac{1}{4}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Run the proximal BPS kernel
<math id="S7.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\varepsilon/2,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\varepsilon/2,1}</annotation></semantics></math> from the implementable law. By
data processing,</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TV}\bigl(\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}K_{\varepsilon/2,1},\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger}K_{\varepsilon/2,1}\bigr)\leqslant\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TV}\bigl(\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}K_{\varepsilon/2,1},\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger}K_{\varepsilon/2,1}\bigr)\leqslant\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{\varepsilon/2}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the hypothesis of
<a href="#S7.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 7.2 (Proximal BPS). ‣ 7.2 From the proxy warm start to high accuracy ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a> with <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, its image under this kernel is
within <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> in total variation. The triangle
inequality therefore gives the desired error <math id="S7.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Put <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}\coloneqq\log(e\kappa d/\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔏</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}\coloneqq\log(e\kappa d/\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. The warm start
cost is at most
<math id="S7.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\mathfrak{L}^{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\mathfrak{L}^{9}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,\kappa\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,\kappa\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the subsequent proximal BPS call, <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S7.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\varepsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\varepsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>BPS</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}_{\mathrm{BPS}}\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus (<a href="#S7.E1" title="Equation 7.1 ‣ Theorem 7.2 (Proximal BPS). ‣ 7.2 From the proxy warm start to high accuracy ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>) gives the cost bound</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\sqrt{\kappa}\,(d^{1/4}\mathfrak{L}^{7/4}+\mathfrak{L}^{2})\log(\kappa\mathfrak{L})\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa}\,(d^{1/4}\mathfrak{L}^{11/4}+\mathfrak{L}^{3})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\sqrt{\kappa}\,(d^{1/4}\mathfrak{L}^{7/4}+\mathfrak{L}^{2})\log(\kappa\mathfrak{L})\leqslant C\sqrt{\kappa}\,(d^{1/4}\mathfrak{L}^{11/4}+\mathfrak{L}^{3})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here we used <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(\kappa\mathfrak{L})\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(\kappa\mathfrak{L})\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The remaining term <math id="S7.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\kappa}\,\mathfrak{L}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\kappa}\,\mathfrak{L}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is absorbed by
<math id="S7.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\mathfrak{L}^{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{7/6}d^{1/6}\mathfrak{L}^{9}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving the stated query bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Terminal RGO implementation by FORS</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix records the FORS subroutine that we use in the paper. After reviewing the generic FORS mechanism,
we describe a variant that is tailored to sampling from RGO distributions.
Since the main arguments here were already introduced in prior works, we will be more terse and only emphasize the differences from the analyses of
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Review of first-order rejection sampling (FORS)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathsf{D}}_{q}(P,Q)\coloneqq\max\Bigl\{\int\Bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}\Bigr)^{q}\,\mathrm{d}Q-1\,,\int\Bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}Q}{\mathrm{d}P}\Bigr)^{q}\,\mathrm{d}P-1\Bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖣</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathsf{D}}_{q}(P,Q)\coloneqq\max\Bigl\{\int\Bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}\Bigr)^{q}\,\mathrm{d}Q-1\,,\int\Bigl(\frac{\mathrm{d}Q}{\mathrm{d}P}\Bigr)^{q}\,\mathrm{d}P-1\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Either term is understood to be infinite when the corresponding
absolute continuity condition fails.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> be a proposal law for a path <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose the
desired path law satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{P}_{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{Q}}(\mathbf{Z})\propto\exp\{w_{\star}(\mathbf{Z})\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{P}_{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{Q}}(\mathbf{Z})\propto\exp\{w_{\star}(\mathbf{Z})\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Given an auxiliary variable <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\sim\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\sim\Xi</annotation></semantics></math>, FORS uses an estimator
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(\xi;\mathbf{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(\xi;\mathbf{Z})</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\mathbf{Z})\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim\Xi}W(\xi;\mathbf{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\mathbf{Z})\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim\Xi}W(\xi;\mathbf{Z})</annotation></semantics></math>. At clipping level
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, its implemented path law <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}\widehat{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{Q}}(\mathbf{Z})\propto\exp\bigl\{\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim\Xi}\operatorname{clip}_{[-B,B]}\bigl(W(\xi;\mathbf{Z})\bigr)\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>clip</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}\widehat{\mathbf{P}}}{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{Q}}(\mathbf{Z})\propto\exp\bigl\{\mathbb{E}_{\xi\sim\Xi}\operatorname{clip}_{[-B,B]}\bigl(W(\xi;\mathbf{Z})\bigr)\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(FORS likelihood comparison)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{P}</annotation></semantics></math> be the laws of the terminal endpoint of
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
respectively. For every <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\log\{1+\overline{\mathsf{D}}_{q}(\widehat{P},P_{\star})\}\leqslant{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖣</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\log\{1+\overline{\mathsf{D}}_{q}(\widehat{P},P_{\star})\}\leqslant{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{P}_{\star}}\exp\bigl\{4q\,|w_{\star}(\mathbf{Z})-w(\mathbf{Z})|\bigr\}+\log\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathbf{P}_{\star}\\
\xi\sim\Xi\end{subarray}}\exp\bigl\{4q\,\bigl(|W(\xi;\mathbf{Z})|-B\bigr)_{+}\bigr\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{P}_{\star}}\exp\bigl\{4q\,|w_{\star}(\mathbf{Z})-w(\mathbf{Z})|\bigr\}+\log\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathbf{P}_{\star}\\
\xi\sim\Xi\end{subarray}}\exp\bigl\{4q\,\bigl(|W(\xi;\mathbf{Z})|-B\bigr)_{+}\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Lemma 2.4]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To draw a sample from the law <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the following mechanism.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Poisson exponentiation)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim Q</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that, conditionally on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=x</annotation></semantics></math>, one can simulate a
random variable <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{x}\in[-B,B]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{x}\in[-B,B]</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(x)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[W_{x}\mid X=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(x)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[W_{x}\mid X=x]</annotation></semantics></math>. Draw
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\sim\mathsf{Poisson}(2B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌𝗌𝗈𝗇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\sim\mathsf{Poisson}(2B)</annotation></semantics></math> and, conditionally on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=x</annotation></semantics></math>,
independent copies <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{x}^{(1)},\ldots,W_{x}^{(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{x}^{(1)},\ldots,W_{x}^{(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Accept <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with
probability</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{k=1}^{N}\frac{B+W_{x}^{(k)}}{2B}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{k=1}^{N}\frac{B+W_{x}^{(k)}}{2B}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the accepted proposal has law proportional to
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(w)\,Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(w)\,Q</annotation></semantics></math>. The acceptance probability of one attempt is
at least <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(-2B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(-2B)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Algorithm 1 and Theorem 2.3]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>FORS for RGO distributions</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a convex potential <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, a variance <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a center <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{a,y}\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(\cdot)-\frac{\lVert\cdot-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{a,y}\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(\cdot)-\frac{\lVert\cdot-y\rVert^{2}}{2a}\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, we describe a variant of FORS diffusion simulation, specialized to distributions of this form.
Compared to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, we exactly integrate the
linear part of the drift in the underdamped Langevin proposal.
Namely, from <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,p)</annotation></semantics></math>, the proposal is the path measure of</p>
<table id="A1.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{t}\,\mathrm{d}t\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{t}\,\mathrm{d}t\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\Bigl\{\frac{X_{t}-y}{a}+\nabla V(x)+\gamma P_{t}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{2\gamma}\,\mathrm{d}B_{t}\,,\qquad c_{0}a^{-1/2}\leqslant\gamma\leqslant C_{0}a^{-1/2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\Bigl\{\frac{X_{t}-y}{a}+\nabla V(x)+\gamma P_{t}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{2\gamma}\,\mathrm{d}B_{t}\,,\qquad c_{0}a^{-1/2}\leqslant\gamma\leqslant C_{0}a^{-1/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The full algorithm is described below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_algorithm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(FORS for RGO)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a block length <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, a number <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> of blocks, a mesh width
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\rm mesh}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\rm mesh}</annotation></semantics></math> dividing <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, a clipping level <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\rm clip}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\rm clip}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a
stopping set <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Compute
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. On each attempt, initialize</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{0}\sim\mathsf{N}\Bigl(x^{+},\frac{a}{1+a\beta}I\Bigr)\qquad\text{and}\qquad P^{0}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{0}\sim\mathsf{N}\Bigl(x^{+},\frac{a}{1+a\beta}I\Bigr)\qquad\text{and}\qquad P^{0}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">independently. Restart the attempt if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X^{0},P^{0})\notin\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X^{0},P^{0})\notin\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0,\ldots,N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0,\ldots,N-1</annotation></semantics></math>, repeat the following proposal until it is accepted.
Starting from <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=X^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=X^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=P^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=P^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, draw
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\sim\mathsf{Poisson}(2B_{\rm clip})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝗈𝗂𝗌𝗌𝗈𝗇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\sim\mathsf{Poisson}(2B_{\rm clip})</annotation></semantics></math> and independent
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{j}\sim\mathsf{Unif}[0,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}\sim\mathsf{Unif}[0,T)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>. Jointly sample the linear
proposal (<a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>), its driving Brownian motion, and all
values needed below. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}\in[T/h_{\rm mesh}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}\in[T/h_{\rm mesh}]</annotation></semantics></math> be the unique index such
that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{j}-1)h_{\rm mesh}\leqslant t_{j}&lt;r_{j}h_{\rm mesh}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{j}-1)h_{\rm mesh}\leqslant t_{j}&lt;r_{j}h_{\rm mesh}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set</p>
<table id="A1.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{\nabla V(X_{t})-\nabla V(x)}{\sqrt{2\gamma}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{\nabla V(X_{t})-\nabla V(x)}{\sqrt{2\gamma}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\mathcal{W}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\mathcal{W}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{T}{\sqrt{2\gamma}\,h_{\rm mesh}}\,\langle B_{T}-B_{r_{j}h_{\rm mesh}},\nabla V(X_{r_{j}h_{\rm mesh}})-\nabla V(X_{(r_{j}-1)h_{\rm mesh}})\rangle+\frac{T}{2}\,\lVert\mu_{t_{j}}\rVert^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\frac{T}{\sqrt{2\gamma}\,h_{\rm mesh}}\,\langle B_{T}-B_{r_{j}h_{\rm mesh}},\nabla V(X_{r_{j}h_{\rm mesh}})-\nabla V(X_{(r_{j}-1)h_{\rm mesh}})\rangle+\frac{T}{2}\,\lVert\mu_{t_{j}}\rVert^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Accept the proposed endpoint <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{T},P_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{T},P_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> with probability</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{j\in[M]}\frac{B_{\rm clip}+\operatorname{clip}_{[-B_{\rm clip},B_{\rm clip}]}(\mathcal{W}(t_{j}))}{2B_{\rm clip}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>clip</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{j\in[M]}\frac{B_{\rm clip}+\operatorname{clip}_{[-B_{\rm clip},B_{\rm clip}]}(\mathcal{W}(t_{j}))}{2B_{\rm clip}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Upon acceptance, set <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X^{n+1},P^{n+1})\coloneqq(X_{T},P_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X^{n+1},P^{n+1})\coloneqq(X_{T},P_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>. If the accepted
state lies outside <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, restart from the initialization step.
After <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> accepted blocks, return <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(FORS for RGO distributions)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be convex and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, and let
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the law above.
Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon,p\leqslant 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon,p\leqslant 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;a\beta\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;a\beta\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, there is a randomized routine using evaluations of
</span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and one evaluation of </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> whose output law
</span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}_{a,y}\mathbin{\|}R_{a,y})\leqslant\varepsilon^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathsf{R}_{q}(\widehat{R}_{a,y}\mathbin{\|}R_{a,y})\leqslant\varepsilon^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Writing</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{L}\coloneqq q+\log\frac{Cd}{a\beta\varepsilon p}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔏</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{L}\coloneqq q+\log\frac{Cd}{a\beta\varepsilon p}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">its expected number of queries and, with probability at least </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, its
realized number of queries are at most</span></p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\mathfrak{L}^{5/3}\,\bigl\{1+\bigl((a\beta)^{2}d\bigr)^{1/3}\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\mathfrak{L}^{5/3}\,\bigl\{1+\bigl((a\beta)^{2}d\bigr)^{1/3}\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that a
point </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is supplied such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert y-a\nabla V(x_{+})-x_{+}\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{da}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert y-a\nabla V(x_{+})-x_{+}\rVert\leqslant\sqrt{da}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{-1}\geqslant C\beta\,\bigl[\sqrt{d\,(q+\log(1/\varepsilon))}+q+\log(1/\varepsilon)\bigr]\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{-1}\geqslant C\beta\,\bigl[\sqrt{d\,(q+\log(1/\varepsilon))}+q+\log(1/\varepsilon)\bigr]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then a gradient-only routine returns a law satisfying
(</span><a href="#A1.E2" title="Equation A.2 ‣ Item 1 ‣ Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">). It uses </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> expected evaluations
of </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and at most </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\log(2/p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\log(2/p)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> evaluations with probability at
least </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The second statement is the smooth case of
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, Theorem D.1]</cite>. We therefore focus on the first statement, which is based on <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Algorithm A.3 (FORS for RGO). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By rescaling, it suffices to consider <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let
<math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=x^{+}+\sqrt{a}\,z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=x^{+}+\sqrt{a}\,z</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(z)\coloneqq V(x^{+}+\sqrt{a}\,z)-V(x^{+})-\sqrt{a}\,\langle\nabla V(x^{+}),z\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(z)\coloneqq V(x^{+}+\sqrt{a}\,z)-V(x^{+})-\sqrt{a}\,\langle\nabla V(x^{+}),z\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">After a change of variables, we consider the density proportional to</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\mapsto\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert z\rVert^{2}-F(z)\Bigr\}\,,\qquad F(0)=0\,,\qquad\nabla F(0)=0\,,\qquad 0\preceq\nabla^{2}F\preceq aI\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\mapsto\exp\Bigl\{-\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert z\rVert^{2}-F(z)\Bigr\}\,,\qquad F(0)=0\,,\qquad\nabla F(0)=0\,,\qquad 0\preceq\nabla^{2}F\preceq aI\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Writing <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\coloneqq\nabla F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\coloneqq\nabla F</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\gamma}\coloneqq\sqrt{a}\,\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\gamma}\coloneqq\sqrt{a}\,\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding space–time rescaling
transforms (<a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>), conditionally on the blockwise
initial state <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{0},P_{0})=(z,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{0},P_{0})=(z,p)</annotation></semantics></math>, into</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{t}\,\mathrm{d}t\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{t}\,\mathrm{d}t\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\{Z_{t}+g(z)+\bar{\gamma}P_{t}\}\,\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{2\bar{\gamma}}\,\mathrm{d}B_{t}\,,\qquad c_{0}\leqslant\bar{\gamma}\leqslant C_{0}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\{Z_{t}+g(z)+\bar{\gamma}P_{t}\}\,\mathrm{d}t+\sqrt{2\bar{\gamma}}\,\mathrm{d}B_{t}\,,\qquad c_{0}\leqslant\bar{\gamma}\leqslant C_{0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We explain the only changes needed in the FORS proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>. Let
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> solve</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime\prime}+\bar{\gamma}S^{\prime}+S=0\,,\qquad S(0)=0\,,\qquad S^{\prime}(0)=1\,,\qquad b_{t}\coloneqq\int_{0}^{t}S_{r}\,\mathrm{d}r\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime\prime}+\bar{\gamma}S^{\prime}+S=0\,,\qquad S(0)=0\,,\qquad S^{\prime}(0)=1\,,\qquad b_{t}\coloneqq\int_{0}^{t}S_{r}\,\mathrm{d}r\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">For bounded <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and sufficiently small <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S_{t}|\leqslant Ct" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S_{t}|\leqslant Ct</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|b_{t}|\leqslant Ct^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|b_{t}|\leqslant Ct^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S_{t}^{\prime}|+|S_{t}^{\prime\prime}|\leqslant C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S_{t}^{\prime}|+|S_{t}^{\prime\prime}|\leqslant C</annotation></semantics></math>. Under
(<a href="#A1.E4" title="Equation A.4 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}-z=S_{t}\,p-b_{t}\,\{z+g(z)\}+\sqrt{2\bar{\gamma}}\int_{0}^{t}S_{t-s}\,\mathrm{d}B_{s}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}-z=S_{t}\,p-b_{t}\,\{z+g(z)\}+\sqrt{2\bar{\gamma}}\int_{0}^{t}S_{t-s}\,\mathrm{d}B_{s}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently the Girsanov control contains only the residual force,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}\coloneqq\frac{g(Z_{t})-g(z)}{\sqrt{2\bar{\gamma}}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}\coloneqq\frac{g(Z_{t})-g(z)}{\sqrt{2\bar{\gamma}}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">This is the main improvement due to exact integration of the linear term.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now put</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(z,p)\coloneqq\lVert p\rVert^{2}+\lVert z\rVert^{2}+a^{-1}\,\lVert g(z)\rVert^{2}+d\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(z,p)\coloneqq\lVert p\rVert^{2}+\lVert z\rVert^{2}+a^{-1}\,\lVert g(z)\rVert^{2}+d\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The calculations in
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Lemmas B.1 and B.3]</cite>, applied to
(<a href="#A1.E5" title="Equation A.5 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>), gives the same estimate
as in that paper with its full smoothness replaced by the residual
smoothness <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, the random likelihood factor has
sub-Gaussian scale</span></p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathbb{E}\exp\{\lambda\,|\mathcal{W}_{t}|\}\leqslant\log 2+C\lambda^{2}\,\frac{a^{2}T^{3}}{\bar{\gamma}}\,\mathcal{R}(z,p)\,,\qquad 1\leqslant\lambda\leqslant\frac{c}{aT^{2}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{E}\exp\{\lambda\,|\mathcal{W}_{t}|\}\leqslant\log 2+C\lambda^{2}\,\frac{a^{2}T^{3}}{\bar{\gamma}}\,\mathcal{R}(z,p)\,,\qquad 1\leqslant\lambda\leqslant\frac{c}{aT^{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">If the control is frozen on a mesh of width <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\rm mesh}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\rm mesh}</annotation></semantics></math>, its
discretization error <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\rm mesh}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\rm mesh}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\mathbb{E}\exp\{\lambda\,|\mathcal{E}_{\rm mesh}|\}\leqslant C\lambda\,\frac{ah_{\rm mesh}}{\bar{\gamma}}\,(d^{-1/2}+aT^{2})\,\mathcal{R}(z,p)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>λ</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>mesh</mi></msub></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mfrac><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{E}\exp\{\lambda\,|\mathcal{E}_{\rm mesh}|\}\leqslant C\lambda\,\frac{ah_{\rm mesh}}{\bar{\gamma}}\,(d^{-1/2}+aT^{2})\,\mathcal{R}(z,p)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">The proofs are the same as
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Lemma C.1 and the proof of Proposition 3.1]</cite>; the bounds on
<math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> above replace the exponential Euler bounds there.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (FORS likelihood comparison). ‣ A.1 Review of first-order rejection sampling (FORS) ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> using
<a href="#A1.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a> and <a href="#A1.E7" title="Equation A.7 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>, and then choosing the
clipping level and mesh exactly as in that proof, gives the required
error on one block. The stopped composition and query tail arguments
are unchanged from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Theorem B.11]</cite>. One <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> factor
uses <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> at no more than three times. Since the linear process
<math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z,P,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z,P,B)</annotation></semantics></math> can be sampled by Gaussian regression at only those times and the
two adjacent mesh points, refining the mesh makes no additional
gradient queries.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Initialize from <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{N}(0,(1+a)^{-1}\,I)\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{N}(0,(1+a)^{-1}\,I)\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. The bounds</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert z\rVert^{2}\leqslant\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert z\rVert^{2}+F(z)\leqslant\frac{1+a}{2}\,\lVert z\rVert^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert z\rVert^{2}\leqslant\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert z\rVert^{2}+F(z)\leqslant\frac{1+a}{2}\,\lVert z\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">imply that the initial
<math id="A1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{R}_{2q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖱</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{R}_{2q}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence is at most <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ad/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ad/2</annotation></semantics></math>. For the choices below,
the logarithmic factor in the stopped composition argument satisfies <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2q+\log\frac{CNq}{\varepsilon^{2}}\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2q+\log\frac{CNq}{\varepsilon^{2}}\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Take</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T\coloneqq c\mathfrak{L}^{-2/3}\min\{1,(a^{2}d)^{-1/3}\}\qquad\text{and}\qquad N\coloneqq\bigl\lceil C\mathfrak{L}/T\bigr\rceil\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mi>N</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>𝔏</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\coloneqq c\mathfrak{L}^{-2/3}\min\{1,(a^{2}d)^{-1/3}\}\qquad\text{and}\qquad N\coloneqq\bigl\lceil C\mathfrak{L}/T\bigr\rceil\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, the cubic restriction from
<a href="#A1.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a> is
<math id="A1.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{3}\leqslant c/(a^{2}d\mathfrak{L}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{3}\leqslant c/(a^{2}d\mathfrak{L}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, while the quadratic restriction is
<math id="A1.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{2}\leqslant c/(a\mathfrak{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{2}\leqslant c/(a\mathfrak{L})</annotation></semantics></math>; the displayed choice satisfies both.
The mesh is then refined until
<a href="#A1.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a> gives the required path accuracy, without
additional gradient queries. Since the target is <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly
log-concave, a total time <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="NT\geqslant C\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NT\geqslant C\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math> suffices in the
LSI mixing and Rényi composition argument of
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, Theorem 3.2(ii)]</cite>, run at Rényi order <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2q</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields
(<a href="#A1.E2" title="Equation A.2 ‣ Item 1 ‣ Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>). Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}^{5/3}\,\{1+(a^{2}d)^{1/3}\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔏</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}^{5/3}\,\{1+(a^{2}d)^{1/3}\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">The stopped implementation uses <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math> expected queries and
<math id="A1.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N+\log(1/p))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N+\log(1/p))</annotation></semantics></math> queries with probability at least <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A1.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1/p)\leqslant\mathfrak{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>𝔏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1/p)\leqslant\mathfrak{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, this proves
(<a href="#A1.E3" title="Equation A.3 ‣ Item 1 ‣ Theorem A.4 (FORS for RGO distributions). ‣ A.2 FORS for RGO distributions ‣ Appendix A Terminal RGO implementation by FORS ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix collects the interpolation facts used by the Picard
integrator.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Nodes, interpolating polynomials, and integrated weights</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For an integer <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> indicating the total number of nodes, define the increasing Chebyshev–Lobatto nodes on
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,h]</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}\coloneqq\frac{h}{2}\,\bigl\{1-\cos\bigl({\textstyle\frac{j-1}{J-1}}\,\uppi\bigr)\bigr\}\,,\qquad 1\leqslant j\leqslant J\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">π</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}\coloneqq\frac{h}{2}\,\bigl\{1-\cos\bigl({\textstyle\frac{j-1}{J-1}}\,\uppi\bigr)\bigr\}\,,\qquad 1\leqslant j\leqslant J\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Their interpolating polynomials are</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell_{j}(t)\coloneqq\prod_{\begin{subarray}{c}1\leqslant k\leqslant J\\
k\neq j\end{subarray}}\frac{t-t_{k}}{t_{j}-t_{k}}\,,\qquad\ell_{j}(t_{k})=\mathbf{1}_{\{j=k\}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{j}(t)\coloneqq\prod_{\begin{subarray}{c}1\leqslant k\leqslant J\\
k\neq j\end{subarray}}\frac{t-t_{k}}{t_{j}-t_{k}}\,,\qquad\ell_{j}(t_{k})=\mathbf{1}_{\{j=k\}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, the operator <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{J,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{J,h}</annotation></semantics></math> in
(<a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 3.5 ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>) is the unique polynomial interpolant of
degree at most <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Its Lebesgue constant is defined as</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{J}\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\sum_{j=1}^{J}|\ell_{j}(t)|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{J}\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\sum_{j=1}^{J}|\ell_{j}(t)|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For a normed space <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f(t_{j})\}_{j=1}^{J}\subseteq E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f(t_{j})\}_{j=1}^{J}\subseteq E</annotation></semantics></math>, the triangle
inequality immediately gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}f)(t)\rVert_{E}\leqslant\Lambda_{J}\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert f(t_{j})\rVert_{E}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}f)(t)\rVert_{E}\leqslant\Lambda_{J}\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert f(t_{j})\rVert_{E}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the quadrature coefficients <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> from
(<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 3.6 ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>). By their
definition, for every polynomial <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> of degree at most <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J-1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t_{i}}(t_{i}-t)f(t)\,\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{t_{i}}(t_{i}-t)f(t)\,\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{i,j}f(t_{j})\,,\qquad\int_{0}^{h}f(t)\,\mathrm{d}t=\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{j}f(t_{j})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{i,j}f(t_{j})\,,\qquad\int_{0}^{h}f(t)\,\mathrm{d}t=\sum_{j=1}^{J}\omega_{j}f(t_{j})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Chebyshev–Lobatto coefficient bounds)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{i\in[J]}\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{i\in[J]}\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\Lambda_{J}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\Lambda_{J}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant 0\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant 0\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Lambda_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Lambda_{J}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2}{\uppi}\log J+1\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2}{\uppi}\log J+1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The classical estimate for <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, Theorem 15.2]</cite>. Using
(<a href="#A2.E1" title="Equation B.1 ‣ B.1 Nodes, interpolating polynomials, and integrated weights ‣ Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>) under the defining integrals gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{0}^{t_{i}}(t_{i}-t)\sum_{j\in[J]}|\ell_{j}(t)|\,\mathrm{d}t\leqslant\frac{t_{i}^{2}}{2}\,\Lambda_{J}\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\Lambda_{J}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{0}^{t_{i}}(t_{i}-t)\sum_{j\in[J]}|\ell_{j}(t)|\,\mathrm{d}t\leqslant\frac{t_{i}^{2}}{2}\,\Lambda_{J}\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\Lambda_{J}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are the
Clenshaw–Curtis weights, which are non-negative. Since the rule integrates
constants exactly on <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,h]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,h]</annotation></semantics></math>, they sum to <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Interpolation error bound</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We record the standard interpolation error bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Banach-valued interpolation error bound)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> be a Banach space and let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in C^{J}([0,h];E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>J</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in C^{J}([0,h];E)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert f(t)-(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}f)(t)\rVert_{E}\leqslant\frac{1}{J!}\sup_{0\leqslant s\leqslant h}\,\lVert f^{(J)}(s)\rVert_{E}\prod_{j=1}^{J}|t-t_{j}|\leqslant\frac{h^{J}}{J!}\sup_{0\leqslant s\leqslant h}\,\lVert f^{(J)}(s)\rVert_{E}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>J</mi></msup><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert f(t)-(\mathcal{I}_{J,h}f)(t)\rVert_{E}\leqslant\frac{1}{J!}\sup_{0\leqslant s\leqslant h}\,\lVert f^{(J)}(s)\rVert_{E}\prod_{j=1}^{J}|t-t_{j}|\leqslant\frac{h^{J}}{J!}\sup_{0\leqslant s\leqslant h}\,\lVert f^{(J)}(s)\rVert_{E}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This is the Banach-valued form of the Genocchi–Hermite interpolation
remainder; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, Section 9]</cite>. Apply the scalar argument to <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\circ f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\circ f</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in E^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in E^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> has unit norm. Taking the supremum over all such <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> concludes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Gaussian analysis</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix collects the Gaussian analysis used throughout
the paper.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Basic inequalities and heat smoothing</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recall the definition of a Wiener chaos. The <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th Wiener chaos is the subspace of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>
consisting of polynomials of degree at most <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> that are
orthogonal to every polynomial of degree less than <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
The zeroth chaos consists of constants.
For <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th chaos, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{OU}}F=-nF" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>OU</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{OU}}F=-nF</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{OU}})^{-1}F=(n+1)^{-1}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>OU</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{OU}})^{-1}F=(n+1)^{-1}F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Derivative and divergence inequalities.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> be standard Gaussian measure on <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also let
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite-dimensional<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              We expect that the results can be extended to the infinite-dimensional setting, but this will not be needed here.</span></span></span> Hilbert space, and let
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=(V_{i})_{i\in[d]}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=(V_{i})_{i\in[d]}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be smooth. Its Gaussian
divergence is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\gamma}V\coloneqq\sum_{i\in[d]}(x_{i}V_{i}-\partial_{i}V_{i})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\gamma}V\coloneqq\sum_{i\in[d]}(x_{i}V_{i}-\partial_{i}V_{i})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It is the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>-adjoint of the gradient:</p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}\langle DF,V\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}=\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}\langle F,\delta_{\gamma}V\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}\langle DF,V\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}=\mathbb{E}_{\gamma}\langle F,\delta_{\gamma}V\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\nabla" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∇</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\nabla</annotation></semantics></math> is the usual gradient.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Componentwise Gaussian Poincaré and two applications of
(<a href="#A3.E1" title="Equation C.1 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) give</p>
<table id="A3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert F-\mathbb{E}F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\leqslant\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,,\qquad\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}^{2}\leqslant\lVert V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}^{2}+\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>V</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert F-\mathbb{E}F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\leqslant\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,,\qquad\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}^{2}\leqslant\lVert V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}^{2}+\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the exact identity behind the second inequality is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}^{2}=\lVert V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}^{2}+\sum_{i,j\in[d]}\mathbb{E}\langle\partial_{j}V_{i},\partial_{i}V_{j}\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,;" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>V</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}^{2}=\lVert V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}^{2}+\sum_{i,j\in[d]}\mathbb{E}\langle\partial_{j}V_{i},\partial_{i}V_{j}\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\,;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">the last sum is at most <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by
Cauchy–Schwarz. If <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}\coloneqq\mathsf{N}(0,tI)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}\coloneqq\mathsf{N}(0,tI)</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\gamma_{t}}V\coloneqq\sum_{i\in[d]}(t^{-1}x_{i}V_{i}-\partial_{i}V_{i})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\gamma_{t}}V\coloneqq\sum_{i\in[d]}(t^{-1}x_{i}V_{i}-\partial_{i}V_{i})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">and the change of variables <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sqrt{t}\,z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sqrt{t}\,z</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\gamma_{t}}V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma_{t})}^{2}\leqslant t^{-1}\,\lVert V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma_{t};\mathrm{HS})}^{2}+\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma_{t};\mathrm{HS})}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>V</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\gamma_{t}}V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma_{t})}^{2}\leqslant t^{-1}\,\lVert V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma_{t};\mathrm{HS})}^{2}+\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma_{t};\mathrm{HS})}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">We also need <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> versions of these inequalities, which requires some groundwork. Let</p>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}}\coloneqq\Delta-\langle x,\nabla\rangle=-\delta_{\gamma}D\,,\qquad Q_{t}\coloneqq\exp(t\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>∇</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}}\coloneqq\Delta-\langle x,\nabla\rangle=-\delta_{\gamma}D\,,\qquad Q_{t}\coloneqq\exp(t\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Mehler’s
formula reads</p>
<table id="A3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q_{t}F)(x)=\mathbb{E}F\bigl(e^{-t}\,x+\sqrt{1-e^{-2t}}\,G\bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q_{t}F)(x)=\mathbb{E}F\bigl(e^{-t}\,x+\sqrt{1-e^{-2t}}\,G\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Recall the basic facts</p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert Q_{t}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,,\qquad Q_{t}^{*}=Q_{t}\,,\qquad DQ_{t}F=e^{-t}Q_{t}DF\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert Q_{t}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,,\qquad Q_{t}^{*}=Q_{t}\,,\qquad DQ_{t}F=e^{-t}Q_{t}DF\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.8" class="ltx_p">These statements remain valid for functions with values in a
finite-dimensional Hilbert space.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gaussian Riesz estimate)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional Hilbert space and let
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;q\leqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;q\leqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>. For every
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\frac{C}{q-1}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\frac{C}{q-1}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The constant is independent of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The estimate in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Theorem 4]</cite> states, for centered scalar
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, that</span></p>
<table id="A3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}f\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}\leqslant 2\,\Bigl[\bigl(q\vee\frac{q}{q-1}\bigr)-1\Bigr]\,\lVert f\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}=\frac{2}{q-1}\,\lVert f\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}\,,\qquad 1&lt;q\leqslant 2\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>f</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}f\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}\leqslant 2\,\Bigl[\bigl(q\vee\frac{q}{q-1}\bigr)-1\Bigr]\,\lVert f\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}=\frac{2}{q-1}\,\lVert f\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}\,,\qquad 1&lt;q\leqslant 2\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> annihilates constants, applying
(<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>) to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f-\mathbb{E}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f-\mathbb{E}f</annotation></semantics></math> and using
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert f-\mathbb{E}f\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant 2\,\lVert f\rVert_{L^{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert f-\mathbb{E}f\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant 2\,\lVert f\rVert_{L^{q}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the same estimate for
arbitrary scalar <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, up to a factor two.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now pass to a Hilbert-valued <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h_{j})_{j\in[m]}\subset\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h_{j})_{j\in[m]}\subset\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{j})_{j\in[m]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{j})_{j\in[m]}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent standard Gaussians, then for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;q\leqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;q\leqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{0}\,\biggl(\sum_{j\in[m]}\lVert h_{j}\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\biggr)^{1/2}\leqslant\Bigl\{\mathbb{E}\Bigl\lVert\sum_{j\in[m]}g_{j}h_{j}\Bigr\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{q}\Bigr\}^{1/q}\leqslant\biggl(\sum_{j\in[m]}\lVert h_{j}\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\biggr)^{1/2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}\,\biggl(\sum_{j\in[m]}\lVert h_{j}\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\biggr)^{1/2}\leqslant\Bigl\{\mathbb{E}\Bigl\lVert\sum_{j\in[m]}g_{j}h_{j}\Bigr\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{q}\Bigr\}^{1/q}\leqslant\biggl(\sum_{j\in[m]}\lVert h_{j}\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\biggr)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">for a universal <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Indeed, this follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, Corollary 3.2]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expand <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\sum_{j\in[m]}F_{j}e_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\sum_{j\in[m]}F_{j}e_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in an orthonormal basis of
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. Apply the lower bound in
(<a href="#A3.E9" title="Equation C.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>) pointwise to the vectors
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then apply
(<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>) to each randomized scalar function,
and finally apply the upper bound in
(<a href="#A3.E9" title="Equation C.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>) pointwise to the vectors
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fubini’s theorem gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\,\Bigl\{\mathbb{E}\Bigl\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}\sum_{j\in[m]}g_{j}F_{j}\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}^{q}\Bigr\}^{1/q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\,\Bigl\{\mathbb{E}\Bigl\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}\sum_{j\in[m]}g_{j}F_{j}\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}^{q}\Bigr\}^{1/q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{C}{q-1}\,\Bigl\{\mathbb{E}\Bigl\lVert\sum_{j\in[m]}g_{j}F_{j}\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}^{q}\Bigr\}^{1/q}\leqslant\frac{C}{q-1}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{C}{q-1}\,\Bigl\{\mathbb{E}\Bigl\lVert\sum_{j\in[m]}g_{j}F_{j}\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}^{q}\Bigr\}^{1/q}\leqslant\frac{C}{q-1}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Second-order Gaussian Riesz estimate)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional Hilbert space and let
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;q\leqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;q\leqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Every smooth compactly supported
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert(1-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}D^{2}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}=\Bigl\lVert\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\frac{C}{(q-1)^{2}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert(1-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}D^{2}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}=\Bigl\lVert\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\frac{C}{(q-1)^{2}}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The constant is independent of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
The operator on the left extends uniquely to all of
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the resolvent</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\coloneqq(1-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}=\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}\,\mathrm{d}t\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\coloneqq(1-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}=\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}\,\mathrm{d}t\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The contraction in (<a href="#A3.E6" title="Equation C.6 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>) gives
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathcal{R}\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)\to L^{q}(\gamma)}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathcal{R}\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)\to L^{q}(\gamma)}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}\coloneqq\binom{1/2}{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}\coloneqq\binom{1/2}{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then, for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|a_{j}|=\frac{1}{2j-1}\,\binom{2j}{j}\,4^{-j}\leqslant\frac{1}{(2j-1)\sqrt{j+1}}\leqslant Cj^{-3/2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn> 4</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{j}|=\frac{1}{2j-1}\,\binom{2j}{j}\,4^{-j}\leqslant\frac{1}{(2j-1)\sqrt{j+1}}\leqslant Cj^{-3/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\geqslant 0}|a_{j}|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\geqslant 0}|a_{j}|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\coloneqq\sum_{j\geqslant 0}a_{j}\mathcal{R}^{j}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\coloneqq\sum_{j\geqslant 0}a_{j}\mathcal{R}^{j}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">converges absolutely in operator norm with
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathcal{M}\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)\to L^{q}(\gamma)}\leqslant C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathcal{M}\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)\to L^{q}(\gamma)}\leqslant C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th Wiener
chaos, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> has multiplier <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+1)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+1)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so for every
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> in that chaos,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}F=\sum_{j\geqslant 0}\frac{a_{j}}{(n+1)^{j}}\,F=\Bigl(\frac{n+2}{n+1}\Bigr)^{1/2}\,F\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}F=\sum_{j\geqslant 0}\frac{a_{j}}{(n+1)^{j}}\,F=\Bigl(\frac{n+2}{n+1}\Bigr)^{1/2}\,F\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}}\coloneqq D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}}\coloneqq D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> on
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued functions. A check on
each Wiener chaos gives the exact factorization</span></p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t=\mathcal{M}\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}\otimes\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}}F\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t=\mathcal{M}\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}\otimes\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}}F\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, if <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th chaos, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, then the
left-hand side of (<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation C.13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.13</span></a>) equals</span></p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-(n-1)t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t=\frac{D^{2}F}{n-1}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-(n-1)t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t=\frac{D^{2}F}{n-1}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiation maps the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th Wiener chaos into the
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-st chaos; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, Proposition 1.2.2]</cite>.
Consequently, for <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th chaos, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}}F=n^{-1/2}DF" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}}F=n^{-1/2}DF</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">belongs to the <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-st chaos.
Thus, the two Riesz transforms on the right-hand side of (<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation C.13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.13</span></a>) produce
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}F/\sqrt{n\,(n-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}F/\sqrt{n\,(n-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
(<a href="#A3.E12" title="Equation C.12 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a>), applied on the
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-2)</annotation></semantics></math>-chaos, supplies <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{n/(n-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{n/(n-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Their product is
exactly (<a href="#A3.E14" title="Equation C.14 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.14</span></a>). This proves
(<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation C.13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.13</span></a>) on Hermite polynomials.
The right-hand side extends to a bounded operator on <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math> by
(<a href="#A3.E7" title="Equation C.7 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Gaussian Riesz estimate). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A3.E11" title="Equation C.11 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.11</span></a>). For a smooth
compactly supported <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, its Hermite expansion converges in the
domain of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so both sides of
(<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation C.13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.13</span></a>) are the same <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
limit. Thus the integral on the left is precisely this bounded
extension in the setting used below.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply (<a href="#A3.E7" title="Equation C.7 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Gaussian Riesz estimate). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>) first with target
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, then with target
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}\otimes\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\otimes\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and use
the operator norm bound following
(<a href="#A3.E11" title="Equation C.11 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.11</span></a>). The factorization
(<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation C.13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.13</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Bigl\lVert\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}=\lVert\mathcal{M}\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}\otimes\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Bigl\lVert\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}=\lVert\mathcal{M}\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}\otimes\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{H}}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\,\Bigl(\frac{1}{q-1}\Bigr)^{2}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\,\Bigl(\frac{1}{q-1}\Bigr)^{2}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gaussian Sobolev inequalities)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in W^{1,q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in W^{1,q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert F-\mathbb{E}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert F-\mathbb{E}F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in W^{1,q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in W^{1,q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\gamma}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\gamma}V</annotation></semantics></math> is its row divergence, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert\mathbb{E}V\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}+Cq^{2}\,\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert\mathbb{E}V\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}+Cq^{2}\,\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If we replace <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the centered Gaussian measure of covariance <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tI</annotation></semantics></math>, then the first term on
the right side of (<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.3 (Gaussian Sobolev inequalities). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>) is multiplied by
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first estimate follows from Pisier’s Gaussian convexity inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, Theorem 2.2]</cite>, applied with the convex
function <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto\lVert u\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto\lVert u\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">As we were unable to find a proof of the divergence estimate with explicit dependence on <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> in the literature, we give a proof here using
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2 (Second-order Gaussian Riesz estimate). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.
First suppose that <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth and compactly supported, and that
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}V=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}V=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Strong continuity and ergodicity of the Mehler semigroup
(<a href="#A3.E5" title="Equation C.5 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\varepsilon}^{T}(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})Q_{t}V\,\mathrm{d}t=Q_{\varepsilon}V-Q_{T}V\longrightarrow V\quad\text{in }L^{q}(\gamma)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>in </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\varepsilon}^{T}(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})Q_{t}V\,\mathrm{d}t=Q_{\varepsilon}V-Q_{T}V\longrightarrow V\quad\text{in }L^{q}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">as <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\searrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>↘</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\searrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\nearrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>↗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\nearrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. For a smooth
compactly supported test function <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, the adjoint
identity (<a href="#A3.E1" title="Equation C.1 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>), the identity
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}}=\delta_{\gamma}D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}}=\delta_{\gamma}D</annotation></semantics></math> in
(<a href="#A3.E4" title="Equation C.4 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>), and
(<a href="#A3.E16" title="Equation C.16 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.16</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\langle F,\delta_{\gamma}V\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\langle F,\delta_{\gamma}V\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\langle DF,V\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\langle DF,\delta_{\gamma}DQ_{t}V\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}\,\mathrm{d}t=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\langle D^{2}F,DQ_{t}V\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}\,\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\langle DF,V\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\langle DF,\delta_{\gamma}DQ_{t}V\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}\,\mathrm{d}t=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{E}\langle D^{2}F,DQ_{t}V\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}\,\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigl\langle DV,\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Bigl\langle DV,\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{-t}Q_{t}D^{2}F\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">The last line uses both the
commutation and self-adjointness statements in
(<a href="#A3.E6" title="Equation C.6 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>). All integrals can first be taken over
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\varepsilon,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\varepsilon,T]</annotation></semantics></math>; the limit follows from
(<a href="#A3.E16" title="Equation C.16 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.16</span></a>) and from the integrable
factor <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}\coloneqq q/(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}\coloneqq q/(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q^{*}-1)^{-1}=q-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q^{*}-1)^{-1}=q-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Apply
(<a href="#A3.E10" title="Equation C.10 ‣ Lemma C.2 (Second-order Gaussian Riesz estimate). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.10</span></a>) at exponent <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and use
Hölder’s inequality in
(<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation C.17 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.17</span></a>) to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\mathbb{E}\langle F,\delta_{\gamma}V\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\bigr|\leqslant C\,(q-1)^{2}\,\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q^{*}}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\mathbb{E}\langle F,\delta_{\gamma}V\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\bigr|\leqslant C\,(q-1)^{2}\,\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q^{*}}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Duality between <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q^{*}}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q^{*}}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math> therefore yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\,(q-1)^{2}\,\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\qquad\text{if }\mathbb{E}V=0\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\,(q-1)^{2}\,\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\qquad\text{if }\mathbb{E}V=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a general <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, apply
(<a href="#A3.E18" title="Equation C.18 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.18</span></a>) to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V-\mathbb{E}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V-\mathbb{E}V</annotation></semantics></math>. The
remaining term is
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\gamma}(\mathbb{E}V)(x)=\sum_{j\in[d]}x_{j}\,(\mathbb{E}V)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\gamma}(\mathbb{E}V)(x)=\sum_{j\in[d]}x_{j}\,(\mathbb{E}V)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. The map
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto\delta_{\gamma}(\mathbb{E}V)(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto\delta_{\gamma}(\mathbb{E}V)(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a centered
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued Gaussian random vector whose <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> norm
is <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathbb{E}V\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathbb{E}V\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The standard equivalence of Gaussian
moments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, Corollary 3.2]</cite> therefore gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\gamma}(\mathbb{E}V)\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert\mathbb{E}V\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\gamma}(\mathbb{E}V)\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert\mathbb{E}V\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A3.E18" title="Equation C.18 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.18</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation C.19 ‣ Proof. ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.19</span></a>) proves
(<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.3 (Gaussian Sobolev inequalities). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">The calculation above applies first to smooth fields. The derivative is
closable and smooth cylindrical fields are dense in the Gaussian
Sobolev norm by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, Proposition 1.2.1]</cite>, so a standard approximation argument extends the proof to vector fields in <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{1,q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{1,q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, the last sentence follows from rescaling.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dual Poincaré inequality.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a centered, finite-dimensional Hilbert-valued <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in L^{2}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in L^{2}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert F\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\coloneqq\sup\bigl\{\mathbb{E}\langle F,H\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}:\mathbb{E}H=0,\quad\lVert DH\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant 1\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.889em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>H</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert F\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\coloneqq\sup\bigl\{\mathbb{E}\langle F,H\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}:\mathbb{E}H=0,\quad\lVert DH\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant 1\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We then have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert F\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}=\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert F\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}=\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The following is the dual form of the Gaussian Poincaré inequality, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Dual Gaussian Poincaré inequality)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all such <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert F\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant\lVert F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert F\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant\lVert F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Heat equation estimates.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For later reference, let <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})_{t\geqslant 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})_{t\geqslant 0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Euclidean heat
semigroup,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t}F)(x)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t}F)(x)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}P_{t}F=\frac{1}{2}\Delta P_{t}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}P_{t}F=\frac{1}{2}\Delta P_{t}F</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is weakly
differentiable, differentiation commutes with the heat semigroup, whereas
Gaussian integration by parts gives the derivative formula</p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DP_{t}F(x)=P_{t}(DF)(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{t}}\,\mathbb{E}[F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)\otimes G]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DP_{t}F(x)=P_{t}(DF)(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{t}}\,\mathbb{E}[F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)\otimes G]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In particular, Jensen and Bessel’s inequality give</p>
<table id="A3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert DP_{t}F(x)\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert DP_{t}F(x)\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\operatorname{Lip}(F)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\operatorname{Lip}(F)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert DP_{t}F(x)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert DP_{t}F(x)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{1}{t}\inf_{a\in\mathcal{H}}\mathbb{E}\lVert F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)-a\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{1}{t}\inf_{a\in\mathcal{H}}\mathbb{E}\lVert F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)-a\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">To justify the second estimate, fix <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and put</p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\coloneqq F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)-a\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\coloneqq F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)-a\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">The orthogonal projection of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in L^{2}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in L^{2}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})</annotation></semantics></math> onto the
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued first Gaussian chaos is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{1}Y\coloneqq\sum_{i\in[d]}G_{i}\,\mathbb{E}[G_{i}Y]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{1}Y\coloneqq\sum_{i\in[d]}G_{i}\,\mathbb{E}[G_{i}Y]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Since the coordinate functions <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G_{i})_{i\in[d]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G_{i})_{i\in[d]}</annotation></semantics></math> are orthonormal in
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, Bessel’s inequality gives</p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in[d]}\lVert\mathbb{E}[G_{i}Y]\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}=\mathbb{E}\lVert\mathcal{P}_{1}Y\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\leqslant\mathbb{E}\lVert Y\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in[d]}\lVert\mathbb{E}[G_{i}Y]\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}=\mathbb{E}\lVert\mathcal{P}_{1}Y\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\leqslant\mathbb{E}\lVert Y\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Moreover, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[a\otimes G]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[a\otimes G]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so
(<a href="#A3.E20" title="Equation C.20 ‣ Heat equation estimates. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.20</span></a>) and the preceding display imply</p>
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\,\lVert DP_{t}F(x)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}=\sum_{i\in[d]}\lVert\mathbb{E}[G_{i}Y]\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\leqslant\mathbb{E}\lVert F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)-a\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\,\lVert DP_{t}F(x)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}=\sum_{i\in[d]}\lVert\mathbb{E}[G_{i}Y]\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\leqslant\mathbb{E}\lVert F(x+\sqrt{t}\,G)-a\rVert_{\mathcal{H}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Taking the infimum over <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> proves
(<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation C.21 ‣ Heat equation estimates. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.21</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For random variables <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1},\ldots,F_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1},\ldots,F_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> whose joint moment-generating
function is finite near the origin, define their joint cumulant by</p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{Cum}(F_{1},\ldots,F_{k})\coloneqq\biggl.\partial_{t_{1}}\cdots\partial_{t_{k}}\log\mathbb{E}\exp\Bigl\{\sum_{j=1}^{k}t_{j}F_{j}\Bigr\}\biggr|_{t_{1}=\cdots=t_{k}=0}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cum</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cum}(F_{1},\ldots,F_{k})\coloneqq\biggl.\partial_{t_{1}}\cdots\partial_{t_{k}}\log\mathbb{E}\exp\Bigl\{\sum_{j=1}^{k}t_{j}F_{j}\Bigr\}\biggr|_{t_{1}=\cdots=t_{k}=0}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is vector-valued, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Cum</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the
symmetric <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-tensor obtained by applying this definition to linear
functionals of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We record the connection with derivatives of the smoothed potential. Let
<math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{y}\sim R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{y}\sim R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set</p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\eta}(y)\coloneqq\int\exp\Bigl\{-V(x)-\frac{\lVert x\rVert^{2}}{2\eta}+\frac{\langle y,x\rangle}{\eta}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}x\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\eta}(y)\coloneqq\int\exp\Bigl\{-V(x)-\frac{\lVert x\rVert^{2}}{2\eta}+\frac{\langle y,x\rangle}{\eta}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}x\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Up to an additive constant,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\eta}(y)=\frac{\lVert y\rVert^{2}}{2\eta}-\log Z_{\eta}(y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\eta}(y)=\frac{\lVert y\rVert^{2}}{2\eta}-\log Z_{\eta}(y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log Z_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log Z_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cumulant-generating function of the exponential
family <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, differentiation gives, for every <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)=\mathbf{1}_{\{k=2\}}\,\eta^{-1}I-\eta^{-k}\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X_{y})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Cum</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)=\mathbf{1}_{\{k=2\}}\,\eta^{-1}I-\eta^{-k}\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X_{y})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We need the following recursive representation of cumulants.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Iterated Gaussian covariance)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1},\ldots,F_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1},\ldots,F_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be smooth scalar functions of a standard Gaussian,
with bounded derivatives of every positive order. Define</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma_{1}(F_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma_{1}(F_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq F_{1}-\mathbb{E}F_{1}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq F_{1}-\mathbb{E}F_{1}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma_{j}(F_{1},\ldots,F_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma_{j}(F_{1},\ldots,F_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\langle DF_{j},D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}\Gamma_{j-1}(F_{1},\ldots,F_{j-1})\rangle\,,\quad j\geqslant 2\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\langle DF_{j},D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}\Gamma_{j-1}(F_{1},\ldots,F_{j-1})\rangle\,,\quad j\geqslant 2\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cum}(F_{1},\ldots,F_{k})=\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{k-1}}\mathbb{E}\Gamma_{k}(F_{1},F_{\pi(2)},\ldots,F_{\pi(k)})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cum</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cum}(F_{1},\ldots,F_{k})=\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{k-1}}\mathbb{E}\Gamma_{k}(F_{1},F_{\pi(2)},\ldots,F_{\pi(k)})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where each permutation is over <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2,\dotsc,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2,\dotsc,k\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is a symmetrized form of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, Theorem 4.4]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Cumulants of a near-identity Gaussian image)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz and, almost everywhere,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert DT\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant 1\,,\qquad\lVert DT-I\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\,,\qquad 0\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\leqslant 1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert DT\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant 1\,,\qquad\lVert DT-I\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\,,\qquad 0\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\leqslant 1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is standard Gaussian, then, for every <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\lVert v\rVert=1}\,\lVert\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(T(G))[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Cum</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\lVert v\rVert=1}\,\lVert\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(T(G))[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant 2\,(k-1)!\,\varepsilon_{T}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant 2\,(k-1)!\,\varepsilon_{T}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(T(G))\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cum</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(T(G))\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant 2\,(k-1)!\,\varepsilon_{T}\sqrt{d}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant 2\,(k-1)!\,\varepsilon_{T}\sqrt{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A[v,\cdot^{k-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[v,\cdot^{k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-tensor obtained by fixing
the first argument of a <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-tensor <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, leaving the remaining
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-1</annotation></semantics></math> arguments free. In particular,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert A[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}=\sum_{j_{2},\ldots,j_{k}\in[d]}\bigl|A[v,e_{j_{2}},\ldots,e_{j_{k}}]\bigr|^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert A[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}=\sum_{j_{2},\ldots,j_{k}\in[d]}\bigl|A[v,e_{j_{2}},\ldots,e_{j_{k}}]\bigr|^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(e_{j})_{j\in[d]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(e_{j})_{j\in[d]}</annotation></semantics></math> is any orthonormal basis of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">First take <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> smooth.
For fixed <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, define the <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-tensor
<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{j}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{j}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\Gamma_{j}(v)]_{i_{2},\ldots,i_{j}}\coloneqq\Gamma_{j}\bigl(\langle v,T(G)\rangle,T_{i_{2}}(G),\ldots,T_{i_{j}}(G)\bigr)\,,\qquad i_{2},\ldots,i_{j}\in[d]\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\Gamma_{j}(v)]_{i_{2},\ldots,i_{j}}\coloneqq\Gamma_{j}\bigl(\langle v,T(G)\rangle,T_{i_{2}}(G),\ldots,T_{i_{j}}(G)\bigr)\,,\qquad i_{2},\ldots,i_{j}\in[d]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">using the scalar recursion (<a href="#A3.E23" title="Equation C.23 ‣ Lemma C.5 (Iterated Gaussian covariance). ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.23</span></a>).
For <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=2</annotation></semantics></math>, its <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry is
<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle DT_{i}(G),D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T(G)\rangle)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle DT_{i}(G),D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T(G)\rangle)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>,
so collecting the entries gives
<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{2}(v)=DT(G)\,D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T(G)\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{2}(v)=DT(G)\,D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T(G)\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v,G\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v,G\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to the first Wiener chaos, so
<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,G\rangle)=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,G\rangle)=v</annotation></semantics></math>.
Subtracting this linear contribution yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\Gamma_{2}(v)-v\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\Gamma_{2}(v)-v\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert(DT-I)\,v\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}+\bigl\lVert DT\,\bigl(D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T\rangle)-v\bigr)\bigr\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert(DT-I)\,v\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}+\bigl\lVert DT\,\bigl(D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T\rangle)-v\bigr)\bigr\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert+\lVert DT\,D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T-I\rangle)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert+\lVert DT\,D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T-I\rangle)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert+\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T-I\rangle)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert+\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}(\langle v,T-I\rangle)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert+\lVert\langle v,T-I\rangle\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma)}\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert+\lVert D\langle v,T-I\rangle\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\leqslant 2\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert+\lVert\langle v,T-I\rangle\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma)}\leqslant\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert+\lVert D\langle v,T-I\rangle\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\leqslant 2\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we applied <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Dual Gaussian Poincaré inequality). ‣ Dual Poincaré inequality. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a> and the Gaussian Poincaré inequality.
This implies</span></p>
<table id="A3.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\Gamma_{2}(v)-\mathbb{E}\Gamma_{2}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant 2\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\Gamma_{2}(v)-\mathbb{E}\Gamma_{2}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant 2\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, collect the free indices into a tensor. Then, <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a
contraction of <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DT" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DT</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}\Gamma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}\Gamma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>; hence, by <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert DT\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert DT\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Dual Gaussian Poincaré inequality). ‣ Dual Poincaré inequality. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\Gamma_{j+1}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}\Gamma_{j}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}=\lVert\Gamma_{j}(v)\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\lVert\Gamma_{j}(v)-\mathbb{E}\Gamma_{j}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖮𝖴</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\Gamma_{j+1}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\lVert D(-\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{OU}})^{-1}\Gamma_{j}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}=\lVert\Gamma_{j}(v)\rVert_{\dot{H}^{-1}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\lVert\Gamma_{j}(v)-\mathbb{E}\Gamma_{j}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Starting from (<a href="#A3.E25" title="Equation C.25 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.25</span></a>) thus gives
<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\Gamma_{k}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant 2\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\Gamma_{k}(v)\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant 2\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert</annotation></semantics></math> for every ordering.
Thus <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma C.5 (Iterated Gaussian covariance). ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>, Minkowski, and Jensen imply</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(T(G))[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{k-1}}\lVert\mathbb{E}\Gamma_{k}^{\pi}(v)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant 2\,(k-1)!\,\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Cum</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">⩽</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">!</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(T(G))[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{k-1}}\lVert\mathbb{E}\Gamma_{k}^{\pi}(v)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant 2\,(k-1)!\,\varepsilon_{T}\,\lVert v\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Squaring and summing over an orthonormal basis proves
(<a href="#A3.E24" title="Equation C.24 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Cumulants of a near-identity Gaussian image). ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.24</span></a>). A standard approximation argument extends the bound to locally Lipschitz <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proofs of the second-order Wasserstein estimates</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By approximation, it is enough to treat smooth <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>. Throughout the
proof, for functions of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z,w)</annotation></semantics></math>, super- or sub-scripts <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> indicate operations in the first and second
arguments, respectively. Thus, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{s}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{s}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the heat semigroup in the
second argument, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are the corresponding derivatives,
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is Gaussian row divergence in the first argument under
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{N}(0,I_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{N}(0,I_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{2,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{2,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is Gaussian row divergence in the
second argument under <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{N}(0,tI_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{N}(0,tI_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let
<math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{t})_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{t})_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}</annotation></semantics></math> be Brownian motion in <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of
<math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}(z,w)\coloneqq P_{1-t}^{(2)}f(z,\cdot)(w)\,,\qquad X_{t}\coloneqq Z+u_{t}(Z,W_{t})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}(z,w)\coloneqq P_{1-t}^{(2)}f(z,\cdot)(w)\,,\qquad X_{t}\coloneqq Z+u_{t}(Z,W_{t})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}=Z+\bar{f}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}=Z+\bar{f}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has the law of <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z+f(Z,G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z+f(Z,G)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Writing <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{t}^{W})_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{t}^{W})_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}</annotation></semantics></math> for the Brownian filtration, the Markov property
gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}(z,W_{t})=\mathbb{E}[f(z,W_{1})\mid\mathcal{F}_{t}^{W}]\,,\qquad(0\leqslant t\leqslant 1)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}(z,W_{t})=\mathbb{E}[f(z,W_{1})\mid\mathcal{F}_{t}^{W}]\,,\qquad(0\leqslant t\leqslant 1)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t})_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t})_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale with respect to the enlarged
filtration <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma(Z)\vee\mathcal{F}_{t}^{W})_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>W</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma(Z)\vee\mathcal{F}_{t}^{W})_{0\leqslant t\leqslant 1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>
solves the backward heat equation with respect to <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>,
Itô’s formula identifies its martingale representation as</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}X_{t}=D_{2}u_{t}(Z,W_{t})\,\mathrm{d}W_{t}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}X_{t}=D_{2}u_{t}(Z,W_{t})\,\mathrm{d}W_{t}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}(z,w)\coloneqq D_{2}u_{t}(z,w)D_{2}u_{t}(z,w)^{\mathsf{T}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}(z,w)\coloneqq D_{2}u_{t}(z,w)D_{2}u_{t}(z,w)^{\mathsf{T}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">A second application of Itô’s formula gives, for any smooth scalar test
function <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}\,\mathbb{E}\varphi(X_{t})=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\langle\Sigma_{t}(Z,W_{t}),D^{2}\varphi(X_{t})\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}\,\mathbb{E}\varphi(X_{t})=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\langle\Sigma_{t}(Z,W_{t}),D^{2}\varphi(X_{t})\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">To estimate the Wasserstein distance, we recast this as a continuity equation. The chain rule gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{1}\nabla\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{1}\nabla\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D^{2}\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\,(I+D_{1}u_{t}(z,w))\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D^{2}\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\,(I+D_{1}u_{t}(z,w))\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{2}\nabla\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{2}\nabla\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D^{2}\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\,D_{2}u_{t}(z,w)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D^{2}\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\,D_{2}u_{t}(z,w)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> are symmetric, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\Sigma_{t}(z,w),D^{2}\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\Sigma_{t}(z,w),D^{2}\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad={}\langle\Sigma_{t}(z,w),D_{1}\nabla\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\rangle-\langle D_{1}u_{t}(z,w)\,D_{2}u_{t}(z,w),D_{2}\nabla\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\rangle\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad={}\langle\Sigma_{t}(z,w),D_{1}\nabla\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\rangle-\langle D_{1}u_{t}(z,w)\,D_{2}u_{t}(z,w),D_{2}\nabla\varphi(z+u_{t}(z,w))\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Here and in the sequel, all derivatives of <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
are understood as evaluated at <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z,W_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z,W_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying the divergence adjoint identity
(<a href="#A3.E1" title="Equation C.1 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) in each Gaussian variable gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\langle\Sigma_{t},D^{2}\varphi(X_{t})\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}=\mathbb{E}\langle\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}-\delta_{2,t}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t}),\nabla\varphi(X_{t})\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\langle\Sigma_{t},D^{2}\varphi(X_{t})\rangle_{\mathrm{HS}}=\mathbb{E}\langle\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}-\delta_{2,t}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t}),\nabla\varphi(X_{t})\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}\mathbb{E}\varphi(X_{t})=\mathbb{E}\langle V_{t},\nabla\varphi(X_{t})\rangle\,,\qquad V_{t}\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\{\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}-\delta_{2,t}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}\mathbb{E}\varphi(X_{t})=\mathbb{E}\langle V_{t},\nabla\varphi(X_{t})\rangle\,,\qquad V_{t}\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\{\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}-\delta_{2,t}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, the evolution of <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\law(LX_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\law(LX_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the continuity equation</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}\law(LX_{t})+\operatorname{div}\bigl(v_{t}\law(LX_{t})\bigr)=0\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}\law(LX_{t})+\operatorname{div}\bigl(v_{t}\law(LX_{t})\bigr)=0\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">where the velocity field is given by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}(y)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[LV_{t}\mid LX_{t}=y]\,,\qquad\lVert v_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\lVert LV_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}(y)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[LV_{t}\mid LX_{t}=y]\,,\qquad\lVert v_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\lVert LV_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to estimate this explicit velocity. The heat semigroup preserves
the first derivative bounds, while (<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation C.21 ‣ Heat equation estimates. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.21</span></a>) applied
to the weak derivatives of <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> gives the following bounds:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert D_{1}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert D_{1}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant A\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant A\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert D_{2}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert D_{2}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant B\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant B\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert D_{1}D_{2}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\vee\lVert D_{2}D_{1}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert D_{1}D_{2}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\vee\lVert D_{2}D_{1}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{A\sqrt{m}}{\sqrt{1-t}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{A\sqrt{m}}{\sqrt{1-t}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert D_{2}^{2}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert D_{2}^{2}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{B\sqrt{m}}{\sqrt{1-t}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{B\sqrt{m}}{\sqrt{1-t}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here, we used
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert D_{1}f\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert D_{1}f\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,A</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert D_{2}f\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert D_{2}f\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,B</annotation></semantics></math>. The product rule and
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert RS\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\lVert R\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,\lVert S\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert RS\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant\lVert R\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,\lVert S\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math> therefore give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant B^{2}\sqrt{m}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant B^{2}\sqrt{m}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert D_{1}\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert D_{1}\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2AB\sqrt{m}}{\sqrt{1-t}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2AB\sqrt{m}}{\sqrt{1-t}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t}\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant AB\sqrt{m}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant AB\sqrt{m}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert D_{2}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert D_{2}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2AB\sqrt{m}}{\sqrt{1-t}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\frac{2AB\sqrt{m}}{\sqrt{1-t}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Every column of <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{2}u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{range}(\Sigma_{t})\subseteq E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{range}(\Sigma_{t})\subseteq E</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed linear subspace,
differentiating the columns of <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> preserves membership
in <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}\in E</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now apply the Gaussian divergence bounds conditionally in each
variable. First,
(<a href="#A3.E2" title="Equation C.2 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) in the <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-variable gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert L\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert L\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lVert\delta_{1}(L\Sigma_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\lVert L\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}(\mathrm{HS})}+\lVert LD_{1}\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}(\mathrm{HS})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lVert\delta_{1}(L\Sigma_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\lVert L\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}(\mathrm{HS})}+\lVert LD_{1}\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}(\mathrm{HS})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\Bigl\{\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+2\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,\frac{AB}{\sqrt{1-t}}\Bigr\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\Bigl\{\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+2\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,\frac{AB}{\sqrt{1-t}}\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here we used <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\Sigma_{t}=L\Pi_{E}\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\Sigma_{t}=L\Pi_{E}\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in the first term. Next,
the estimate
(<a href="#A3.E3" title="Equation C.3 ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>) in the <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>-variable gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert L\delta_{2,t}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert L\delta_{2,t}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={}\lVert\delta_{2,t}(LD_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={}\lVert\delta_{2,t}(LD_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant t^{-1/2}\,\lVert LD_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}(\mathrm{HS})}+\lVert LD_{2}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}(\mathrm{HS})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant t^{-1/2}\,\lVert LD_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}(\mathrm{HS})}+\lVert LD_{2}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}(\mathrm{HS})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,\{t^{-1/2}+2\,(1-t)^{-1/2}\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,\{t^{-1/2}+2\,(1-t)^{-1/2}\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these two estimates in the definition of <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert LV_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,t^{-1/2}+2\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,(1-t)^{-1/2}\Bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert LV_{t}\rVert_{L^{2}}\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,t^{-1/2}+2\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,(1-t)^{-1/2}\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">The first singularity comes from rescaling Gaussian divergence under
<math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{N}(0,tI_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{N}(0,tI_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second from differentiating the heat extension.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}t^{-1/2}\,\mathrm{d}t=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)^{-1/2}\,\mathrm{d}t=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}t^{-1/2}\,\mathrm{d}t=\int_{0}^{1}(1-t)^{-1/2}\,\mathrm{d}t=2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{2}(\law(LX_{\varepsilon}),\law(LX_{1-\varepsilon}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{2}(\law(LX_{\varepsilon}),\law(LX_{1-\varepsilon}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{\varepsilon}^{1-\varepsilon}\lVert v_{t}(LX_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}}\,\mathrm{d}t\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+5\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\Bigr\}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\int_{\varepsilon}^{1-\varepsilon}\lVert v_{t}(LX_{t})\rVert_{L^{2}}\,\mathrm{d}t\leqslant\sqrt{m}\,\Bigl\{\frac{1}{2}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+5\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\Bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">We can then let <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\searrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>↘</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\searrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves
(<a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 4.21 ‣ Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.21</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5.5 (Second-order 𝑊_𝑞 estimate). ‣ 5.3.1 Variance bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Use the notation and repeat the proof of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma 4.11 (Second-order 𝑊_2 estimate). ‣ 4.4.2 Variance bound ‣ 4.4 Local error bounds ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.11</span></a> through the construction of
<math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t},X_{t},\Sigma_{t},V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t},X_{t},\Sigma_{t},V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, including all the displayed
pointwise derivative estimates. Conditional expectation is now used as
an <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction. Applying
(<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.3 (Gaussian Sobolev inequalities). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>) conditionally in the <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-variable,
and retaining separately its mean and derivative terms, gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert L\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{m}\,\bigl\{\sqrt{q}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+q^{2}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,(1-t)^{-1/2}\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert L\delta_{1}\Sigma_{t}\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{m}\,\bigl\{\sqrt{q}\,\lVert L\Pi_{E}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,B^{2}+q^{2}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,(1-t)^{-1/2}\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Its rescaled version in the <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>-variable similarly gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert L\delta_{2,t}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{m}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,\bigl\{\sqrt{q}\,t^{-1/2}+q^{2}\,(1-t)^{-1/2}\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>L</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert L\delta_{2,t}(D_{1}u_{t}D_{2}u_{t})\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{m}\,\lVert L\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\,AB\,\bigl\{\sqrt{q}\,t^{-1/2}+q^{2}\,(1-t)^{-1/2}\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating these bounds proves
(<a href="#S5.E4" title="Equation 5.4 ‣ Lemma 5.5 (Second-order 𝑊_𝑞 estimate). ‣ 5.3.1 Variance bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Gaussian polynomial bounds</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For this subsection, <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the gradient in <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the
Gaussian divergence is the operator defined above with <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by
<math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.7</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gaussian polynomial estimates)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer. If <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial of total
degree at most <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\sqrt{r}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>r</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\sqrt{r}\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial vector field of total degree
at most <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\leqslant\sqrt{r+1}\,\lVert V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>V</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\leqslant\sqrt{r+1}\,\lVert V\rVert_{L^{2}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These estimates are standard; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, Propositions 1.2.2 and 1.3.1]</cite>, restricting to Wiener chaoses of degree at
most <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also need <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> versions of these inequalities. We remark that the constants below are likely not sharp.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.8</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> Gaussian polynomial estimates)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer. If
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial of total degree at most <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant Cr\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant Cr\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{H}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial vector field of total degree
at most <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\,(\sqrt{q}+q^{2}r)\,\lVert V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>V</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}\leqslant C\,(\sqrt{q}+q^{2}r)\,\lVert V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In this proof, we allow <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> to be infinite-dimensional.
Write</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F(p)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}\\
|\alpha|\leqslant r\end{subarray}}a_{\alpha}p^{\alpha}\,,\qquad a_{\alpha}\in\mathcal{H}\,,\qquad\mathcal{H}_{F}\coloneqq\operatorname{span}\{a_{\alpha}:\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d},\ |\alpha|\leqslant r\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>span</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">⩽</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(p)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}\\
|\alpha|\leqslant r\end{subarray}}a_{\alpha}p^{\alpha}\,,\qquad a_{\alpha}\in\mathcal{H}\,,\qquad\mathcal{H}_{F}\coloneqq\operatorname{span}\{a_{\alpha}:\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d},\ |\alpha|\leqslant r\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The space <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite-dimensional, and both <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DF" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DF</annotation></semantics></math> take
values in <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="A3.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{F}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I_{\mathcal{H}_{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{F}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I_{\mathcal{H}_{F}})</annotation></semantics></math>, independently of <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote its
law by <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Viewed as an <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued Gaussian,
<math id="A3.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> has covariance <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathcal{H}_{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{H}_{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is finite rank and hence
trace class.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For every fixed <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\lVert D\langle G_{F},F\rangle(p)\rVert^{2}=\sum_{j\in[d]}\mathbb{E}\bigl|\langle G_{F},\partial_{j}F(p)\rangle\bigr|^{2}=\sum_{j\in[d]}\lVert\partial_{j}F(p)\rVert^{2}=\lVert DF(p)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\lVert D\langle G_{F},F\rangle(p)\rVert^{2}=\sum_{j\in[d]}\mathbb{E}\bigl|\langle G_{F},\partial_{j}F(p)\rangle\bigr|^{2}=\sum_{j\in[d]}\lVert\partial_{j}F(p)\rVert^{2}=\lVert DF(p)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\lVert D\langle G_{F},F\rangle\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma\otimes\gamma_{F})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant\lVert D\langle G_{F},F\rangle\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma\otimes\gamma_{F})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, the Gaussian moment bound gives, pointwise in <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(\mathbb{E}\bigl|\langle G_{F},F(p)\rangle\bigr|^{q}\bigr)^{1/q}\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert F(p)\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\mathbb{E}\bigl|\langle G_{F},F(p)\rangle\bigr|^{q}\bigr)^{1/q}\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert F(p)\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">The dimension-free Gaussian Bernstein–Markov inequality of
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, Proposition 5]</cite>, applied conditionally on <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> to the
scalar polynomial <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\mapsto\langle G_{F},F(p)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\mapsto\langle G_{F},F(p)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, therefore yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert DF\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert D\langle G_{F},F\rangle\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma\otimes\gamma_{F})}\leqslant\frac{Cr}{\sqrt{q+1}}\,\lVert\langle G_{F},F\rangle\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma\otimes\gamma_{F})}\leqslant Cr\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert D\langle G_{F},F\rangle\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma\otimes\gamma_{F})}\leqslant\frac{Cr}{\sqrt{q+1}}\,\lVert\langle G_{F},F\rangle\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma\otimes\gamma_{F})}\leqslant Cr\,\lVert F\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma)}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">This proves (<a href="#A3.E26" title="Equation C.26 ‣ Lemma C.8 (𝐿^𝑞 Gaussian polynomial estimates). ‣ C.4 Gaussian polynomial bounds ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.26</span></a>) for an arbitrary
Hilbert space <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the divergence estimate, write</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{j}(p)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}\\
|\alpha|\leqslant r\end{subarray}}a_{\alpha,j}p^{\alpha}\,,\qquad j\in[d]\,,\qquad\mathcal{H}_{V}\coloneqq\operatorname{span}\{a_{\alpha,j}:\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d},\ |\alpha|\leqslant r,\ j\in[d]\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>span</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">⩽</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{j}(p)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}\\
|\alpha|\leqslant r\end{subarray}}a_{\alpha,j}p^{\alpha}\,,\qquad j\in[d]\,,\qquad\mathcal{H}_{V}\coloneqq\operatorname{span}\{a_{\alpha,j}:\alpha\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d},\ |\alpha|\leqslant r,\ j\in[d]\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">All quantities involving <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> take values in the finite-dimensional
spaces generated by <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma C.3 (Gaussian Sobolev inequalities). ‣ Derivative and divergence inequalities. ‣ C.1 Basic inequalities and heat smoothing ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> applies with target <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using Jensen’s inequality and
(<a href="#A3.E26" title="Equation C.26 ‣ Lemma C.8 (𝐿^𝑞 Gaussian polynomial estimates). ‣ C.4 Gaussian polynomial bounds ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.26</span></a>) with target <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{V}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{V}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we
obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\delta_{\gamma}V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathcal{H})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert\mathbb{E}V\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}+Cq^{2}\,\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant C\,(\sqrt{q}+q^{2}r)\,\lVert V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>q</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>V</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HS</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant C\sqrt{q}\,\lVert\mathbb{E}V\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}+Cq^{2}\,\lVert DV\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\leqslant C\,(\sqrt{q}+q^{2}r)\,\lVert V\rVert_{L^{q}(\gamma;\mathrm{HS})}\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Approximate proximal queries</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math>, an
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate proximal query at <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> returns a
measurable point <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="A4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\widetilde{x}_{y}-\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\widetilde{x}_{y}-\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Given such a query and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta,\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}(y;G)\coloneqq\nabla V(\widetilde{x}_{y}+\sqrt{\eta}\,G)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta,\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}(y;G)\coloneqq\nabla V(\widetilde{x}_{y}+\sqrt{\eta}\,G)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The approximate proximal variant of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Algorithm 3.1 (Smoothed Picard HMC). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> replaces every
occurrence of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta,\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta,\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (𝑊_𝑞 guarantee). ‣ 5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> in the main text assumes exact
proximal queries. We now record the modifications needed when these calls
are replaced by the approximate proximal queries from
(<a href="#A4.E1" title="Equation D.1 ‣ D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For every queried center <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the output of an
abstract <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate proximal oracle, and let
<math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}^{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}^{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the resulting kernel.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stability under approximate proximal centers)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K}^{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}\,,\delta_{z}\widehat{K})\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm prox}\coloneqq C\Lambda_{J}h\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,,\qquad q\geqslant 1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}(\delta_{z}\widehat{K}^{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}\,,\delta_{z}\widehat{K})\leqslant\mathcal{E}_{\rm prox}\coloneqq C\Lambda_{J}h\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,,\qquad q\geqslant 1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leqslant c/(\kappa\,(q+\log J))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leqslant c/(\kappa\,(q+\log J))</annotation></semantics></math>, and every phase-space law <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}(\widehat{K}^{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}})^{N},\Pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu}(\widehat{K}^{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}})^{N},\Pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant e^{-cNh/\kappa}\,W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+\frac{C\kappa q}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa^{2}}{h^{2}}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{\rm prox}^{2})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>var</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>bias</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>disc</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>prox</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant e^{-cNh/\kappa}\,W_{q,M_{\kappa}}^{2}(\widehat{\mu},\Pi_{\eta})+\frac{C\kappa q}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{{\rm var},q}^{2}+\frac{C\kappa^{2}}{h^{2}}\,(\mathcal{E}_{{\rm bias}}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{{\rm disc},q}^{2}+\mathcal{E}_{\rm prox}^{2})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the same Gaussian <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> in the stochastic gradient, <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness and
(<a href="#A4.E1" title="Equation D.1 ‣ D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>) imply</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(\widetilde{x}_{y}+\sqrt{\eta}G)-\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}G)\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(\widetilde{x}_{y}+\sqrt{\eta}G)-\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}G)\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The first stochastic gradient block therefore moves every Picard node by at most
<math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The error in the second block
stochastic gradient is at most
<math id="A4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}+h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}+h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields position error at most
<math id="A4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math> and momentum error at most
<math id="A4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ch\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ch\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving
(<a href="#A4.E2" title="Equation D.2 ‣ Lemma D.1 (Stability under approximate proximal centers). ‣ D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>).
Then, (<a href="#A4.E3" title="Equation D.3 ‣ Lemma D.1 (Stability under approximate proximal centers). ‣ D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>) by
applying the triangle inequality and Young’s inequality in the one-step recurrence
(<a href="#S5.E2" title="Equation 5.2 ‣ Theorem 5.4 (Local error analysis in 𝑊_𝑞). ‣ 5.2 𝑊_𝑞 local error analysis ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For the gradient-only implementation, set</p>
<table id="A4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\coloneqq c\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{-4}\sqrt{d}\,h^{3}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\coloneqq c\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{-4}\sqrt{d}\,h^{3}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Since
<math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\rm prox}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\rm prox}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\kappa}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm prox}\leqslant C\kappa\Lambda_{J}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{9}\kappa\sqrt{d+q}\,h^{3}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>9</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\kappa}{h}\,\mathcal{E}_{\rm prox}\leqslant C\kappa\Lambda_{J}\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{9}\kappa\sqrt{d+q}\,h^{3}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Thus (<a href="#A4.E3" title="Equation D.3 ‣ Lemma D.1 (Stability under approximate proximal centers). ‣ D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>) gives the same
conclusion as the exact proximal proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (𝑊_𝑞 guarantee). ‣ 5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Gradient-only implementation</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Picard HMC algorithm in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Algorithm 3.1 (Smoothed Picard HMC). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> is stated using exact
proximal queries, and <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> introduces its
<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate variant. This subsection implements every
such approximate query using only evaluations of the gradient.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a potential <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying
<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>, a smoothing variance
<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant c_{0}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and a center <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{y}^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{y}^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_algorithm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gradient descent)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(0)}\coloneqq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(0)}\coloneqq y</annotation></semantics></math> and
iterate</p>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x^{(k+1)}\coloneqq y-\eta\nabla V(x^{(k)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(k+1)}\coloneqq y-\eta\nabla V(x^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">until</p>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert x^{(k+1)}-x^{(k)}\rVert\leqslant(1-\eta)\,\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x^{(k+1)}-x^{(k)}\rVert\leqslant(1-\eta)\,\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Return <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}_{y}\coloneqq x^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}_{y}\coloneqq x^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Certificate and pointwise work)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The iteration in <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Algorithm D.2 (Gradient descent). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> stops after finitely many steps
and satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\widetilde{x}_{y}-x_{y}^{+}\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\widetilde{x}_{y}-x_{y}^{+}\rVert\leqslant\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Its number <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{prox}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{prox}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> of gradient evaluations obeys</span></p>
<table id="A4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{prox}}(y)\leqslant C_{c_{0}}\,\Bigl[1+\log\Bigl(1+\frac{\lVert\nabla V(y)\rVert}{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}\Bigr)\Bigr]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{prox}}(y)\leqslant C_{c_{0}}\,\Bigl[1+\log\Bigl(1+\frac{\lVert\nabla V(y)\rVert}{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}\Bigr)\Bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The map <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T_{y}\coloneqq y-\eta\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{y}\coloneqq y-\eta\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-contraction, and its
unique fixed point is <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{y}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{y}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert x^{(k)}-x_{y}^{+}\rVert\leqslant\sum_{j=k}^{\infty}\,\lVert x^{(j+1)}-x^{(j)}\rVert\leqslant\frac{\lVert x^{(k+1)}-x^{(k)}\rVert}{1-\eta}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.111em">⩽</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x^{(k)}-x_{y}^{+}\rVert\leqslant\sum_{j=k}^{\infty}\,\lVert x^{(j+1)}-x^{(j)}\rVert\leqslant\frac{\lVert x^{(k+1)}-x^{(k)}\rVert}{1-\eta}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the certificate is valid. Moreover, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert x^{(k+1)}-x^{(k)}\rVert\leqslant\eta^{k}\,\lVert x^{(1)}-x^{(0)}\rVert=\eta^{k+1}\,\lVert\nabla V(y)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert x^{(k+1)}-x^{(k)}\rVert\leqslant\eta^{k}\,\lVert x^{(1)}-x^{(0)}\rVert=\eta^{k+1}\,\lVert\nabla V(y)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leqslant c_{0}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leqslant c_{0}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>
gives (<a href="#A4.E6" title="Equation D.6 ‣ Lemma D.3 (Certificate and pointwise work). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.6</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The pointwise bound depends on the queried center. To obtain the expected
complexity claimed by the gradient-only sampler, we record that the centers
encountered along the realized run have controlled second moments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expected work along the Picard HMC run)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the parameter choices in
(<a href="#S5.E12" title="Equation 5.12 ‣ Proof of . ‣ 5.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.12</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A4.E4" title="Equation D.4 ‣ D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>), assume
also that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\mathfrak{L}_{q}\leqslant c/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\mathfrak{L}_{q}\leqslant c/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leqslant c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leqslant c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and implement every
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate proximal query in
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Algorithm 3.1 (Smoothed Picard HMC). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> using
<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Algorithm D.2 (Gradient descent). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>. Every argument <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> supplied to this routine
obeys</span></p>
<table id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla V(Y)\rVert^{2}\leqslant C\kappa d\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{18}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>18</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla V(Y)\rVert^{2}\leqslant C\kappa d\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{18}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently the expected total number of gradient evaluations is at most</span></p>
<table id="A4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leqslant C\,\frac{\kappa}{h}\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{3}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}N_{\nabla V}\leqslant C\,\frac{\kappa}{h}\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{3}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> minimize <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. By
(<a href="#A4.E3" title="Equation D.3 ‣ Lemma D.1 (Stability under approximate proximal centers). ‣ D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>) with <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=2</annotation></semantics></math> and
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 4.16 (Initialization). ‣ 4.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.16</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{j\leqslant N}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\lVert X_{j}-x_{\star}\rVert^{2}+\lVert P_{j}\rVert^{2}\bigr]\leqslant C\kappa d\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{18}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi><mn>18</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{j\leqslant N}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\lVert X_{j}-x_{\star}\rVert^{2}+\lVert P_{j}\rVert^{2}\bigr]\leqslant C\kappa d\,\mathfrak{L}_{q}^{18}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">This also controls every layer <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> node. Since
<math id="A4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{x_{\star}}^{+}=x_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{x_{\star}}^{+}=x_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, non-expansiveness and
(<a href="#A4.E5" title="Equation D.5 ‣ Lemma D.3 (Certificate and pointwise work). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>) give
<math id="A4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\widetilde{x}_{Y}-x_{\star}\rVert\leqslant\lVert Y-x_{\star}\rVert+\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\widetilde{x}_{Y}-x_{\star}\rVert\leqslant\lVert Y-x_{\star}\rVert+\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>; hence <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness and Gaussian
second moments control the gradients used to form layer <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. The bound
<math id="A4.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{i\in[J]}\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{i\in[J]}\sum_{j\in[J]}|\omega_{i,j}|\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> then controls
every layer <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> node. Finally,
<math id="A4.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\nabla V(Y)\rVert\leqslant\lVert Y-x_{\star}\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla V(Y)\rVert\leqslant\lVert Y-x_{\star}\rVert</annotation></semantics></math> at either layer, proving
(<a href="#A4.E7" title="Equation D.7 ‣ Lemma D.4 (Expected work along the Picard HMC run). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.7</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Certificate and pointwise work). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> and Jensen’s inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}N_{\mathsf{prox}}(Y)\leqslant C\,\Bigl[1+\log\Bigl(1+\frac{(\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla V(Y)\rVert^{2})^{1/2}}{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}\Bigr)\Bigr]\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}N_{\mathsf{prox}}(Y)\leqslant C\,\Bigl[1+\log\Bigl(1+\frac{(\mathbb{E}\lVert\nabla V(Y)\rVert^{2})^{1/2}}{\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}}\Bigr)\Bigr]\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">There are <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2J</annotation></semantics></math> proximal and <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2J</annotation></semantics></math> direct gradient calls per phase.
Using <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\leqslant C\mathfrak{L}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leqslant C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}/h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔏</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leqslant C\kappa\mathfrak{L}_{q}/h</annotation></semantics></math> proves
(<a href="#A4.E8" title="Equation D.8 ‣ Lemma D.4 (Expected work along the Picard HMC run). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.8</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (𝑊_𝑞 guarantee). ‣ 5.1 𝑊_𝑞 guarantee ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Replace every proximal query in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Algorithm 3.1 (Smoothed Picard HMC). ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> by
<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Algorithm D.2 (Gradient descent). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> at the tolerance
(<a href="#A4.E4" title="Equation D.4 ‣ D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>).
The certificate in <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Certificate and pointwise work). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> makes every call a valid
<math id="A4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗑</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathsf{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate proximal query. Then, <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Approximate proximal queries ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> gives the
claimed <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> bound, and the query bound follows from
<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4 (Expected work along the Picard HMC run). ‣ D.2 Gradient-only implementation ‣ Appendix D Replacing proximal queries by gradient queries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> after substituting the step size
chosen in the main text proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Extension to arbitrary Picard depth</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm used in the main results takes Picard depth <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. In this appendix, we record the discretization error of Picard HMC using the exact smoothed gradient, at arbitrary depth.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Retain the Chebyshev–Lobatto nodes and coefficients from
(<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 3.6 ‣ Chebyshev–Lobatto quadrature. ‣ 3.2 The higher-order integrator and the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>); their properties are summarized in
<a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. Let <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}\coloneqq\nabla V_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}\coloneqq\nabla V_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, let
<math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}\otimes\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, set
<math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\coloneqq(\omega_{i,j})_{i,j=1}^{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>J</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\coloneqq(\omega_{i,j})_{i,j=1}^{J}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{i\in[J]}\sum_{j\in[J]}\lvert\omega_{i,j}\rvert\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{i\in[J]}\sum_{j\in[J]}\lvert\omega_{i,j}\rvert\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_algorithm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Depth-<math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> exact Picard HMC phase)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{\rm init},P_{\rm init})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{\rm init},P_{\rm init})</annotation></semantics></math>, draw independent
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1}\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, set
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{h}\coloneqq e^{-h/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}\coloneqq e^{-h/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{h}\coloneqq(1-e^{-h})^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{h}\coloneqq(1-e^{-h})^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</p>
<table id="A5.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq a_{h}P_{\rm init}+\sigma_{h}\zeta_{0}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq a_{h}P_{\rm init}+\sigma_{h}\zeta_{0}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t_{i}}^{[0]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t_{i}}^{[0]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+t_{i}P_{0}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+t_{i}P_{0}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t_{i}}^{[\ell+1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t_{i}}^{[\ell+1]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+t_{i}P_{0}-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}g_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[\ell]})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+t_{i}P_{0}-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}g_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[\ell]})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leqslant\ell&lt;K-1\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leqslant\ell&lt;K-1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(E.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Set</p>
<table id="A5.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{h}^{[K]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{h}^{[K]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq P_{0}-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}g_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[K-1]})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq P_{0}-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}g_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[K-1]})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{h}^{[K]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{h}^{[K]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+hP_{0}-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{J,j}g_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[K-1]})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{\rm init}+hP_{0}-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{J,j}g_{\eta}(X_{t_{j}}^{[K-1]})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and write the resulting next-phase initialization as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{\rm init}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{\rm init}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{h}^{[K]}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq X_{h}^{[K]}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\rm init}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\rm init}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq a_{h}P_{h}^{[K]}+\sigma_{h}\zeta_{1}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq a_{h}P_{h}^{[K]}+\sigma_{h}\zeta_{1}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(X_{\rm init},P_{\rm init})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(X_{\rm init},P_{\rm init})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=(\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=(\zeta_{0},\zeta_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{z}^{[J,K]}(\zeta)\coloneqq(X_{\rm init}^{+},P_{\rm init}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{z}^{[J,K]}(\zeta)\coloneqq(X_{\rm init}^{+},P_{\rm init}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\eta,h}^{[J,K]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\eta,h}^{[J,K]}</annotation></semantics></math> for its kernel.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Depth-<math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> Picard HMC)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in C^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{-1}I\preceq\nabla^{2}V\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>. There are
universal <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, if</span></p>
<table id="A5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant\frac{1}{4}\,,\qquad h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant\frac{c}{\kappa}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant\frac{1}{4}\,,\qquad h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant\frac{c}{\kappa}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(E.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then, for every integer <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, every <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>, every
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z,z^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z,z^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and every <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
