<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{J,q}\coloneqq C_{0}^{J+1}q^{2J}J!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{J,q}\coloneqq C_{0}^{J+1}q^{2J}J!</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is universal.
In particular, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math> recovers <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 5.9 (Discretization error bound). ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contraction and coupling.<span id="A5.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
As in the proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 4.7 (Contraction). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>, couple inputs
<math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(x_{\rm init},p_{\rm init})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(x_{\rm init},p_{\rm init})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\prime}=(x^{\prime}_{\rm init},p^{\prime}_{\rm init})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\prime}=(x^{\prime}_{\rm init},p^{\prime}_{\rm init})</annotation></semantics></math> using the same Gaussian variables, and
write <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{0}\coloneqq z-z^{\prime}=(\Delta x,\Delta p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{0}\coloneqq z-z^{\prime}=(\Delta x,\Delta p)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}\coloneqq\Phi_{z}^{[J,K]}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z^{\prime}}^{[J,K]}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}\coloneqq\Phi_{z}^{[J,K]}(\zeta)-\Phi_{z^{\prime}}^{[J,K]}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then,</span></span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta X_{t_{i}}^{[0]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta X_{t_{i}}^{[0]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta x+a_{h}t_{i}\Delta p\,,\qquad\Delta X_{t_{i}}^{[\ell+1]}=\Delta X_{t_{i}}^{[0]}-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}H_{j}^{[\ell]}\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[\ell]}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta x+a_{h}t_{i}\Delta p\,,\qquad\Delta X_{t_{i}}^{[\ell+1]}=\Delta X_{t_{i}}^{[0]}-\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{i,j}H_{j}^{[\ell]}\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[\ell]}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}^{[\ell]}\coloneqq H\bigl(X_{t_{j}}^{[\ell]},X_{t_{j}}^{\prime[\ell]}\bigr)\,,\qquad(2\kappa)^{-1}I\preceq H_{j}^{[\ell]}\preceq I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}^{[\ell]}\coloneqq H\bigl(X_{t_{j}}^{[\ell]},X_{t_{j}}^{\prime[\ell]}\bigr)\,,\qquad(2\kappa)^{-1}I\preceq H_{j}^{[\ell]}\preceq I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{i\in[J]}\sum_{j\in[J]}\lvert\omega_{i,j}\rvert\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{i\in[J]}\sum_{j\in[J]}\lvert\omega_{i,j}\rvert\leqslant h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1/4</annotation></semantics></math>,
induction in <math id="A5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[K-1]}-\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}\rVert\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{j\in[J]}\,\lVert\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[K-1]}-\Delta X_{t_{j}}^{[0]}\rVert\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now set</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j}\coloneqq H\bigl(X_{t_{j}}^{[K-1]},X_{t_{j}}^{\prime[K-1]}\bigr)\,,\qquad H\coloneqq h^{-1}\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}H_{j}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j}\coloneqq H\bigl(X_{t_{j}}^{[K-1]},X_{t_{j}}^{\prime[K-1]}\bigr)\,,\qquad H\coloneqq h^{-1}\sum_{j\in[J]}\omega_{j}H_{j}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">The endpoint calculation in
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 4.6 (First-order difference expansion). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a> therefore applies unchanged and
yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}=(I+hA_{H})\Delta_{0}+\mathcal{R}_{h}\Delta_{0}\,,\qquad\lVert\mathcal{R}_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}=(I+hA_{H})\Delta_{0}+\mathcal{R}_{h}\Delta_{0}\,,\qquad\lVert\mathcal{R}_{h}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">The matrix inequality in the proof of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 4.7 (Contraction). ‣ 4.3 Properties of the exact-gradient kernel ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>, followed by
<math id="A5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant c/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\Lambda_{J}\leqslant c/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, proves
(<a href="#A5.E3" title="Equation E.3 ‣ Theorem E.2 (Depth-𝐾 Picard HMC). ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>).
Moreover, subtracting <math id="A5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from the expansion and using
<math id="A5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert A_{H}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert A_{H}\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant C</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\Delta_{1}-\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\,(h+\Lambda_{J}h^{2})\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant Ch\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\Delta_{1}-\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\,(h+\Lambda_{J}h^{2})\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\leqslant Ch\,\lVert\Delta_{0}\rVert_{M_{\kappa}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">which is (<a href="#A5.E4" title="Equation E.4 ‣ Theorem E.2 (Depth-𝐾 Picard HMC). ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.4</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discretization error.<span id="A5.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Start the phase from <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The first OU half-refresh preserves this law. Let <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leqslant t\leqslant h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leqslant t\leqslant h</annotation></semantics></math>, be the position along the exact Hamiltonian trajectory,
and put <math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(X_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(X_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The interpolation estimate already proved in
(<a href="#S5.E11" title="Equation 5.11 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.11</span></a>) gives</span></span></p>
<table id="A5.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g(t)-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}g(t)\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant B_{J,q}\sqrt{d+q}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>J</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\coloneqq\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g(t)-\mathcal{I}_{J,h}g(t)\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant B_{J,q}\sqrt{d+q}\,\Bigl(\frac{h}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)^{J}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(E.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{X}\coloneqq(X_{t_{j}})_{j\in[J]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖷</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{X}\coloneqq(X_{t_{j}})_{j\in[J]}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{X}^{[0]}\coloneqq(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]})_{j\in[J]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖷</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{X}^{[0]}\coloneqq(X_{t_{j}}^{[0]})_{j\in[J]}</annotation></semantics></math>, and use the norm given by
the maximum over nodes of the <math id="A5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm. The exact Volterra equation
and polynomial interpolation give</span></p>
<table id="A5.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{X}=\mathsf{X}^{[0]}-\Omega g_{\eta}(\mathsf{X})+\varrho\,,\qquad\lVert\varrho\rVert\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖷</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝖷</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖷</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϱ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>ϱ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{X}=\mathsf{X}^{[0]}-\Omega g_{\eta}(\mathsf{X})+\varrho\,,\qquad\lVert\varrho\rVert\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2}\,\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(E.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The map <math id="A5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}:\mathsf{y}\mapsto\mathsf{X}^{[0]}-\Omega g_{\eta}(\mathsf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝗒</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖷</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}:\mathsf{y}\mapsto\mathsf{X}^{[0]}-\Omega g_{\eta}(\mathsf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> has Lipschitz constant at most <math id="A5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="A5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz. Let <math id="A5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathsf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖷</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathsf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> be its fixed point. From
(<a href="#A5.E7" title="Equation E.7 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.7</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\overline{\mathsf{X}}-\mathsf{X}\rVert\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2\,(1-h^{2}\Lambda_{J})}\,\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖷</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖷</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\overline{\mathsf{X}}-\mathsf{X}\rVert\leqslant\frac{h^{2}}{2\,(1-h^{2}\Lambda_{J})}\,\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(E.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem9" title="Proposition 5.9 (Discretization error bound). ‣ 5.3.2 Discretization error bound ‣ 5.3 𝑊_𝑞 local error bounds ‣ 5 𝑊_𝑞 analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a> gives
<math id="A5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g(t)\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{d+q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant h}\,\lVert g(t)\rVert_{L^{q}}\leqslant C\sqrt{d+q}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining this with
(<a href="#A5.E8" title="Equation E.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.8</span></a>) and the fixed-point equation yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathsf{X}^{[0]}-\overline{\mathsf{X}}\rVert\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\sqrt{d+q}+C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖷</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖷</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathsf{X}^{[0]}-\overline{\mathsf{X}}\rVert\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\sqrt{d+q}+C\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">The recursion (<a href="#A5.E1" title="Equation E.1 ‣ Algorithm E.1 (Depth-𝐾 exact Picard HMC phase). ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>) is precisely the iteration of
<math id="A5.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, starting from <math id="A5.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{X}^{[0]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖷</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{X}^{[0]}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathsf{X}^{[K-1]}-\overline{\mathsf{X}}\rVert\leqslant C\,(h^{2}\Lambda_{J})^{K-1}\,\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\{\sqrt{d+q}+\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖷</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖷</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathsf{X}^{[K-1]}-\overline{\mathsf{X}}\rVert\leqslant C\,(h^{2}\Lambda_{J})^{K-1}\,\Lambda_{J}h^{2}\,\{\sqrt{d+q}+\mathcal{E}_{J,q}\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(E.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The exact Hamiltonian endpoint satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X_{\rm init}+hP_{0}-\int_{0}^{h}(h-t)g(t)\,\mathrm{d}t\,,\qquad P_{h}=P_{0}-\int_{0}^{h}g(t)\,\mathrm{d}t\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X_{\rm init}+hP_{0}-\int_{0}^{h}(h-t)g(t)\,\mathrm{d}t\,,\qquad P_{h}=P_{0}-\int_{0}^{h}g(t)\,\mathrm{d}t\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The quadrature rules integrate <math id="A5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{J,h}g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{J,h}g</annotation></semantics></math> exactly. Use
(<a href="#A5.E8" title="Equation E.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.8</span></a>)–(<a href="#A5.E9" title="Equation E.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.9</span></a>),
<math id="A5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitzness of <math id="A5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the coefficient bounds in
(<a href="#A2.E2" title="Equation B.2 ‣ Proposition B.1 (Chebyshev–Lobatto coefficient bounds). ‣ B.1 Nodes, interpolating polynomials, and integrated weights ‣ Appendix B Chebyshev–Lobatto interpolation and quadrature ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>). The momentum estimate dominates and
gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert(X_{\rm init}^{+},P_{\rm init}^{+})-(X_{h},P_{h}^{+})\rVert_{L^{q},M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}\,\bigl\{h\mathcal{E}_{J,q}+h^{3}\,(h^{2}\Lambda_{J})^{K-1}\sqrt{d+q}\bigr\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>init</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert(X_{\rm init}^{+},P_{\rm init}^{+})-(X_{h},P_{h}^{+})\rVert_{L^{q},M_{\kappa}}\leqslant C\Lambda_{J}\,\bigl\{h\mathcal{E}_{J,q}+h^{3}\,(h^{2}\Lambda_{J})^{K-1}\sqrt{d+q}\bigr\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(E.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{h}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{h}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> includes the common final OU half-refresh. The terms in
(<a href="#A5.E9" title="Equation E.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.9</span></a>) containing <math id="A5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{J,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{J,q}</annotation></semantics></math> are
absorbed into the first term because <math id="A5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>J</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{2}\Lambda_{J}\leqslant 1/4</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting
(<a href="#A5.E6" title="Equation E.6 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.6</span></a>) into
(<a href="#A5.E10" title="Equation E.10 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.10</span></a>) proves
(<a href="#A5.E5" title="Equation E.5 ‣ Theorem E.2 (Depth-𝐾 Picard HMC). ‣ Appendix E Extension to arbitrary Picard depth ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
